window.INVESTING_CHAPTERS=(window.INVESTING_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":201,"title":"Chapter 201 | Elena","paragraphs":["Dexter looked at her.","He looked at the girl who had followed him to a rooftop because she wanted to know where he was, the girl who had remembered his birthday when no one else did. The girl who had spent what was probably a significant portion of her money on a secondhand sweater for a boy that the rest of the estate treated like furniture.","He looked at her, and he felt so thing breaking inside of him; twisting like a key unlocking an old doo.","\"Jasmine,\" he said.","She turned her head and looked at him with her cute eyes.","Dexter held his gaze as he looked at her.","\"Thank you,\"","Those two words were inadequate for what she had gone through to give her the gifts but his words meant everything.","Those words that couldn’t possibly carry the weight of what he actually meant.","But Jasmine smiled as though she understood what he meant.","The quiet smile started at the corners of her mouth and spread slowly to her eyes.","\"You’re welcome,\" she said.","Then she turned back to the sunset.","They sat together on the crumbling wall of the forgotten rooftop, shoulder to shoulder, watching the sky burn itself out in shades of gold and crimson and violet. The city hummed below them but none of it mattered.","The rooftop was ugly, but sitting there, in a blue sweater that was slightly too large, beside a girl who had remembered his birthday, Dexter Ashford felt something he had never felt before in his fourteen years of life.","He felt like he belonged somewhere.","---","The weeks that followed were the happiest of his life.","They developed a routine. Every evening, after their respective duties were finished, they would meet on the rooftop. Sometimes they talked about everything, about nothing, about the heroes they admired. About the places they wanted to visit. About the lives they dreamed of living once they escaped the Ashford estate.","Sometimes they didn’t talk at all. They simply sat together and watched the city change colors as the sun moved across the sky.","Jasmine told him about her family. Her younger brother, who wanted to be a hero when he grew up. Her older sister, who had married a merchant and moved to another city.","Dexter told her about his mother. About the fragments of information he had gathered over the years from servants who had been present when she was alive.","Her name was Elena. She had been brought to the Ashford estate as a servant when she was sixteen. She had been quiet. Gentle. She had sung while she worked, soft melodies that the other servants remembered years after her death.","She had died giving birth to him.","That was all he knew.","Jasmine listened to every word. She didn’t interrupt nor did she offer hollow platitudes. She simply listened, her hand finding his, interlacing with his and holding on.","---","One evening, three months after the birthday sweater, they sat on the wall watching a particularly spectacular sunset. The sky was doing something unusual. The clouds had arranged themselves into long, thin bands that caught the light and glowed like rivers of molten gold flowing across a violet sky.","Jasmine leaned her head against his shoulder.","\"Dexter?\"","\"Yeah?\"","\"When you leave this place, and you will leave this place, where will you go?\"","Dexter was quiet for a moment. He had thought about leaving. Every day. Every hour. The desire to walk through the Ashford estate gates and never return was like a real demon whispering in his mind.","But the Ashford family would never let him go, knowingl he was still connected to them by blood. Even if he ran away, he had no money, no resources, no education, and an F-Rank mana affinity that made him less valuable than the lowest hired servant.","\"I don’t know,\" he said honestly. \"Anywhere. Everywhere. Somewhere far from here. Somewhere quiet. Maybe a small house. With a garden. And a kitchen where I can cook whatever I want.\"","\"You like cooking?\" Jasmine lifted her head from his shoulder and looked at him with genuine surprise.","\"I love cooking,\" Dexter said. He had never admitted this to anyone. In the Ashford estate, cooking was a servant’s job. A menial task. Not something a person did because they enjoyed it. \"When I was younger, I used to sneak into the kitchen after everyone had gone to sleep. I would take whatever ingredients were left over and just... cook. Experiment. Try different combinations. See what worked and what didn’t.\"","He paused. \"The head cook caught me once. She didn’t report me. She just gave me a recipe book and told me to clean up after myself.\"","Jasmine stared at him.","Then she smiled.","It was the widest smile he had ever seen on her face. Bright. Unfiltered. The kind of smile that rearranged everything he thought he knew about the way faces worked.","\"What?\" he asked, suddenly self-conscious.","\"Nothing,\" she said. \"I just think you’re full of surprises.\"","She leaned her head back against his shoulder.","\"When you open your restaurant,\" she said, her voice drowsy and warm, \"I want to be your first customer.\"","Dexter looked down at her. Her eyes were closed. Her lashes were dark crescents against her cheeks. Her breathing was slow and even. The sunset painted her face in gold.","\"When I open my restaurant,\" he said quietly, \"you’ll be more than a customer.\"","He wasn’t sure what he meant by that. He wasn’t sure what he was trying to say. He was fourteen. He had never been on a date. He had never held a girl’s hand before Jasmine. He didn’t know the right words for the things he was feeling, because nobody had ever taught him the vocabulary of tenderness.","But Jasmine smiled without opening her eyes.","\"I know,\" she whispered.","---","They stayed on the rooftop until the stars came out.","The city below had transformed into a sea of lights. Towers and streets and homes, each one a small point of illumination in the vast darkness. From above, it looked like a reflection of the sky. As if the stars had fallen and settled on the earth, creating a second constellation that hummed with life.","Jasmine had fallen asleep against his shoulder.","Dexter sat perfectly still, not wanting to disturb her. The blue sweater kept him warm. The stars kept him company. The weight of her head on his shoulder kept him grounded.","He didn’t sleep. He didn’t want to and he wanted to stay in this moment for as long as it lasted.","The Ashford estate would surely notice and someone would see them and would report.","But Dexter at that moment didn’t care. Be just wanted to stay up there with her."]},{"number":202,"title":"Chapter 202 | The Meeting","paragraphs":["Dexter reached the restaurant at 12:40 PM.","He had ten minutes to make up for. His jacket was torn at the shoulder from the fight. His knuckles were bruised and the adrenaline from the confrontation at Harvest Homes was still humming through his veins like electricity through a live wire.","None of it showed on his face.","He walked through the restaurant entrance with the calm, composed expression of a man who had not, in fact, just been thrown through a wall by a four-meter Ultra Realm expert thirty minutes ago.","The receptionist looked up and smiled.","\"Good afternoon, sir. Welcome. How may I help you?\"","\"I’m Dexter Ashford. I have a reservation. Booth 24.\"","The receptionist checked the tablet in front of her. Her eyes moved across the screen. Then she looked up, her smile brightening.","\"Welcome, Mr. Ashford. Your party is already seated. Please head down the main hallway, second door on your left.\"","Dexter thanked her and walked through the dining area.","The restaurant was busier and every table was occupied.","Waiters wove between chairs carrying steaming plates of meals.","He reached the hallway, Booth 24.","He placed his hand on the door handle, pushed it open, and stepped inside.","When he stepped inside, there were six people seated in the booth.","He had expected five.","A few meant three or four, maybe five at most. Dexter had prepared himself for a small, informal gathering of mid-rank heroes who wanted to swap war stories and discuss squad formation over a meal.","He had not prepared himself for six.","He had especially not prepared himself for the woman sitting alone in the corner chair, sipping a glass of palm wine with the unhurried patience of someone who was accustomed to being the most important person in any room she entered.","Dexter controlled his expression.","It took effort. A significant amount of effort. His brain registered the scene in a single, comprehensive snapshot, processing every face, every posture, every detail in the fraction of a second before his expression could betray his surprise.","He smiled.","The booth was a private room. Circular table. Seating for eight. The lighting was warm. The walls were decorated with handwoven textiles in geometric patterns of indigo and gold. A large platter of assorted appetizers sat in the center of the table, surrounded by glasses and bottles.","Five men sat in a loose circle around one side of the table. They were relaxed. Comfortable. The body language of people who had been chatting long enough to settle into their seats and claim their territory.","The sixth person sat alone.","Aurora.","The youngest S-Rank hero in the Hero Association.","She sat in the corner chair, separated from the others by a gap of empty space that was clearly not accidental. The five men had arranged themselves on the opposite side of the table, grouped together in a cluster that spoke volumes about their collective willingness to sit within arm’s reach of someone who could probably level the building if she sneezed.","Aurora didn’t seem to mind. She leaned against the table with one elbow, her glass of palm wine held loosely in her hand, her dark eyes fixed on Dexter with an expression of quiet, evaluating interest.","Dexter catalogued the other faces.","Cole who was called Plasmatic Man. Seated at the center of the group. He was the one who had organized this meeting. Mid-twenties. Clean-shaven. Blue t-shirt and jeans. His plasma energy was fully suppressed, giving no hint of the devastating power he could wield.","To Cole’s left was a man Dexter recognized from the outbreak. Blitz. A speed-type hero whose talent allowed him to move at extraordinary velocities for short bursts.","He had been the one pulling injured civilians from collapsed buildings during the attack, darting in and out of danger zones with a fearlessness that had impressed even the veteran responders. He was slender. Wiry. His features were sharp, his eyes constantly moving, scanning the room with the restless energy of someone whose brain operated at a faster clock speed than everyone else’s.","To Cole’s right was a man Dexter recognized but did not like.","Bullet Spear Man.","His real name was apparently something else, but everyone in the hero community knew him by his combat moniker. He was tall. Muscular. His arms were thick, and his hands were large. He carried a collapsed spear harness on his back, the weapon’s shaft visible above his shoulder. His face was handsome in a rough, aggressive way. Strong jaw. Cropped hair. A scar running from his left ear to his collar.","Dexter remembered him from the outbreak.","He remembered what Bullet Spear Man had done.","During the Goblin attack, when a group of civilians had been cornered in an alley by a pack of six-star beasts, Bullet Spear Man had been in a position to rescue them directly. Instead, he had positioned himself at the opposite end of the alley and attacked the monsters from behind, using the civilians as bait.","The strategy was effective. The distracted monsters were easier to kill from behind. The civilians survived, though two of them were injured in the process.","Dexter understood the tactical logic. He understood that sometimes, in combat, difficult choices produced better outcomes than heroic ones. He understood that Bullet Spear Man’s decision had resulted in fewer total casualties than a direct rescue attempt might have.","But understanding logic and trusting a person were two different things.","A man who would use civilians as bait would use teammates as bait. Given the right circumstances. Given the right tactical calculation. Given the right price.","Dexter did not trust Bullet Spear Man.","He nodded politely, smiled and said nothing beyond the basic social courtesies.","The fourth person was a man called Gridlock. A defensive specialist. His talent allowed him to create localized force fields that could absorb and redirect kinetic energy.","During the outbreak, he had used his barriers to create safe zones where civilians could shelter while the combat heroes engaged the monsters."]},{"number":203,"title":"Chapter 203 | Aurora","paragraphs":["The fifth was the Tank. His actual hero name was Bulwark, but everyone called him the Tank because it was more accurate. His talent was straightforward and devastatingly effective. Extreme durability. His body could absorb physical punishment that would kill most heroes. Blades bounced off his skin.","Blunt force that would shatter bones merely bruised. During the outbreak, he had stood in front of a charging six-star Dark Hound and let it slam into him at full speed.","One Six arm goblin had broken its neck on impact but the Tank had gotten a bruise.","He was the quietest of the group. Sitting at the edge of the circle, his massive arms folded across his massive chest with a calm look.","Five heroes. All of them from the outbreak.","And then Aurora.","Dexter took the empty seat that Cole was pointing to. It was on the opposite side of the table from Aurora, positioned between the Tank and Gridlock. He sat down, settled into the chair, and looked at the group.","\"I’m sorry for being late,\" he said. \"I got held up.\"","The others waved dismissively.","\"No worries, no worries,\" Cole said, grinning. \"We understand.\"","Blitz leaned forward. \"If it were some of us, we might have been even later. I got stuck in traffic on the way here. Literally had to run the last three blocks.\"","Gridlock nodded solemnly. \"I was early. I’m always early.\"","\"That’s because you have no life,\" Bullet Spear Man said with a smirk.","\"That’s because I’m responsible,\" Gridlock replied, completely unfazed.","The table chuckled.","Dexter smiled. The banter was easy. Natural. The kind of exchange that happened between people who had shared a dangerous experience and come out the other side with a bond that was hard to articulate but impossible to deny.","He glanced at Aurora.","She was still watching him. Her dark eyes were steady. Unblinking. Her expression was neutral, giving nothing away. She sipped her palm wine with the slow, deliberate patience of someone who was content to observe until she had seen enough.","Cole leaned toward Dexter. His voice dropped to a murmur that was pitched just below the threshold of the others’ conversation.","\"We had already gathered here before you arrived,\" Cole said quietly. \"We were expecting you. Then she walked in.\"","He glanced at Aurora.","\"She said she wanted to meet you. Specifically.\"","Dexter blinked. \"Do you know why?\"","Cole shook his head. \"No. She hasn’t said. She’s been sitting there since she arrived, drinking palm wine and not talking to anyone.\"","He paused.","\"I suspect she’ll tell you when she’s ready.\"","Dexter looked at Aurora again. She met his gaze for a brief moment, then returned her attention to her glass.","\"Okay,\" Dexter said.","He turned back to the group and let the conversation carry him.","---","The discussion flowed naturally. They talked about the outbreak.","Blitz talked about the rescues of how close to being with death as he saved a few heroes from the clutches of death.","The Tank said very little. When asked about his experience, he simply said, \"I stood in front of things. The things broke.\"","Dexter listened to Bullet Spear Man’s account and said nothing.","’Bullet Spear Man is competent and he kills without hesitation. But his priorities are wrong. He values results over people and sees civilians as resources, not as lives. And a person who sees other people as resources will eventually see you the same way.","’I cannot be on a squad with this man.’","The thought was firm.","Dexter continued chatting with the others, avoiding direct conversation with Bullet Spear Man without making it obvious. He laughed at Blitz’s jokes. He complimented Gridlock’s barrier technique. He nodded respectfully at the Tank.","And throughout it all, Aurora sat in her corner. Sipping her drink while watching silently.","---","After the discussion had wound down and the appetizers had been substantially reduced, Cole reached for his glass and tapped it with a spoon.","Ting. Ting","The table quieted.","Cole stood. He raised his glass with a genuine, unguarded smile.","\"Today, one of the reasons we gathered here is to thank Dexter for what he did during the outbreak.\"","His voice was warm and sincere. The voice of a man who genuinely believed that he owed his life to the person sitting across from him.","\"Dexter, we say thank you. For giving us a second chance at life.\"","He raised his glass higher.","\"Cheers.\"","\"Cheers!\" the table echoed.","Glasses rose. Blended. The sound of glass meeting glass rang through the booth like a small, musical bell.","Blitz grinned and Gridlock nodded solemnly as the Tank raised his glass witb his large hands.","Even Bullet Spear Man raised his drink, his smirk softening into something that resembled genuine gratitude.","Dexter looked at the glass in front of him. Amber liquid. The sharp, smoky scent of aged whiskey.","He picked it up.","\"I accept your appreciation,\" he said. \"Thank you.\"","He downed the drink in one smooth motion.","The whiskey burned down his throat, spreading warmth through his chest. It wasn’t the Emperor Void Flame. It wasn’t mana circulation. It was simpler than that. Rougher. The warmth of alcohol shared between people who had bled together.","The heroes clapped. They cheered. They took their own drinks and downed them with the enthusiastic commitment of people who believed that any problem could be temporarily improved by the application of sufficient alcohol.","The atmosphere lightened. The formality dissolved. What remained was something more honest. More human. Five people who had fought beside each other, survived, and come back to talk about it over food and drinks.","Dexter found himself genuinely enjoying the company. Blitz’s manic energy was infectious. Gridlock’s dry, deadpan humor caught him off guard more than once. Even the Tank, in his monosyllabic way, contributed moments of unexpected comedy.","At one point, Blitz asked the Tank why he never dodged attacks.","The Tank looked at Blitz as though the question had offended his ancestors.","\"Why would I dodge?\" he said. \"Dodging means moving. Moving means effort. Standing still is free.\"","The table erupted."]},{"number":204,"title":"Chapter 204 | Join Our Squad","paragraphs":["Cole suddenly set his glass down and leaned forward, resting his forearms on the table.","\"Now that we’ve gotten that out of the way, we should probably talk about why we’re actually here.\"","The table went quiet.","\"The five of us have been talking,\" Cole continued. \"Since the outbreak. We’ve been discussing the idea of forming a squad.\"","He looked around the table.","\"A standard squad consists of six people and we currently have five people here.","Cole’s gaze moved to Dexter.","\"We’d be very honored if you become our sixth member.\"","Dexter looked at Cole and then stated at the others who nodded and smile at him.","Bullet Spear Man was leaning back in his chair, with a neutral expression in hhs face.","Cole continued. \"You saved our lives. And from what we’ve seen, you’re the kind of person who doesn’t abandon his position, no matter what comes at you.\"","He paused.","\"That’s the kind of person we want watching our backs.\"","Dexter remained silent as he stared at the five people before him. Logically, joining a squad is quite useless and would simple tie him to multiple people and take his time to use to take care of his wives.","But if he could join a squad, it would be easier to hunt and clear dungeons with them when they familiarize themselves with their techniques, strengths and weaknesses.","Moroever, he wouldn’t need to respond to every single Monster outbreak nearby. As clearing one dungeon would automatically give him the month off.","Moreover, if he hopes to actually be able to get a land in this city, he would need lots of money and lots of connections that even the Ashford family can’t influence.","Surely, the incident with the housing agent would happen again so he needed all these things. But it’s a gradual process.","The others seem to hold their breathe as they waited for Dexter’s response.","\"Alright.\"","Cole exhaled slowly.","\"That’s exactly what we were hoping you’d say.\"","He extended his hand across the table.","\"Welcome to the squad, Dexter.\"","Dexter looked at the hand.","He thought about his wives, about the house he didn’t have, the money he had lost, the fight he had just been in. The enemies that were circling his family like wolves around a campfire.","Dexter reached across the table and shook Cole’s hand.","\"Thabk you.","\"Welcome to the squad,\" Cole repeated, grinning.","The table broke into applause as Blitz whooped, Gridlock clapped and the others smiled.","Dexter smiled and from the corner of his eyes, he saw Aurora set down her glass and turned to look at him with a small smile.","Dexter chose to ignore it.","The conversation continued as they drank, they laughed and discussed.","Dexter found himself relaxing as the tension from the Harvest Homes confrontation and the adrenaline that had been simmering beneath his skin since the fight with the old man disappeared.","He hadn’t realized how much he had needed this.","Dexter checked his phone and saw it was 2:30 PM.","He had been here for almost two hours. The girls had been alone since morning but he had left food for them in the kitchen, so they wouldn’t go hungry. But food wasn’t the issue.","The issue was that three disabled women were sitting in a house in a neighborhood that had suffered two monster outbreaks in three weeks.","Even if he was sure nothing would happen, his mind wasn’t settled.","They might need him but here he was, drinking whiskey and having fun. A pang of guilt struck his chest and Dexter chose to ignore it as he chuckled at Gridlock’s joke.","However, the guilt strangely spread through his entire body, making him frown. He didn’t expect to have such a reaction.","Dexter sighed and he immediately stood up.","\"I’m really sorry to cut this short, but I have to go. I hope you all understand where I’m coming from.\"","The table looked at him as the five people, each carrying a slightly different expression.","Cole smiled first. \"Yes, yes. We understand. There’s no need to explain.\"","Blitz nodded rapidly. \"We get it, man. Family first.\"","Gridlock inclined his head. \"Of course.\"","The Tank nodded with a small smile while Bullet Spear Man said nothing as he simply raised his glass in a lazy salute.","Dexter smiled. \"I apologize once again. You guys have fun and text me the details of when the combat training will occur. I’ll make sure to come early this time and make sure there are no unexpected incidents to delay me.\"","Cole laughed. \"We’ll hold you to that.\"","Dexter smiled, raised a hand in farewell, and walked toward the door.","He opened the door and stepped into the hallway, closing it behind him.","He had taken three steps down the corridor when he heard the door open behind him again. He didn’t turn around immediately, but his Enhanced Hearing picked up the sound.","Reaching the restaurant lobby, he crossed it, stepped through the front door, and onto the sidewalk.","Halfway to his SUV, keys already in hand, he felt something.","His eyes flashed and he immediately turned around.","Aurora was there.","She hadn’t been there a second ago but she had suddenly appeared in a split second.","Ultra Realm experts possessed an ability transcending conventional movement not teleportation, exactly.","Teleportation involved instantaneous matter displacement, bypassing space but the ability Ultras possess was different.","It was a burst speed their bodies move at.","It was instantaneous repositioning. They could move from one location to another within their line of sight in a fraction of a second, their body translating through space with such speed that it looked like teleportation.","The range was roughly a hundred meters and anything within their visual field was reachable in an instant.","This was what made Ultra Realm experts so fundamentally different from Superhumans.","Dexter’s brows furrowed slightly.","\"You wanted to see me,\" he said.","He had been waiting for this moment since he first saw her in the booth."]},{"number":205,"title":"Chapter 205 | I Have A Preposition For You","paragraphs":["Aurora looked at him for a long, silent moment.","Her eyes studied his face as she studied him.","She was an S-Rank hero.","She had fought and killed creatures that would have slaughtered entire squads of lower-rank heroes. She could read people the way Dexter read ingredients.","\"Yes,\" she said finally. \"I wanted to meet you. But it has proven quite difficult to get a hold of you.\"","Dexter raised an eyebrow. \"I’m not that hard to find.\"","\"You are, actually,\" Aurora replied, her voice carrying a trace of genuine frustration. \"Getting your contact information from the Hero Association was impossible. They said you explicitly refused to have your details shared.\"","She paused.","\"It is the first time I have been rejected.\"","Dexter shrugged. \"There’s a first time for everything.\"","Aurora’s eyes flashed with interest.","She didn’t respond immediately as she let the silence between them stretch even further, still staring at Dexter with the same interest.","Dexter’s brows remained furrowed, his mind working through possibilities.","’ Why is she looking at me like that? What does she want?’","’She is an S-Rank hero and one of the youngest S-Rank in the association. She has access to the best squads, the best resources and the best missions. So what does she want’","At that moment, Aurora opened her mouth.","\"During the monster outbreak,\" she said, her voice dropping to a register that was meant for his ears only, \"you were in quite a hurry to leave. As if you sensed something.\"","She paused.","\"Did something happen to your wives?\"","Dexter’s eyes flashed.","He studied her face for a moment, she was perceptive and knew it was about his wives.","\"Yes,\" Dexter said. \"But the situation was under control.\"","Aurora nodded slowly as the answer seemed to satisfy her.","\"You are quite different from what the news says about you,\" she said in a normal tone as she stared at Dexter.","\"You care quite a bit about your wives, don’t you?\"","Dexter shrugged. \"The news likes to exaggerate everything. Don’t believe everything you hear. Most of it is false. Or at least heavily exaggerated.\"","Aurora’s eyes narrowed slightly.","\"Is that so?\" she asked.","\"Yes.\"","Dexter didn’t like her tone.","\"What does it matter to you?\"","Aurora remained silent for a moment.","\"I was curious.\"","\"Curiosity can get people into trouble.\"","\"So can hiding your strength.\"","Dexter’s eyes narrowed.","Aurora continued calmly.","\"During the monster outbreak, everyone thought you were only a relatively ordinary Superhuman. Yet you appeared in the middle of the battlefield and killed monsters far beyond what someone at your supposed level should have been capable of.\"","Dexter’s expression remained unchanged. \"Perhaps I’m simply stronger than I look.\"","\"I thought so.\" Aurora’s eyes flashed faintly. \"That is why I wanted to meet you.\"","Dexter folded his arms. \"And now that you’ve met me?\"","\"I haven’t decided yet.\"","Dexter almost laughed. \"You followed me out of a restaurant just to tell me that?\"","\"No.\" Aurora looked directly into his eyes. The gold flecks in her irises caught the light, giving them an almost luminous quality. \"I wanted to ask you something.\"","Dexter’s expression became slightly more serious. \"Go ahead.\"","Aurora was silent for several seconds. The sounds of the city filled the gap between them.","Finally, she spoke.","\"Join my team.\"","Dexter blinked.","\"Your team?\"","\"Yes.\"","Dexter frowned. \"As you saw, I already have a team. Moreover, the Hero Association has already paired you with some of the most talented heroes of our generation. The best in the city. So I don’t think there is any space for me to join you.\"","Aurora shook her head. \"Not that team. Nor a Association-sanctioned squad.\"","She paused.","\"Another team. I have a proposition for you.\"","Her eyes flicked to the left. Then to the right. Scanning the street. The parked cars. The restaurant entrance behind them. The pedestrians walking past on the far side of the road.","\"But it is quite a delicate matter,\" she said, her voice dropping half a register. \"And I can’t say it out here. In case of listening ears.\"","As she said this, she looked directly behind Dexter. At his SUV.","Dexter blinked.","He understood what she meant and knew wanted him to invite her into the vehicle so she could speak further and away from potential eavesdroppers.","His first instinct was to refuse.","He didn’t know this woman. While he knew her reputation, her public profile and her hero ranking, he didn’t know her.","But then he thought about what had happened an hour ago.","The fight at Harvest Homes, there would surely be repercussions.","Harvest Homes was not a small company.","It was a registered, legitimate business with political connections, financial resources, and at least several Ultra Realm expert on its payroll.","The Ashford name might carry enough weight to deter direct retaliation. But they might even make the retaliation even stronger so he needed connections, allies.","Rachel was an option but he didn’t know Rachel’s full background.","Grandma Lucy was another option. The old woman who could disperse an Ultra-Rank aura with a tap of her finger. But he didn’t know her story either. Didn’t know her limitations. Didn’t know whether her protection extended beyond the sidewalk in front of his house.","Aurora was different.","Aurora was an S-Rank hero, one of the youngest S-Rank in the Association.","An Ultra Realm expert and her name alone carried more weight than most families in Stargate City. If she was associated with him, even loosely, it would give pause to anyone considering retaliation.","And she wanted something from him, which meant there was room for negotiation. Room for a mutually beneficial arrangement that could provide him with the backing he needed.","He would hear her out. If her proposition was unacceptable, he could simply tell her to leave.","Dexter nodded.","\"Okay.\"","He walked to the passenger side and opened the door for Aurora.","Aurora looked at him for a brief moment before she then entered the vehicle.","Dexter walked around to the driver’s side and slid behind the wheel and then closed the door.","The moment Aurora entered, her face changed slightly.","[A/N: Fine! I will mass release extra 5 Chapters! You guys are quite persistent! 😅]"]},{"number":206,"title":"Chapter 206 | The 4th Dimension","paragraphs":["Aurora’s face changed the moment she settled into the passenger seat.","Her eyes moved across the entire interior of the entire vehicle and her face kept changing even more rapidly.","Her fingers reached out she suddenly knocked on the glass panel of the passenger window as her brows furrowed.","Aurora had been inside many vehicles and had ridden in Type 2 transports during Association deployments.","She had been chauffeured in Type 3 vehicles too and had even entered a Type 4 vehicle once, owned by young master Crowell from one of the Nine Families who had attempted to impress her with his family’s wealth.","While she had been unimpressed by the young master, the type 4 car stood out to her.","But this vehicle was truly different.","The interior was simpler than the Type 4 Car and at first glance, it looked like a perfectly ordinary SUV with a slightly nicer interior than average.","But Aurora was born with an S-rank mana affinity. She could sense intense mana radiating off every part of the entire vehicle.","The Type 4 vehicle owned by the young master Crowell sas beautiful and strong but this vehicle gave Aurora the feeling of an expert in hiding.","Like a crouching tiger and a hidden dragon. It was wierd. It was when she tapped on the glasses that she confirmed her suspicion.","\"This car is above Type 4,\" Aurora murmured.","Dexter had just settled into the driver’s seat when he heard her words. He froze for a second, then forced his expression to remain neutral.","He was quite surprised she had figured it out so quickly.","It’s no wonder she was one of the most talented young generations.","The vehicle was in its default mode and he hadn’t activated any of its Type-6 features and had deliberately kept it in its dormant state precisely to avoid this kind of situation.","But Aurora had detected it anyway.","Her composure broke as she turned toward him with stunned expression on her face.","\"I’m right, aren’t I?\" she said, her voice carrying absolute certainty. \"This is above Type 6.\"","Her face instantly turned serious.","\"Who exactly are you?\"","Not to mention how impossible it was to find a vehicle above Type 4, the price of the vehicle would definitely be astronomical!","While Dexter was the illegitimate son of the Ashford family, he was clearly a nobody but yet, he had a Type 5 Vehicle with him!","This meant he wasn’t just hiding his strength, he might also possess a hidden background.","Even if one had the money to purchase the vehicle, the moment it enters the City’s Auction, it would definitely be fought by the entire Nine Families.","A type 5 weapon wasn’t that rare, but a type 5 vehicle was.","Dexter blinked expressionlessly and waved his hand offhandedly.","\"This is just a random vehicle I bought,\" he said in a dissmissive tone.","\"Now, do you want to tell me exactly what you want to say, or do you want to continue admiring an ordinary vehicle?\"","Aurora stared at him.","She knew he was lying, and he knew she knew.","She also knew he knew she knew.","But Aurora didn’t press. Very few things surprised her and Dexter certainly had slightly exceeded her expectations.","But that was that.","If she knew it was actually type 6, her reaction would definitely be way different.","She had been slightly hesitant to involve Dexter, as she needed a wild card but the vehicle’s discovery had simply made the decision easier.","If Dexter had access to Type 4 object, then it was like she had suspected, Dexter definitely wasn’t ordinary.","Her expression turned very serious as she turned and stared forward through the glass and spoke.","\"I found a map.\"","Hearing this, Dexter was quite confused.","’If you found a map, keep it. What does it have to do with me?’ Bhe he waited for her to finish hee words.","\"A map leading to a portal.\"","Dexter pursed his lips and wanted to sneer. ’It’s most likely leading to an S rank dungeon. Seems like they’re satusfued with crippling my wives uhn...’","Aurora continued. \"A portal leading to the 4th Dimension.\"","Dexter blinked.","The words didn’t register immediately as those words were rarely spoken or heard by Dexter. It was a concept very unfamiliar to him.","The mysterious 4th Dimension.","The 3rd Dimension was space, length, width, and depth. The dimension in which all known life existed, the dimension in which Stargate City stood.","But they call this realm the 4th dimension because no one truly knows its realm name and not just anyone could enter into that realm","What was known about the Fourth Dimension could be summarized in a very short list.","But as it settled in Dexter’s mind and he remebered the fragments and pieces he heard from people over the years, his face started to change as his face changed slightly.","He stared at Aurora with a stunned expression in his face.","\"You found a map to the 4th Dimension,\" he repeated slowly.","\"Yes.\"","Dexter’s mouth opened. Then closed. Then opened again.","\"That’s not possible,\" he said. \"Portals to the 4th Dimension don’t exist. Its only pure fiction and science that everyone else ignores because it’s fantasy.\"","Aurora glanced at him but continued staring at the outside world.","\"Once your rank in the hero association reaches A rank, you gain clearance and access to some materials and learn somethings are very much true. The information leaked so the Hero Association put it out there because they know humans try to rationalize everything. They would never truly believe that there might be other civilizations out there.\"","\"It’s like the rumors of the moon landing being fake, the earth is flat or the world is just a dome meant to trap us.\"","Dexter’s mind trembled.","The 4th Dimension was the source from which monsters poured here.","Every dungeon that had ever been discovered, every gate that had ever opened, every monster outbreak that had ever devastated a neighborhood, all of it traced back to the same cause.","Dungeons themselves seemed like the byproduct, not the main event. The main event was the dimensional bleed. The slow, persistent leaking of 4th Dimensional energy (mana) into this world.","Dexter didn’t fully understand it but there was a law governing the interaction between the two dimensions that dictated how and why dungeons formed.","What Dexter know was that the 4th dimension was dangerous.","Throughout recorded history, there had been instances of individuals attempting to enter the 4th Dimension.","The people who went to there were those that are desperate.Old heroes and Powerhouses who had reached the peak of their cultivation and felt the cold hand of mortality closing around them.","These were the people who chose to enter the Fourth Dimension. To seek miracles pills, herbs and techniques to advance to the next level, expand their lifespan and survive death.","Dexter looked at Aurora and spoke.","\"No.\""]},{"number":207,"title":"Chapter 207 | Treasure Trove","paragraphs":["Aurora glanced at Dexter as though he had suddenly grown a second head.","Her eyebrows furrowed. She continued to look at him for a long moment, her dark eyes searching his face for any sign that his refusal was a negotiating tactic rather than a genuine rejection.","She found none. Suddenly, she smirked and then turned to face forward, looking through the windshield at the pedestrians walking past the restaurant.","She remained silent for a while, Dexter also remained silent. A pigeon landed on the hood, stared at its own reflection in the windshield for a few seconds, and flew away.","Ot was at that moment that Aurora spoke.","\"All right. Rachel said you would reject.\"","Dexter blinked. His eyebrow rose sharply.","\"You know Rachel?\"","Aurora nodded. \"Yeah. We are quite familiar with each other.\"","Dexter’s brows furrowed.","\"Was she the one who told you about me?\" Dexter asked carefully. \"Did she point you in my direction for this expedition?\"","Aurora shook her head slightly. \"She knows almost nothing about this mission. But when I mentioned that I was considering you for the expedition team, she smiled. And she said you would never agree.\"","Aurora glanced at Dexter from the corner of her eye.","\"Which, now that I’m looking at it, is quite correct.\"","Dexter blinked. \"Oh.\"","Aurora looked at Dexter.","\"The expedition is in three months,\" she said. \"I told you that already but didn’t want to say this,\" she continued.","Dexter waited.","\"Although we are entering the Fourth Dimension, we are not truly entering the Fourth Dimension.\"","Dexter blinked his eyes. \"What does that mean?\"","\"The location we’re entering is a space connected to the fourth dimension. It’s like a dungeon but not truly one as there is a chance we could actually head outside 4th dimension.","Aurora’s tone became solemn.","\"It is believed to be the death place of a Legend Realm expert.\"","Dexter’s pupils constricted.","Legend Realm which is above Transcendent and even Above Supreme. The highest cultivation realm that existed.","There were no Legend Realm experts alive in this country. There were none alive anywhere, as far as anyone knew. The last confirmed sighting of a Legend Realm existence had been over two hundred years ago.","A death place of a Legend Realm expert was a massive treasure trove of knowledge, techniques, resources, and power.","\"That is the only thing I can tell you,\" Aurora continued. \"As for which Legend Realm expert it was, I can’t reveal that information. Not until you are committed to the expedition.\"","She let the information settle.","\"It was said that there are techniques inside that pocket space. Techniques to advance past the Transcendent Realm. Techniques to reach the Supreme Realm. Perhaps even beyond.\"","Each realm was exponentially more difficult to reach than the last. Talent alone was not enough!","The gap between Ultra and Transcendent was considered the greatest bottleneck in cultivation. Thousands of Ultra Realm experts across the country spent their entire lives trying to break through and failed.","Anyone who broke through to the Supreme Realm would gain absolute power and authority.","\"You should think much deeper about it,\" Aurora said. Her voice was quiet but insistent. \"You are already at the Superhuman Realm. You will break through to the Ultra Realm eventually. But above Ultra is Transcendent. And to break through to the Transcendent Realm, talent is not enough.\"","She looked at him.","\"You have three months until the expedition. But you have two months to change your mind. After that, the preparation window closes and I proceed with or without you.\"","She reached for the door handle.","\"My contact information is with Rachel. You can also obtain it from the Hero Association if you prefer.\"","She didn’t wait for Dexter to respond.","The passenger door opened and warm afternoon air rushed in as Aurora stepped out, closed the door behind her, and walked away without looking back.","---","Dexter sat alone in the SUV.","He stared at the space where Aurora had been sitting as he thought about what she had said.","The death place of a Legend Realm expert. A pocket dimension within the 4th Dimension, Techniques to advance past the Transcendent Realm. Possibly beyond.","It was true that reaching the Transcendent and Supreme Realms was extraordinarily difficult. For most hero, it was impossible.","Even the most gifted heroes in the city, the Auroras and the S-Rank prodigies, would eventually hit that wall and stop.","’ But I am not most people! I have the 10,000x Investment Multiplier System.’","Every investment he made in his wives, returned to him multiplied a hundredfold.","As long as he continued to invest in his wives, the system would continue to advance his strength.","He was not afraid of encountering a bottleneck.","He wasn’t sure if the system could break through natural cultivation bottlenecks, the fundamental barriers between major realms that existed independent of mana quantity or talent level.","But that was a problem for the future.","He was currently at the Tenth Stage of the Superhuman Realm.","Each of those barriers was a bridge he would cross when he reached it.","For now, the system was sufficient.","What the system could not do, however, was heal his wives.","The system gave him the tools to help them. But the healing was slow. Incremental. Mira’s right arm had moved after three weeks of sustained, daily effort. At that rate, full recovery could take months. Years.","The Fourth Dimension, according to Aurora, offered a 50 percent chance of finding a cure.","Dexter shook his head.","’Not now. I have time. Two months to decide.’","He started the engine. Pulled away from the curb and merged into traffic.","Twenty minutes later, he turned onto his street and the bungalow came into view.","The freshly painted fence gleamed in the late afternoon light and the repaired window caught the sun and threw it back without a crack or a blemish.","He looked at the house and felt something settle in his chest.","He had been gone for hours which was probably the longest he had been away from his wives since they moved in.","’I kind of miss them.’","The thought actually caught him offguard."]},{"number":208,"title":"Chapter 208 | Home Coming","paragraphs":["Dexter smiled and opened the gate, walked up the path, and unlocked the front door.","He stepped inside and sighed in relief.","’ Finally home!’","It felt like he had been out of the house for a long time when he had just been out for about 8 to 19 hours.","His opened his eyes and what he saw made his expression freeze and his heart skip a tiny bit.","At that moment, Mira was sitting in her wheelchair exactly one meter from the front door and was facing the entrance as though she had been waiting for hours.","Her crimson eyes were fixed on the doorway and as Dexter came in, her eyes immediately locked in on him.","Dexter blinked.","He let out an awkward smile and spoke.","\"I’m home.\"","Mira continued staring at him without blinking, her crimson eyes boring into his face intensely.","Then she spoke.","\"Who is she?\"","Dexter’s face filled with genuine confusion.","\"Who are you talking about?\"","Mira smiled and it was not a warm smile.","\"The fourth wife, of course,\" Mira said.","Dexter swallowed.","\"Stop joking. Of course there is no fourth wife. You three are enough for me.\"","Mira glanced at him.","\"Three?\" she repeated. \"Three is never enough for a man.\"","She leaned her head forward slightly in her wheelchair.","\"Don’t worry. I won’t be angry. Just tell me who she is.\"","Dexter scratched the back of his head. \"I am serious, Mira. There is no one else.\"","Mira continued staring at him and her expression didn’t soften.","\"This is your opportunity to tell me the truth,\" she said. \"I promise I won’t tell the other two girls.\"","She paused.","\"I might even support you in collecting a fourth wife.\"","Dexter stared at her. \"What?\"","\"Just tell me who she is.\" Mira tilted her head. \"And how was she?\"","Dexter frowned. \"What do you mean, how was she?\"","Mira shrugged with exaggerated nonchalance. \"Of course I have to ask. How was she compared to us?\"","Dexter’s mouth opened. Then closed. Then opened again.","\"I have no idea who you are talking about, Mira.\"","Mira smiled wider.","\"Does she have a better figure than me?\"","\"No,\" Dexter said immediately. The response was instinctive. Reflexive. The product of a survival instinct that had been honed by three weeks of living with three women.","\"Oh, that means she’s prettier than me?\"","\"No!\"","Mira blinked. Then she smirked.","\"Oh,\" she said. \"So it was a prostitute.\"","Dexter pressed his palm against his face.","\"Mira. There is no other woman.\"","Mira stared at him for several seconds. Her expression was unreadable.","\"So you’re are saying you didn’t go to see a woman?\"","\"Dexter immediately shook his head. \"Like I told you before I left, I went to see the heroes I fought with and also to get a place for us to live.\"","Mira nodded her head slowly and then she leaned back in her wheelchair.","\"Then why do you smell like another woman?\"","Dexter’s face changed slightly.","’This girl is quite perceptive. Didn’t know she had an extraordinary sense of smell!’","His mind raced as it hit him.","Aurora.","She had been sitting in the passenger seat of his SUV for a few minutes. And he had been sitting in that same cabin for the twenty-minute drive home.","He had never expected her scent to linger on him to the extent that Mira would notice.","But Mira had noticed.","Because Mira was not an ordinary person. She was a former A-Rank hero with S-Rank mana affinity. Even with her cultivation sealed and her body crippled, her sensory perception was far beyond that of a normal human.","And she had caught him.","Mira’s smile became even more dangerous.","\"Oh, did you think I wouldn’t notice?\" she asked. Her voice was sweet. Honeyed.","\"You were gone for hours,\" she continued. \"You said you were meeting some heroes.\"","Dexter replied quickly. \"I was.\"","Mira’s smile widened by a fraction. \"So the hero you went to meet was a woman.\"","It wasn’t a question. It was a conclusion. Delivered with the finality of a judge reading a verdict.","Dexter’s mouth twitched.","’This is getting dangerous.’","He tried again. \"There isn’t another woman, Mira.\"","\"So explain this scent,\" Mira said. Her voice was no longer sweet. It was flat. Direct. The voice of a woman who had moved past the interrogation phase and was now demanding evidence.","Dexter stood in the entryway, as he sighed.","Then he noticed a figure in the corridor.","Lyra was standing at the edge of the hallway, partially hidden by the doorframe.","Her dark eyes were fixed on Dexter as she smiled in amusement. She seemed to be enjoying this.","Dexter took in a deep breath and exhaled slowly.","\"What do you know about the Fourth Dimension?\"","Mira’s face changed drastically as the dangerous smile on her face vanished as her crimson eyes widened.","\"Who told you about the Fourth Dimension?\" she asked.","Dexter blinked.","He was surprised by her reaction. Not by the fact that she knew about the Fourth Dimension. He had suspected she might, given her previous status as one of the city’s top heroes. But the intensity of her response surprised him.","Then he told her everything from the beginning.","He didn’t have to as he could have just ignored her told her but then, he chose to tell her everything.","He told her about the squad meeting.About Cole and Blitz and Gridlock and the Tank, about the squad formation and his acceptance.","Then he told her about Aurora.","About how she had followed him to the parking lot, her proposition, the portal, the death place of a Legend Realm expert.","He told her everything and Mira listened quietly.","When Dexter finished, Mira was quiet for a long time.","Then she said something that surprised both of them.","\"You could go.\"","Dexter stared at her.","\"I’m sorry?\"","\"You could go,\" Mira repeated. \"With the speed of your advancement, you will enter the Ultra Realm in a year or two. Maybe sooner. And within five years, you might reach the peak of Ultra Realm.\""]},{"number":209,"title":"Chapter 209 | Serious Dexter!","paragraphs":["Mira paused.","\"But talent alone is not enough to break through from Ultra to Transcendent. \"","She looked at him.","\"So yes. Eventually, you will have to go. If you want to advance past Ultra, you will need access to something that exists beyond our dimension. That’s just reality.\"","Dexter blinked. He hadn’t expected this. He had expected Mira to list every reason why he couldn’t leave.","Instead, she was giving him permission.","\"But,\" Mira continued, and her voice hardened, \"you are not going with Aurora.\"","Dexter blinked again. \"What?\"","\"You are not going with Aurora,\" Mira repeated. Each word was enunciated with the precision of a hammer driving nails.","\"But it is Aurora who knows the location of the portal,\" Dexter said. \"She has the map. She has the coordinates. She’s the one organizing the expedition.\"","Mira’s jaw tightened. Her crimson eyes flashed.","\"I don’t care,\" she said. \"You are not going with that woman.\"","Dexter stared at her. The pieces were falling into place. The jealousy from moments ago.","\"Are you jealous?\" he asked carefully. \"Is there something between you and Aurora? A rivalry?\"","Mira snorted coldly.","\"Aurora,\" she said. The name left her lips like something distasteful. \"That bitch.\"","Dexter raised both eyebrows.","\"People try comparing her to us, to the three of us. They say she’s the youngest S-Rank. The most talented hero of her generation. The pride of Stargate City.\"","Her crimson eyes burned.","\"That bitch took my place.\"","\"I was the youngest hero in the city’s history,\" Mira said.","\"Then the dungeon happened. And we were crippled. And suddenly, the spotlight needed somewhere else to shine. And there she was. Aurora.\"","\"Nobody would even know her name if it wasn’t for the fact that the three of us were removed from the picture,\" Mira said. \"She got her S-Rank because there was no one left to compete with. The youngest S-Rank? Please.\"","She glared at Dexter.","\"And now she wants to take our husband.\"","The last sentence came out with a venom that made the air in the entryway feel several degrees warmer.","\"Absolutely not,\" Mira said. \"You are not going anywhere with that woman.\"","Dexter looked at her.","He could argue.","But he didn’t.","\"All right, all right,\" Dexter said, holding up both hands. \"I didn’t want to go in the first place. So I won’t go with her. If I ever want to get to the Fourth Dimension, I’ll find another way. Are you satisfied?\"","Mira glanced at Dexter.","She blinked, Then she smirked a small, self-satisfied smirk.","But Dexter could see the smile she was trying to suppress.","She was pleased.","Dexter chuckled at her poorly concealed satisfaction. She eqs cute.","\"Did you get to eat?\" he asked.","Mira shrugged. \"I wasn’t hungry.\"","Dexter’s brows furrowed.","The amusement drained from his face. What replaced it was a cold seriousness.","\"You shouldn’t do that,\" he said.","Mira was a bit surprised by his tone. She looked at him. The playfulness in her expression faded when she saw his face.","\"Do what?\" she asked.","\"Not eat the food I made for you,\" Dexter said in a calm but firm tone.","\"Every meal I make for you girls is very important. Not to me. To you. Every dish is designed to accelerate your recovery.\"","He held her gaze.","\"So you should not skip the food I make. You should always eat. Every time with no exceptions, alright?\"","Mira’s brows furrowed at his commanding tone.","She opened her mouth and wanted to instinctively retort but she saw Dexter’s expression and knew he was dead serious.","She blinked and closed her mouth and then nodded her head","\"All right,\" she said. \"All right. I will eat the food you make.\"","\"Always,\" Dexter added.","\"Always,\" Mira repeated, her voice quieter than usual.","Dexter nodded. \"Good.\"","He straightened up from his kneeling position.","\"I’ll go set up the table. Come to the dining room in five minutes.\"","He turned and walked toward the corridor, leaving Mira sitting in her wheelchair with an expression that hovered between annoyed and something she would rather die than identify.","---","Dexter reached the corridor.","Lyra was gone.","She had been there minutes ago, but the hallway was now empty.","Dexter walked to the girls’ room and pushed the door open.","Lyra was sitting cross-legged on the bed. The Primordial Beast Egg rested in her lap, and her eyes were closed as she cultivated.","Or pretending to cultivate.","Dexter knew better but he didn’t call her out on it.","\"I’m back,\" he said.","Lyra’s eyes remained closed. She nodded once.","Dexter frowned.","\"Have you eaten?\"","Lyra’s eyes stayed closed. She shook her head.","Dexter’s frown deepened. He projected his thoughts toward her through their telepathic connection, ensuring the message was unmissable.","\"Food will be ready in five minutes. Come to the dining room. No room for negotiation.\"","He didn’t wait for a response and simply closed the door and walked to the backyard.","---","Selene was on the swing.","Even with the perpetual cold that lived inside her body, the frost that crept beneath her skin and seeped into her bones, she still preferred the outdoors. It was a contradiction that Dexter had noticed but never questioned.","Perhaps the open air helped. Perhaps the breeze carried away some of the cold energy that accumulated around her. Perhaps she simply liked the feeling of space around her, the absence of walls and ceilings, after years of being confined indoors.","She was cultivating. Her silver-white hair hung still around her shoulders. The swing moved gently in the breeze, giving her the appearance of a ghost suspended between earth and sky.","The moment his foot touched the backyard porch, Selene’s head turned toward him. Her Echolocation had detected his approach through the vibrations of his footsteps on the wooden boards.","\"You’re back,\" she said. Her voice was soft and quiet. Aimed roughly in his direction.","Dexter smiled. \"Yes. I’m back.\"","He paused. \"Hope everything was all right while I was gone.\"","\"Yes,\" she said. \"Everything was fine.\"","Dexter nodded. Then asked the question he asked the other two girls.","\"Have you eaten?\"","Selene blinked. Her pale, sightless eyes widened slightly. Then she slowly shook her head.","Dexter frowned.","He knew she couldn’t see his expression. She was blind. His furrowed brow and tightened jaw were invisible to her. So he did something he rarely did. He let his voice carry the weight that his face couldn’t communicate to her.","\"Do you girls only eat when I’m around?\"","Selene was silent.","\"Food will be ready in two minutes,\" Dexter continued. \"Come and eat immediately. And next time, when I’m not here, you must eat the food I prepare. It’s not just food. It’s medicine. It helps your healing. Every meal is designed to push back the frost inside your body. Skipping them is not an option.\"","He paused.","\"Please make sure to eat. Even when I’m not around.\"","Selene was slightly stunned by his tone. He didn’t usually speak like this. Not to her.","But tonight he was stern towards her.","She slowly nodded her head and said quietly.","Okay,\"","Dexter held his position for a moment longer. Then he exhaled, nodded once, and turned back toward the house.","\"Good. Two minutes.\"","---","He walked to the kitchen and began plating the food.","He placed the stew into four bowls. Positioned them on the wooden dining table. Placed a spoon beside each bowl. Poured four cups of warm Star-Shaped Leaf tea.","Then he waited."]},{"number":210,"title":"Chapter 210 | When Will You Perform Your Marital Duties","paragraphs":["Mira arrived first.","She parked herself at the table, her crimson eyes scanning the bowls and then, aroma hit her, despite her earlier claim of not being hungry, her nostrils flared at the sweet smell.","Selene arrived second and walked carefully from the backyard and found her chair by memory, her fingers brushing the edge of the table as she sat down with her hands in her lap and waited.","Lyra was surprisingly the last to come as she came out from the bedroom without the Primordial Beast Egg as she walked to the table, sat down.","Dexter sat down at his own seat.","\"Lets eat.\" he said.","They all ate in silence.","As Dexter ate his own portion he observed the girls and noticed something different about Mira.","She was eating slowly and she was still in her first portion. She hadn’t asked for more.","Dexter frowned slightly.","Although this was the second time he was noticing it, it was still unusual. Lyra’s appetite had been massive for weeks.","She ate more than any human being he had ever encountered but now she wasn’t eating like usual.","Dexter discreetly activated his system interface and pulled up Lyra’s status panel.","[Name: Lyra Vance](Switch)","[Shadow Corruption Level: 0%]","The shadow corruption that had been at two percent for days, that the system had warned could reach one hundred percent and transform her body into a portal to the Shadow Realm, was completely gone.","Dexter frowned as the corruption level had reduced all the way to 0 so what was happening?","He checked Mira’s own.","[Name: Mira Calloway]","[Meridian Damage: 65% (Improved: 25% healed)]","[Nerve Regeneration: Right arm fully functional. Left arm: 15% nerve activity detected. Legs: 8% nerve activity detected.]","The Phoenix Heart Elixir, dissolved into the Celestial Dawn Nectar Bowl, had accelerated the repair significantly.","Her left arm was showing early signs of nerve activity. Her legs, while still far from functional, were beginning to respond.","Dexter closed the system interface.","The girls were all making progress and everything he was doing wasn’t wasted.","He placed Lyra behavior at the back of his mind as he continued to eat in silence.","Then, without warning, Dexter felt something.","He raised his head and saw Lyra was staring at him. He wanted to say so thing and then she suddenly smirked mischievously.","Dexter’s spoon paused halfway to his mouth as he stared at Lyra.","’So, husband.’","Lyra raised her head.","Her dark eyes locked onto Dexter across the table.","Her voice resonated through the minds of all three women and Dexter simultaneously.","\"When are we going to perform our marital duties?\"","The dining table immediately went silent and one could even hear pin drop throughout the entire house.","Mira’s Spectral Arms froze mid-motion, the spoon suspended between the bowl and her mouth.","Selene’s hand stopped halfway to her cup, her fingers hovering in the air.","Dexter, who had been in the middle of drinking a glass of water, felt the liquid travel down the wrong pipe.","\"Pfffttt!!!\"","He turned his head sharply to the side and spat out a mouthful of water to the side of the table rather than the table, or any of his wives.","He turned back sharply to Lyra as slight redness creeped up his neck.","\"Stop speaking nonsense,\" he said. \"What marital duties?\"","Lyra’s mysterious smile widened.","\"Don’t act as if you haven’t been thinking about it.\"","Dexter opened his mouth but before he could speak, Lyra’s voice sounded through their minds.","\"Three beautiful women in a house with a single man, of course you’ll be tempted.\"","She tilted her head slightly.","\"I don’t blame you. So which of us do you think you will start with? Me? Selene? Or Mira?\"","Dexter stared at her.","Then he frowned. If it was Mira who said this, he wouldn’t have been worried but it was Lyra who said this instead.","\"Are you okay?\" he asked in a concerned tone.","Lyra shrugged. \"What do you mean? I’m feeling quite alright.\"","Dexter frowned deeper. He subtly activated his system interface again, pulling up Lyra’s status panel while maintaining eye contact.","[Name: Lyra Vance](Switch)","[Shadow Corruption Level: 0%]","Dexter blinked.","Switch?","He stared at the word in the bracket beside Lyra’s name. He had never seen this tag before. The system had displayed various mental states for the girls. But he had never seen the world switch.","’ What the hell did \"switch\" mean?’","Dexter closed the interface.","\"Finish your food,\" he said, his voice carrying a firmness that was designed to end the conversation. \"Your food is getting cold.\"","Lyra snorted softly.","\"Fine. Don’t answer.\"","She picked up her spoon.","\"But we all know who you will choose first.\"","Dexter raised an eyebrow despite himself. \"Oh? Who do you think I will choose?\"","Lyra smirked. \"Of course you will choose Mira first.\"","Mira’s Spectral Arms jerked, causing the spoon to clatter against the rim of the bowl. Selene’s gaze changed slightly and a chill seem to rise through the entire house.","Dexter looked at Lyra for a long moment, then he smirked back.","\"What makes you think I wouldn’t choose you first?\"","The silence that followed was absolute as all three women stared at him, stunned.","Mira’s crimson eyes went wide and her mouth opened slightly.","Selene’s hand lowered her cup to the table with a soft click as her sightless eyes glanced at Dexter’s direction, and through her Echolocation, she was tracking his heartbeat.","Lyra’s smirk froze on her face as she blinked her eyes rapidly. She had wanted to tease Dexter but hadn’t expected to be teased back.","Dexter then chuckled.","\"If you are done with your shenanigans, finish your food, so you can heal up and cultivate. I have to wash the plates and cultivate and deal with some matters.\"","He returned his attention to his own bowl and resumed eating calmly like what had happened earlier was nothing.","The three women slowly resumed eating as the atmosphere had shifted slightly."]},{"number":211,"title":"Chapter 211 | That’s Lyra","paragraphs":["Selene finished her food first.","She placed her spoon neatly beside her bowl, stood up, and drifted toward the backyard without a word.","Mira finished second and also left.","It was obvious theh had been slightly unsettled by what had happened.","Lyra who was always the first to finish was the last to finish this time.","Dexter watched her from across the table, his own bowl long since empty.","’ Something is wrong.’","After the other two had left, Dexter turned his attention toward Lyra.","She was still sitting at the table, quietly eating.","Dexter flipped his right hand.","A packet of chips appeared in his palm.","He held it out toward her.","\"Do you want some?\"","Lyra glanced at the chips.","Then she looked directly at Dexter.","Her expression suddenly changed.","She leaned back, dropped her spoon onto the table, and folded her arms.","\"Are you testing me?\"","Dexter’s brows furrowed.","A strange feeling settled in his chest.","Testing her?","He deliberately kept his voice casual.","\"Testing you? Why would I test you?\"","Lyra stared at him for several seconds.","\"Why do you think I’m testing you?\"","Lyra’s gaze shifted toward the chips before returning to Dexter.","Then she chuckled.","Without another word, she stood up and walked toward the bedroom.","Dexter watched her back disappear through the doorway.","His brows furrowed even deeper.","Something is definitely wrong with her.","He didn’t immediately follow.","Instead, he took a deep breath, collected the girls’ plates, and washed the dishes.","He finished the dishes. Dried his hands. Walked to his room.","---","He sat on his bed, cross-legged and closed his eyes.","He wanted to cultivate but his mind wouldn’t settle.","He thought about Lyra, the diary, the voice, the \"Switch\" tag.","---","He opened his eyes, checked the time. 7:00 PM.","He stood up and walked to the living room.","Mira was in her wheelchair by the window. Cultivating. Her crimson hair caught the last light of the evening, turning it to burnished copper. Her Spectral Arms were folded behind her back, motionless. Her breathing was slow and steady.","\"Ready for your massage,\" Dexter said.","Mira opened her eyes.","In the past, there had always been a beat of hesitation before she agreed. A momentary flash of resistance. Pride battling practicality. The instinct to refuse warring with the knowledge that the massage was helping.","Tonight, there was no hesitation.","She nodded immediately.","The right arm was proof that his efforts were working so she didn’t fight him anymore. Well, not about this.","Dexter wheeled her to the bedroom.","As he pushed the wheelchair through the doorway, he saw Lyra.","She was sitting cross-legged on the bed, the Primordial Beast Egg cradled in her lap. Her eyes were closed as she was cultivating.","She opened her eyes as Dexter and Mira entered and looked at them and she understood what was happening.","All of a sudden, she suddenly smiled warmly as the cold Lyra from the dining room was gone.","She picked up the egg, cradling it carefully against her chest, and slid off the bed. She walked past Dexter, her shoulder brushing his arm as she passed.","’ Take care.’","She said in his mind and then she left the room.","Dexter watched her go.","’ She’s back to normal uhn?’","He shook his head. The oscillation between her personality was making him think she might have aplit personality or something.","He needed to cook the Harmony Congee. Tomorrow. First thing in the morning. Before anything else happened.","He turned back to Mira.","He lifted her from the wheelchair and placed her on the bed. Face down. He removed her blouse. Unclasped her bra. Draped a towel across her lower back for modesty.","He pulled on the Shockwave Glove. Applied the Grade-4 Spiritual Massage Oil. Set the vibration to its lowest setting.","He began.","The Massage Sutra guided his hands along the precise pathways of her meridian system. The Shockwave Glove hummed softly against her skin, sending gentle, penetrating vibrations deep into the muscle tissue. The Grade-4 oil seeped into her pores, its medicinal properties working in conjunction with the technique to stimulate nerve regeneration and repair damaged pathways.","He started with her shoulders. Moved to her upper back. Her spine. Her lower back.","The room was quiet. The glove hummed. The oil glistened. Mira’s breathing was slow and even.","Then she spoke.","\"Are you spooked?\"","Dexter’s hands paused for a fraction of a second. Then resumed.","\"What do you mean?\"","\"Lyra,\" Mira said. Her voice was muffled by the pillow. Relaxed. The particular tone of someone who was comfortable enough to speak about things that would normally be left unsaid. \"She’s been like that for a while.\"","Dexter’s hands paused again. Longer this time.","\"What do you mean, like that?\"","Mira turned her head slightly on the pillow. One crimson eye was visible, aimed sideways at nothing in particular.","\"She’s been like that from a young age,\" Mira said. \"Don’t be surprised if she behaves a bit unusual around you.\"","Dexter’s brow furrowed. His hands resumed their mechanical motion, but his mind was no longer on the massage.","\"She’s been like this since childhood?\"","Mira nodded against the pillow. \"Yeah. One minute she can be smiling at you. Warm. Sweet. The kindest person you’ve ever met. And the next minute...\"","She paused.","\"She can just decide to kill you.\"","Dexter’s brows furrowed even deeper.","\"For no reason at all,\" Mira continued. \"No provocation. No warning. No trigger. Just like a switch.\"","Dexter stared at the back of Mira’s head.","\"Which is why everyone is wary of her,\" Mira said. \"Everyone in the hero community. The Hero Associatio, the Nine Families and even the Villian’s organizations. Nobody dares to cross Lyra Vance. Not because she’s the strongest. But because she’s the most unpredictable.\"","Dexter chuckled. But the chuckle was hollow. \"She’s been alright for the past few weeks. I don’t think it’s like that.\"","Mira shrugged.","\"It was worse three years ago before the dungeon incident.\"","She paused.","\"She was the most troublesome hero in all of Stargate City. Absolutely no one dared to speak, move, or breathe wrong in her presence. She tried dueling with anyone strong. \"","\"If I and Selene weren’t strong enough, she might have defeated us too.\""]},{"number":212,"title":"Chapter 212 | Bloodline Manifestation","paragraphs":["\"If I and Selene weren’t strong enough, she might have defeated us too.\"","Dexter’s hands had stopped moving entirely. He was staring at Mira’s back, his mind struggling to reconcile the image she was painting with the girl who kissed his cheek over chips.","\"Luckily, that wasn’t the case,\" Mira said. \"But after the dungeon incident she became less predictable and ...\"","Mira searched for the word.","\"Quiet.\"","She exhaled slowly.","\"Most people in the city were relieved. Every hero in the city breathed easier because the troublemaker had been neutralized.\"","Dexter’s throat tightened.","\"She has more enemies than me and Selene combined,\" Mira continued. \"Even if you multiplied that combination by two.","She paused again.","\"If it weren’t for the fact that the assassins wanted to kill all three of us, I would have suspected the assassins came for Lyra specifically. With the amount of enemies she has made, it would have made more sense.\"","The room was very quiet.","\"But now that she can use mana again and her cultivation is returning...\"","She didn’t finish the sentence. She didn’t need to as Dexter understood she she meant.","Dexter frowned. He had only seen the cute side of Lyra, the shy, food-obsessed girl.","Mira seemed to read his thoughts.","\"She probably likes you,\" Mira repeated.","\"I suspected you might have died during the first week from unknown circumstances in your sleep.\"","Dexter sat on the edge of the bed,","’I guess I will have to keep an eye on her.’","Dexter made a quiet decision as his hands worked from Mira’s legs, to her upper thigh.","The glove’s vibration, which he had been gradually increasing throughout the session, was now at a moderate setting as it went through Mira’s internal body.","\"Hmm.\"","Mira suddenly let out a moan which made Dexter’s heart skipped a beat.","The atmosphere in the room froze as the temperature seem to increase","Dexter immediately cleared his throat and chose to think about something else like Lyra as he continued the massage.","He loved upper to Mira’s spine but then, his fingers found something.","Two marks on her shoulder blades. One on each side, unning from the center of each blade downward, tracing a path along the curve of her back before disappearing beneath the towel line.","Dexter’s hands stopped as he frowned. His fingers traced the length of the first mark and it was roughly ten inches long.","The skin was vivid red, the color of fresh inflammation and the marks looked like whip wounds. As though someone had taken a lash to her back, twice, in perfectly symmetrical strokes.","But nobody had touched Mira’s back except him. He had massaged her every day for two weeks. He had seen every inch of her skin. These marks had not been there yesterday.","\"Mira,\" Dexter said, his voice careful. \"Did something happen to you while I was gone?\"","Mira, face down on the bed, shrugged. \"No.\"","She paused. \"Why?\"","Another shrug. \"Do you think we’re hiding a man in the house?\"","Dexter chuckled despite his concern. \"You can’t hide a man. Even if you wanted to.\"","Mira snorted coldly at his mockery. Then she shifted slightly on the bed, adjusting her position as his fingers returned to the marks.","\"That kind of hurts,\" she said suddenly.","body part that had been numb for three years.","She frowned into the pillow. \"Is something there?\"","\"Yes,\" Dexter said. \"Something is there.\"","Mira’s brow furrowed. \"Huh?\"","\"Oh.\"","Her expression shifted from confusion to something more introspective. As though she was searching her memory for something she hadn’t thought important until now.","\"I had a dream,\" she said.","Dexter’s fingers paused on the marks.","\"Last night,\" Mira continued. \"I had a dream that I had wings. A pair of wings ripped out from my back. And I flew through the air like a phoenix or dragon. I’m not sure.\"","\"The pain of the wings ripping through my back felt very real,\" she said. \"I could feel the skin tearing, the muscles stretching. The bones pushing outward. It was...\"","She trailed off.","\"And it is at that exact spot you are touching.\"","Dexter stared at the two marks and his mind went to two words.","’ Bloodline Awakening.’","He had given all three girls the Bloodline Evolution Crystal weeks ago and had expected them to awaken their bloodlines relatively quickly, given the pace of their other improvements.","But the bloodline hadn’t awakened. Not for Mira. Not for Lyra. Not for Selene. Weeks had passed, and the system had shown no indication that the Bloodline Evolution Crystal had taken effect.","Dexter had begun to wonder if the crystal was defective. Or if the girls’ damaged bodies were unable to process the crystal’s energy while their meridians were still shattered.","Now he had his answer.","The awakening was happening but it was happening. The marks on Mira’s back were the physical manifestation of a bloodline trying to emerge.","Wings.","The dream, the pain, the marks, all of it pointed to the same conclusion. Whatever bloodline the Evolution Crystal was granting Mira, it involved wings and probably a phoenix bloodline, or something similar.","And the process was underway. Her body was changing at a cellular level, the dormant bloodline genes being activated and integrated into her physical structure. The marks were the first visible sign. The dream was the first conscious experience of the transformation.","’It won’t be long now. A month. Maybe two. The bloodline will fully manifest.’","Mira chuckled softly into the pillow.","\"This kind of feels like bloodline awakening,\" she said. The chuckle was self-deprecating.","Then she shook her head against the pillow.","\"No one in our family has ever awakened a bloodline, in the entire history of the Calloway family. We are talented and strong but we have never been a bloodline family.\"","She paused.","\"It would be nice, though. If I actually awakened one. We might have had the strength to rival those top three families. The Ashfords. The Sterlings. The Montclairs.\"","\"But it’s impossible, right?\""]},{"number":213,"title":"Chapter 213 | Matter Of Time","paragraphs":["Dexter’s hands resumed their motion as he continued the massage, working around the marks carefully to avoid direct contact with the sensitive areas while still channeling mana into the surrounding tissue.","\"Nothing is impossible,\" he said in a casual tone. \"What would happen if I actually managed to awaken a bloodline?\" He asked.","Mira was silent for a while, then she shook her head.","\"There is no need Imagining the impossible. Sticking to reality is better.\"","She paused.","\"I am already happy by the fact that I can finally move my right hand. And I am healing. Every day, I feel a little stronger and that is enough.\"","\"Asking for a bloodline would be asking for too much.\"","Dexter smiled knowingly.","He knew because he had given them the bloodline. The Bloodline Evolution food, quietly integrated into their bodies weeks ago. It was only a matter of time.","He was looking forward to it, looking forward to the moment when all three women discovered their talent.","The looks on their faces would be worth it.","He massaged Mira every day and saw her skin. He could detect the subtle changes in her body that signaled the bloodline’s emergence.","He didn’t massage Lyra or Selene.","He had no way of knowing what was happening beneath their skin and no way of monitoring the progress of a transformation that might already be underway without their knowledge.","This thought led to another thought.","The body massage Sutra wasn’t just a relaxation technique. It stimulated meridian function and accelerated the body’s natural healing processes.","If he applied the same technique to Selene and Lyra, their healing rates would increase dramatically.","But how could he tell two women, one of whom was blind and the other deaf and mute, that he wanted to rub oil on their bodies and press vibrating gloves against their skin?","How could he frame it in a way that didn’t make him sound like a pervert who just wanted to touch them and want satisfied with just touching one of them.","’I want to rub oil on your body and press vibrating gloves against your skin. Strictly for medical purposes, I promise.’","No version of that sentence existed that didn’t make him sound like a pervert.","He glanced at Mira, then an idea formed.","He could tell Mira and then if she agreed, she could communicate the proposal to Selene and Lyra.","Dexter turned to Mira.","\"How would you feel if I started giving Selene and Lyra massages?\"","The question landed in the quiet bedroom like a stone in still water.","Mira’s eyes opened.","\"The massage technique I use on you,\" Dexter continued, \"It stimulates healing at a cellular level, accelerates the body’s natural recovery process.\"","He paused.","\"If I apply the same technique to Selene and Lyra, their healing rates would increase significantly.\"","He looked at Mira.","\"In a month or two, Selene might show improvement in her vision, Lyra might show improvement in her hearing and by the end of the year, both of them could be significantly further along in their recovery than they would be without the massages.\"","The room suddenly went silent and in that instant, the temperature in the room increased drastically","Dexter’s eyes widened as he looked at her. Her eyes were closed and her expression was normal but Dexter could feel waves of incredible heat radiating off of her like a lava.","But in that split second, the rising temperature returned to normal as though it had been an illusion.","Mira then shrugged.","\"They are also your wives,\" she said in a light tone. \"You can do whatever you want to them.\"","Dexter blinked.","The words were fine as she acknowledged what he said, but Dexter’s spine tingled.","The brief, flash-fast spike in temperature that had originated from her body and disappeared before it could be confirmed.","’ She is angry.’","And it was the quiet type of anger!","She was jealous.","The jealousy of a woman who had something that was hers, a daily ritual, a private intimacy, a shared moment between husband and wife that nobody else was part of, and was now being told that this thing might be shared with others.","The massage was not just a medical procedure to Mira. It was the one part of her day that was exclusively hers. The time when Dexter’s attention was focused entirely on her.","And now he was proposing to extend that same intimacy to the other two.","Dexter understood it Immediately and sighed.","’I mess up again, didn’t I?’","Each wife had something that was uniquely theirs. A specific form of interaction that defined their relationship with him and separated it from their relationships with each other.","With Lyra, it was food. Snacks. Chips. Pastries. The small, edible gifts that made her eyes light up and her lips curve into brilliant smiles.","With Selene, it was warmth. The nightly cultivation sessions.","With Mira, it was the massage.","Each of these was sacred.","Sharing them across all three would dilute it.","The massage might increase the other two’s healing rates. That was true.","But logic was not the only operating principle in a household of three women and one man. Sometimes, preserving the emotional ecosystem was more important than optimizing the physical one.","The girls already had the Grand Cosmos Scripture. They didn’t need meridians to cultivate. Their Star Nodes were absorbing mana independently. The massage’s primary function, meridian stimulation, was largely redundant for them. Its secondary function, general healing acceleration, was helpful but not critical.","The benefit was incremental. The cost was disruption and it was not worth it.","Maybe later. When things had settled. When the bloodline awakenings were further along he would try again.","But not today.","Dexter shook his head.","\"Never mind,\" he said. \"I was just thinking out loud. Forget I said anything.\"","Mira’s eyes remained closed. Her expression remained neutral. The temperature in the room remained normal.","But something in the quality of her silence shifted.","The rest of the massage proceeded in silence.","Mira didn’t speak a single word or a complaint. She lay on the bed and accepted the massage with the passive, closed-eyed stillness of a woman who was processing something internally and did not wish to be disturbed while doing so.","When it was done, Dexter cleaned the oil from her skin, dressed her, and placed her in her wheelchair.","\"Thank you,\" she said without looking at him and wheeled herself out of the room.","Her Spectral Arms operated the wheels, carrying her down the hallway and into the living room without a backward glance.","Dexter stood in the bedroom doorway and watched her go.","’She’s definitely angry.’","He shook his head.","’Definitely behaving like a jealous cat.’","Dexter found this simultaneously exasperating and endearing.","Dexter shook his head again and walked to his room.","---","He cleaned up andcultivated for an hour,","After an hour, he opened his eyes and stretched. The tension from the day’s events faded and he stood up and walked to the kitchen.","It was late, nearly eight o’clock. The girls had eaten a substantial meal at five, so a heavy dinner wasn’t necessary. But they needed something before bed. A light meal that would provide sustained nourishment through the night without overwhelming their digestive systems.","He prepared a simple rice porridge. Plain. Gentle. Easy on the stomach. He added a thin slice of ginseng root for warmth and a handful of goji berries for their restorative properties. No mana infusion. No special techniques. Just good, simple food that would sit well in a body that was already processing the day’s accumulated spiritual energy.","He ladled the porridge into four bowls and called the girls.","They came.","Mira arrived first.","She ate quickly and finished before the others and then, she wheeled herself away from the table without a word and headed for the window in the living room..","Dexter watched her go.","’ Yep. Still angry.’"]},{"number":214,"title":"Chapter 214 | Others Had Died With That Gaze","paragraphs":["Mira arrived first.","She ate quickly and to Dexter’s shock, she finished before the others and then wheeled herself away from the table without a word and headed for the window in the living room.","Dexter watched her go.","’Yep. Still angry.’","Dexter frowned angrily. ’While I understand that she might be jealous, she’s well aware I didn’t marry just her right?’","He has tried to be understanding to the girls to the extent that others in his situation might even call him a whimp. But Dexter had suffered from his family which was why he was considerate to the girls because they had also being bullied by their own families.","But enough is enough. If he kept on keeping quiet, they would think he’s a real push over while he’s just trying his best to understand them.","Fine, they were the pride and talent of the city but now, it’s a different case.","Dexter who was thinking about this suddenly paused as he heard Lyra’s voice spoke in his mind.","’D-Dexter, c-can I have... more.’","Even till now, she was still hesitant about asking for more.","Dexter’s mind calmed a bit because as a Food smith, he felt quite proud when others ask for more of his food.","\"Of course. Give me a second.\"","Dexter smiled as he went to bring more meals for her.","And just like that, much to Dexter’s surprise, Lyra actually ate eight portions.","Thankfully, he had been prepared ahead of time and had prepared extra meals.","But even his precautions hadn’t been enough and by the eighth portion, the supply was running so low that he had to give her half of his own bowl to satisfy the final round.","She ate it with a all with a smile as then stared as Dexter with a gaze Dexter hadn’t seen in a long time.","’ What was that?’","He had seen that gaze in other’s face but only one had lived till now while the others had died.","And now, he was seeing that gaze in another’s person.","’ I’m probably wrong.’","Dexter stood at the sink as he started washing the plates.","\"Bang Bang Bang\"","Three sharp knocks at the gate.","’Who?’","Dexter’s Enhanced Hearing activated and in a split second, he identified the heartbeat before the third knock landed.","It was Tessa.","He dried his hands and walked to the gate.","In his way, he saw Mira was in the living room and was cultivating by the window.","She didn’t look up nor did she acknowledge his movement when he walked by like she sometimes does.","She was definitely still sulking and Dexter at this moment was alredy tired of it.","Dexter sighed and walked out of the house and then opened the gate.","Tessa stood on the other side with her usually smile on her face. Her curly red hair bounced in the evening breeze as her green eyes sparkled at the sight of him.","Suddenly, she tilted her head as the grin on her face faded slightly and was replaced by a curious look on her face.","\"You’re in a bad mood,\" she said without question.","Dexter was a bit surprised but he simply shrugged. \"Not particularly. How are you doing and how were sales today?\"","The word \"sales\" was the magic incantation and Tessa’s grin returned instantly.","\"Sales were fantastic!\" she declared. \"Way more customers than we expected. Some people came specifically to order your meals in batches this time.\"","\"We sold the first thirty portions at the standard price in under eight hours. Then, for the remaining twenty portions, I even had to increase the price.\"","Dexter raised an eyebrow. \"Increased it to what?\"","\"Eight thousand Dollars per portion.\"","Dexter stared at her.","\"Eight thousand?\"","\"Eight thousand,\" Tessa said with a proud smile on her face. \"The demand was so high that people were willing to pay double. I sold the last twenty portions at eight thousand each, and every single one was gone before closing.\"","She crossed her arms and tilted her chin upward.","\"I’m smart, aren’t I?\"","Dexter chuckled at her smartness and her cuteness.","\"Yes, yes,\" he said. \"You are definitely very smart.\"","And Dexter wasn’t even kidding. She had identified a supply-demand imbalance in real time, adjusted pricing on the fly, and maximized revenue without losing a single customer.","In a few years, with the right resources and guidance, Tessa was definitely going to be a force to be reckoned with in the business world.","Tessa pulled out her phone and transferred the day’s earnings to Dexter’s account.","Dexter’s phone buzzed and he checked the notification.","[Transfer received: 340,000 Dollars]","The number pushed his account balance back toward the seven-figure mark. The one million he had lost to Marcus’s scam was slowly being rebuilt.","Dexter smiled in relief. ’ In no time, I should be able to recover.’","At that moment, Tessa’s expression suddenly shifted as her gaze turned serious.","\"I heard about something happening today,\" she said casually. \"In the city.\"","Dexter looked at her curious about what she was about to say.","\"Harvest Homes was actually attacked by an angry customer,\" Tessa continued in a light but casual tone.","\"It wa said that someone actually sent an executive of Harvest Homes flying out of the building with one punch.\"","\"It was even said that if the executive wasn’t an Ultra Realm expert, they probably would have died from falling twenty-four floors.\"","Dexter’s expression didn’t change much but he raise an eyebrow of surprise and spoke.","\"Really? That’s insane.\"","Tessa nodded and continued.","\"The news tried to get information from Harvest Homes but they denied everything and even refused to share any details about the incident. It was really strange.\"","\"Don’t you think that’s weird?\"","Dexter stared at Tessa as he thought in his mind.","’ Why is she telling me this specifically?’","Harvest Homes wasn’t the only incident in the city today as Stargate City was a metropolis of millions and things happened every day. Crimes, accidents, hero interventions, monster sightings.","But Tessa had chosen to tell him about this specific incident out of everything that had happened in the city today.","Which meant one of two things. Either she was making conversation and this was the most interesting thing she had heard today. Or she knew something.","[A/N: You guys left enough gifts I had no choice but it Mass release so, the 5 Chapter Mass release within 2 hours. Others are complaining that I’m writing authors note here instead of the space given by WebNovel. I do this so I don’t want you guys to have to click on the button. Moreover, I make sure my authors note doesn’t waste or take your coin so I don’t think it’s harmful. Tell me what you think guys. I’d like your opinion.]"]},{"number":215,"title":"Chapter 215 | Want to Try Something...","paragraphs":["Dexter’s face remained impassive.","\"What is Harvest Homes?\" he asked. His voice carried the perfect blend of ignorance and disinterest. \"Some kind of store? And why would it be my business either way?\"","Then he shrugged and changed the subject smoothly.","\"How many containers did you bring this time?\"","Tessa gazed at Dexter for what seem to be an uncomfortable about if time before she suddenly smiled and spoke.","\"I brought one hundred this time,\" she said.","Dexter was stunned.","\"One hundred?\"","\"One hundred,\" Tessa confirmed, hefting two large bags onto the gate post. \"Customers have already pre-ordered twenty meals for tomorrow. So one hundred is the minimum to make enough sales for the day.\"","Dexter blinked.","One hundred portions was a bit much and required even more preparations.","Which meant waking up at 3 AM instead of 5.","He sighed.","\"Alright then,\" he said, accepting the bags. \"I guess I’ll have to wake up very early tomorrow morning.\"","Tessa grinned. Then her expression turned soft.","\"So,\" she said. \"Have you made your decision about the festival? It’s next tomorrow, you know.\"","Dexter looked at her and frowned. He had almost forgotten about the festival and wouldn’t have gone if the girls hadn’t decided to come.","\"Alright. I’ll come.\"","The smile that broke across Tessa’s face was astonishing as dimples lit up in her cheeks, and radiated outward with enough warmth to melt the sun itself.","\"Perfect!\" she squealed. \"I can’t wait to introduce you to the other neighbors!\"","Dexter held up a warning finger.","\"Don’t get any ideas.\"","Tessa placed both hands over her heart with exaggerated innocence. \"Of course not. I’m a very good girl.\"","Dexter snorted. \"Good night, Tessa.\"","\"Good night, Dexter!\"","She chuckled and then turned back and Dexter watched as she skipped down the sidewalk as she waved at him.","Dexter closed the gate and then locked it as he back inside.","---","Mira was still in the parlor, cultivating and even when he walked past her, she didn’t say anything like she always did.","He didn’t say anything as he entered the kitchen and placed the bags of containers on the counter, organized them neatly, and confirmed that he had sufficient ingredients in his spatial storage to produce one hundred portions of Grade One Enchanted Meal.","Then he walked to his room, closed the door, and sat cross-legged on his bed as he began cultivating the mana hurricane around his house was starting to erupt when suddenly a ding rang out in his mind.","’Finally! The system notification.’","He was a bit excited about it because with more power, he could oppress his enemies which he silent increased after today and maybe when the Ashford family might come after him this time.","’[Ding!]","The notification materialized in his mind as a golden text hovered in the darkness behind his closed eyelids.","He was about to read it when he heard footsteps drectly in front of his door.","Dexter’s Enhanced Hearing focused and he isolated the heartbeat. Then he realized that heartbeat was familiar but also not familiar.","He knew Lyra’s heartbeat as he heard it every day as he knew it the way he knew his own pulse. Intimately.","This heartbeat was close to Lyra’s and had the same base rhythm and the same general pattern. But there were subtle differences that even confused Dexter. It was faster than usual.m this time, faster than when Lyra had always been nervous to asked for extra meals.","It was Lyra’s heartbeat and also not quite.","Dexter’s hand moved toward his spatial storage. His fingers twitched, ready to summon the Void Star Saber at a moment’s notice but then the scent reached him and he immediately knew who it was. At that split second, the door suddenly opened.","A tall, dark-haired woman stepped into the room. As she stepped into the room, she turnd and then closed the door behind her.","Then she suddenly turned around and to Dexter’s confirmation, it was Lyra.","Dexter smiled as he projected his thoughts to her.","\"Is something the matter? Do you need something?\"","Lyra nodded, then she shook her head and then nodded again.","Dexter was confused but then he smile as he fliped his hand and a chip oppress in his hand.","Lyra quickly end forward as she snatched it in her hands.","She at on his bed and started to eat it but then she passed as she stared at Dexter.","\"Do you want more or do you need something?\"","\"I...\" Lyra’s telepathic voice stuttered. The tremor was back. Stronger than before. \"I want to try something.\"","Dexter blinked. \"What do you want to try?\"","Lyra’s blush deepened and she looked down at the chips in her lap in embarrassment as her fingers tightened around the bag, crinkling the plastic.","Then she shook her head.","\"No, nothing, forget it.\"","She reached for another chip and began eating again but even faster this time.","Dexter watched her for a moment then he flipped his hand and a Celestial Pastry appeared as he held it out toward her.","Lyra saw the pastry and her eyes widened as she looked at the pastry then at Dexter, then at the pastry again.","And with speed even shockjng to Dexter, she snatched it from his hand with the speed of a striking cobra.","Then she looked at him with a deep blush spreading from her cheeks to her ears to the visible skin above the collar of her shirt.","\"I wanted to try this,\" she said.","She placed the chips on the bed beside her. Both hands free as she straightened her posture and drew in a breath.","\"You’ve been so good to me,\" she said. Her telepathic voice was barely above a whisper. \"And I feel I should do something for you.\"","In in that split second, she leaned forward.","Dexter’s mind processed the approaching motion. He expected her lips to touch his cheek. The same gesture she had performed that morning in the kitchen, when the chips and pastries had overwhelmed her gratitude and her body had acted before her brain could intervene.","A cheek kiss. That was what he was preparing for. A brief, warm, slightly awkward press of lips against skin that would leave him flustered and her blushing and both of them pretending it hadn’t happened.","Her lips didn’t touch his cheek.","They touched his lips.","Dexter’s eyes widened.","His entire body went into shock like what was actually happening was an hallucination instead as his heart skipped two solid beats!"]},{"number":216,"title":"Chapter 216 | Who Are You!?","paragraphs":["The warmth started in his chest, spreading outward through his neck, across his face and unto his lips, which were still pressed against Lyra’s, lips.","Without his instruction. Hus hands rose from the bed as it found her cheeks.","It was warm and softer than he had expected from the bed and found the side of Lyra’s face.","’Is this okay?’","Dexter suddenly asked but at that moment, Lyra leaned into his hand as she pressed her cheek against his palm.","’Yes .’","The moment she said this, the kiss went even deeper as the two lips entangled even further than the French kiss.","Lyra’s fingers slid through his hair as she gradually pulled him even closer, consuming his lips like a predator.","In that split second, something sparked in the back of Dexter’s mind. But before it could register itself, the warm sensation form the kiss overwhelmed Dexter’s mind.","Even when the sensation worked through his body, Dexter almsot didn’t feel it. Who in their right mind would ignore a top beauty kiss!?","His hand rose and unconsciously found Lyra’s waist as he pulled her closer.","In that split second, Lyra moved forward, even closer to Dexter as she suddenly shifted her body and then landed on Dexter’s lap as her legs folded on either side of his crossed knees. Her weight settled onto his lap and her arms wrapped around his neck.","In that moment, she kissed him deeper.","And in that split second, the spark in the back of his mind flared again.","’ Is something wrong?’","The thought was vague but immediately vanished as he thought about it.","Then the Tranquility Band on his wrist suddenly activated as a wave of cool, soothing energy radiated from the band into Dexter’s wrist, traveling up his arm and into his brain like ice water being splashed into his brain.","In that split second, the fog lifted and his brain started to work and everything connected in that split second.","The kiss was real, the body, the lips and everything else law but the person behind them...","\"Bang!\"","Dexter’s activated Flame Burst Step and his body blurred, as he flashed away from the bed and glared at the figure on the bed.","Lyra still sat on the bed where he had left her and her face was of pure genuine confusion.","\" What ?\" she said.","The telepathic voice trembled. \" What happened? Why?\"","She was incredibly confused and her eyes started to turn teary and she was very hurt.","Just now, she had just shared an incredible kiss with Dexter a few seconds ago and now Dexter had actually recoiled away as though it worst thing he had ever felt.","She looked genuinely hurt. And when Dexter saw this, his heart pounded.","But Dexter’s clarity had not faded and he glared at Lyra as he suddenly spoke.","\"You are not Lyra, are you?\"","Lyra blinked in confusion as she stared at him.","\" What do you mean by that?\" Her telepathic voice continued to sound so sweet it was almost identical. \" We just kissed and now you’re denying me? Is it because of Mira and Selene? You can tell me if that’s the case.\"","\"Don’t bring them into this,\" Dexter immediately snapped. \"You are not Lyra. Who are you?\"","His voice resonated through the entire room as he stared at Lyra indifferently.","Lyra’s face which was confused suddenly turned even more pitiful at Dexter’s words.","But even after seeing this, Dexter still stared at her coldly.","The room turned silent for a almost a minute and then strangely, Lyra’s lips suddenly lifted up until it formed an amused smirk on her face.","Sha gently stood up from the bed touched the corner of her mouth with one finger as she said in a thoughtful tone.","\"That’s quite strange.\" she said.\"","The voice was cold and the telepathic voice had changed. It wasn’t as sweet as it had always sounded. Even when Lyra was mad, she didn’t sound like that!","\"I behaved eaacvrly like she would. But you still noticed. But don’t you think it was a little too late? \" she continued.","\"You already kissed me.\"","She tilted her head.","\" Or should I say, you just sexually assaulted Lyra? You kissed her without her permission in the first place\"","Dexter’s blood ran cold and his face turned extremely cold as his saber instantly materialized in his hand.","The dark blade hummed as it drank the light around it as he pointed the blade at the strange Lyra.","\"If you don’t speak this instant, I will make you speak.\"","Lyra looked at the blade and then she looked at him and suddenly laughed.","The sweet laugh echoed in Dexter’s mind and it was even colder than before.","\" What are you going to do?\" she asked. \" Kill me?\"","She tilted her head again as her smirk widened.","\" Kill her?\"","\" Come ,\" she said, spreading her arms wide. \"Try it if you dare.\"","Dexter’s grip on the saber tightened. His knuckles went white. He had never expected this circumstance to happen and didn’t even think it was possible in real life.","But he didn’t move because that strange Lyra was right.","He couldn’t kill her because the body standing in front of him was Lyra’s body. The incredibly cute and sweet girl and if he struck, it would directly affect Lyra!","The entity wearing Lyra’s body knew this and she chuckled seeing the struggle on Dexter’s face.","Suddenly, Dexter’s face relaxed and he shook his head with a small smile on hhs face.","\"There are other things I can do apart from killing,\" he said.","The entity raised an eyebrow.","\" Oh ?\" The telepathic voice carried amusement. \"What other things? You just kissed me with your tongue, so what other things can you do to me? Besides kissing me again, I mean, I wouldn’t object.\"","Dexter’s jaw tightened, the saber hummed in his grip as the Ancient Flame Demon Bloodline stirred. In that split second, massive heat radiated from his skin rapidly as the air around him shimmered.","But the entity didn’t flinch."]},{"number":217,"title":"Chapter 217 | Aurelyx","paragraphs":["Dexter continued staring at Lyra with a frosty look on his face.","\"Tch...boring.\"","Lyra clicked her tongue and rolled her eyes and then smirked.","\"You can call me Aurelyx.","Dexter stared at her as his heart squeezed tightly. It was even more serious than he feared, it was a whole other personality and it even has a name.","Dexter’s aura started to leak out of his body as killing intent flashed in his mind.","\"What the fuck are you doing in Lyra’s body?\"","Aurelyx laughed and it sounded sinister and sweet at the same time in Dexter’s mind.","\"Lyra?\" she repeated. \"Lyra’s body?\"","She tilted her head.","\"What makes you think this is Lyra’s body and not my body?\"","Dexter’s eyes narrowed.","Then he grinned coldly.","\"Do you think you can manipulate me?\" he said. \"If it wasn’t Lyra’s body, you would be called Lyra. You would be the one with the name, and she would be the one who had to invent one for herself.\"","He held her gaze.","\"But she is called Lyra. And you had to name yourself Aurelyx. You named yourself because you’re the addition.\"","Aurelyx’s eyes flashed coldly.","Then she smiled.","\"Now I get why Lyra likes you,\" she said. \"I assumed she liked you because you give her food. That’s what I thought. Chips and pastries and six-bowl stews. Simple transactional affection. Feed the hungry girl and she follows you home.\"","She paused.","\"But it’s different, isn’t it? She likes you because you see things. You notice what other people don’t. You pay attention.\"","Her eyes held his.","\"That’s dangerous. For someone like me.\"","Dexter didn’t acknowledge the compliment. He didn’t acknowledge the threat. He simply stood there, saber still in his hand but lowered to his side, and spoke.","\"What do you want?\"","Aurelyx shrugged. Lyra’s shoulders. Lyra’s movement. But the casualness was exaggerated. Performed. The shrug of someone who was very deliberately trying to appear relaxed.","\"I don’t want anything.\"","\"Then what do you mean by kissing me?\"","The question was blunt. Uncomfortable. The kind of question that most people would circle around with diplomatic language and careful phrasing. Dexter didn’t bother. He wanted a straight answer and he was going to get one.","Aurelyx’s expression didn’t change.","\"Why can’t I just kiss you because I like you?\"","Dexter’s grin faded as his expression hardened.","\"State your true intentions,\" he said. \"Do you really believe I can do nothing to restrain you? Do you truly believe I have no means of dealing with you?\"","The threat was not explicit. It didn’t need to be. The Void Star Saber humming at his side was explicit enough. The Ancient Flame Demon Bloodline radiating heat from his skin was explicit enough. The fact that he had just fought an Ultra Realm expert to a standstill earlier that afternoon was explicit enough.","Aurelyx gazed into his eyes.","She was searching. Reading. Analyzing the micro-expressions and the mana fluctuations and the subtle, almost imperceptible signals that told her whether the man in front of her was bluffing or not.","She had been watching him for weeks. Through Lyra’s eyes. Through Lyra’s ears. Through Lyra’s brain. She had observed the way he moved, the way he fought, the way he made decisions. She had catalogued his abilities, his resources, his patterns.","She knew about the Seventh-Tier cultivation technique he had given the girls. A technique that shouldn’t exist. That was beyond anything any family in the city possessed. That had no business being in the hands of a disowned bastard with an F-Rank mana affinity.","She knew about the Type-3 weapons he had placed in their room. Weapons that had since been swapped for something even more powerful, though she hadn’t yet determined what.","She knew he had means. Connections. Resources. A background that didn’t match his public profile.","She also knew that he was serious. Right now, in this moment, he was not playing. He was not negotiating. He was demanding.","She smiled.","\"You’re quite boring, you know that?\" she said.","Dexter didn’t respond.","\"Others would have taken advantage of this,\" she continued. Her voice carried a trace of genuine bewilderment, as though she was describing behavior she had encountered in others and found incomprehensible. \"Others would have taken advantage of this opportunity. A beautiful woman enters their room at night. Locks the door. Sits on their bed. Kisses them.\"","She spread her hands.","\"But you? You’re behaving like a cute, innocent virgin boy. Others would have slept with me by now. But you...\"","She frowned.","\"Annoying.\"","Dexter’s expression didn’t waver.","\"Speak,\" he said coldly.","Aurelyx stared at him for a long moment. Then she sighed.","\"Fine,\" she said. \"I was teasing you. That’s all.\"","Dexter’s eyes narrowed.","\"You just wanted to tease me. So you decided to kiss a stranger instead.\"","\"That’s a lie, isn’t it?\" he added.","Aurelyx rolled her eyes.","\"Fine,\" she said again. \"It’s about your heavenly physique.\"","Dexter’s heart skipped a beat.","But his face didn’t change.","\"What heavenly physique?\" he said in a puzzled tone.","\"I have no idea what you are talking about.\"","Aurelyx sneered.","\"Now you are denying,\" she said. \"You should learn to lie better.\"","Dexter’s expression remained blank. \"I truly have no idea what you are talking about.\"","Aurelyx rolled her eyes again. Harder this time. More exasperated.","\"Fine,\" she said for the third time. The response of someone who was accustomed to getting their way through persistence and was running out of patience with a man who refused to play along.","\"If you won’t admit you have a heavenly physique, then I won’t tell you what I plan to do.\"","She turned away.","The movement was abrupt. Final. The kind of turn that signaled the end of a conversation rather than a pause in one. She walked to the door, unlocked it, and pulled it open.","Dexter stood in the center of the room, watching her go. His mind was still processing. Still analyzing. Still trying to determine how much she actually knew and how much she was guessing and whether the gap between the two was wide enough to be safe.","She stepped through the doorway. Paused.","Without turning back, she spoke one final time.","\"Good night, Dexter.\""]},{"number":218,"title":"Chapter 218 | Selene...","paragraphs":["The door closed behind her and Dexter stood alone in his room.","He stared at the closed door, then he punched the air in anger.","\"What the fuck,\" he muttered to the empty room.","He sat down on his bed and pressed his palms against his face.","The first question was the most fundamental. When had the switch happened? When Lyra entered his room, was she Lyra? Or was she already Aurelyx?","He replayed the sequence.","The first one had seemed like Lyra. The shyness. The hesitation. The nervous energy.","But the heartbeat had been slightly wrong but even then, the chips.","’Was she Aurelyx from the beginning? Or did they switch midway?’","The chips. The way her eyes had lit up. The way she had flashed across the room. The way she had eaten with content, rhythmic precision. The \"thank you\" that was soft and warm and genuine.","That had felt like Lyra. Completely, absolutely Lyra.","But then the crunching had stopped. The gaze had changed. The kiss had happened. And the voice that followed the kiss, the voice that asked \"You don’t like it?\", had carried a tremor that could have been either Lyra’s genuine nervousness or Aurelyx’s imitation of Lyra’s genuine nervousness.","’Did they switch during the kiss? Was Lyra the one who initiated it, and Aurelyx the one who took over when it deepened?’","’Or was Aurelyx there from the start, performing Lyra’s nervousness with enough accuracy to fool me?’","He didn’t know.","And that was the part that was driving him insane.","Was it Lyra? The sweet, shy, chip-loving girl who had kissed his cheek and then run away? Or was it Aurelyx? The Shadow Queen?","The uncertainty was maddening.","And then there was the other thing. The thing that Aurelyx had said before she left.","’Your heavenly physique.’","Dexter’s hands tightened into fists.","How did she know? What did she know? How much had she observed during her time in control of Lyra’s body?","’Think. Think. Think. The only way she can know about the physique is if she can sense it or she can actually read my inner most thoughts unlike Lyra who can read just the surface.’","He didn’t know that either.","Dexter lay back on his bed and stared at the ceiling.","Everything was starting to make sense now. The strange behaviors. The cold voice in the bedroom. The diary entry. The single-portion meals. The \"Are you testing me?\" reaction to the chips. All of it was starting to make sense.","It had been Aurelyx every time.","Two people and one body. One who remembered everything and one who remembered nothing.","And Dexter was caught between them.","He thought about what to do. The options were limited. He could confront Lyra directly, tell her about Aurelyx, and hope that the knowledge would help rather than harm. But he didn’t know if telling Lyra might trigger her or cause even more harm than good.","Or it might help and give Lyra the awareness she needed to fight back.","He didn’t know which but he knew one thing.","Between Aurelyx and Lyra, he had already chosen Lyra and not the Shadow Queen.","His Lyra.","Dexter would find a way to erase Aurelyx. To remove the secondary personality from Lyra’s body and give Lyra full, permanent, unchallenged control over her own mind and her own life.","He didn’t know how yet ans didn’t have the tools yet or knowledgeyet but he would find them.","Whatever it took and however long it took.","’ For now, I can only keep an eye on her.’","The thought was unsatisfying. But it was the only strategy available to him at the moment. Charging into Lyra’s room and demanding answers from Aurelyx would accomplish nothing except potentially destabilizing a situation that was already balanced on a knife’s edge.","He was still pondering when the door opened.","\"Click.\"","Dexter’s expression changed instantly.","The killing intent erupted from his body before his conscious mind could intervene.","For a split second, he thought Aurelyx had returned.","His hand shot toward his spatial storage as the Void Star Saber’s hilt materialized against his palm and his muscles coiled as his mana surged.","The door opened fully.","Dexter froze.","It wasn’t Aurelyx nor was it Lyra.","It was Selene.","She stood in the doorway, her silver-white hair falling over her shoulders, her pale face tilted slightly forward, her sightless eyes aimed roughly in his direction. She wore a simple white sleeping gown that reached her upper thighs, and her bare feet made almost no sound on the wooden floor.","At the same moment she appeared, the temperature in the room plummeted.","An icy chill seeped through the doorway like fog rolling across a frozen lake.","Selene had sensed Dexter’s killing intent and her face turned cold.","’Assassin.’","Without hesitation, her own killing intent exploded.","’BOOM!’","A violent, chilling aura erupted from Selene’s body.","The frost on the doorframe exploded outward, coating the walls, the ceiling, the floor. The window behind Dexter developed a thick layer of ice that blocked the moonlight. The air temperature dropped below freezing in an instant, cold enough to make breath painful, cold enough to freeze moisture on contact.","The killing intent was staggering.","It didn’t roar or crash or thunder like Dexter’s flame-forged aggression. It was silent as it consumed Dexter’s own.","Dexter’s eyes widened.","’What the...’","He hadn’t expected Selene to respond with a counter-surge that made his own killing intent feel like a campfire compared to a blizzard.","For a brief moment, the two killing intents collided and the atmosphere in the room became suffocating. Fire and ice.","Even crippled and blind and chronically ill. The killing intent she radiated was enough to make Dexter’s survival instincts scream.","He was caught off guard.","Not by the power. By the speed. By the instant, reflexive response of a woman who should have been helpless but whose body still remembered how to kill.","Dexter immediately withdrew his killing intent.","\"Wait,\" he said. His voice was calm. Firm. Designed to cut through the confusion without escalating it. \"There isn’t an assassin.\"","Selene’s killing intent held for another moment, then it gradually, it faded."]},{"number":219,"title":"Chapter 219 | Selene... II","paragraphs":["The frost stopped spreading and the temperature began to climb as the oppressive weight in the air dissipated, replaced by the normal, comfortable atmosphere maintained by the Pure-Air Fragrance Artifact.","Selene tilted her head toward Dexter’s direction.","\"Then why were you releasing killing intent?\"","Dexter fell silent.","How was he supposed to explain that he had spent the past several hours worrying about the possibility of Aurelyx returning?","He sighed.","\"It’s a long story.\"","Selene frowned slightly. The expression was subtle, visible only in the slight tightening of the skin around her pale eyes and the barely perceptible downward pull of her lips.","\"A long story?\"","\"Yeah.\"","He looked at her. She was standing in the doorway, her white sleeping gown slightly rumpled, her silver hair disheveled.","Dexter hesitated for a moment.","Then he spoke.","\"What do you know about Aurelyx?\"","The effect was immediate.","Selene’s eyes flashed and as harp, sudden flash of recognition that triggered her Echolocation into a burst of rapid, intense pulses, as though her body had involuntarily sharpened its senses in response to a name that carried weight.","Her brows furrowed.","\"Where did you hear that name?\"","Dexter blinked.","The reaction was not what he had expected.","Selene knew the name.","Dexter’s mind recalibrated instantly.","\"I heard it randomly,\" he said carefully. \"When I was speaking with the heroes at the meeting today. Someone mentioned it in passing.\"","It was a lie. He knew it was a lie. Selene probably knew it was a lie. But the truth, that Aurelyx had appeared in his bedroom and kissed him and claimed to be a separate personality living inside Lyra, was not a truth he was prepared to share. Not yet. Not without understanding more.","Selene’s expression became solemn.","She stood in the doorway for a long moment, her body perfectly still, her head tilted slightly downward.","Then she spoke.","\"Aurelyx is said to be the number one assassin in this city.\"","The words landed in the room like stones.","Dexter stared at her.","\"No one knows who she is,\" Selene continued in a quiet voice as thought she didn’t want anyone else to hear. \"No one knows who he or she is. No one has seen their face or one knows where they live or who they work for.\"","She paused.","\"But it is said that Aurelyx is the number one assassin in the entire city. Possibly in the country and any mission accepted has a 100 percent success rate and have never failed.\"","Dexter’s mind went blank.","The number one assassin in the entire city.","Aurelyx which was living inside Lyra was actually that person.","The number one assassin in the entire city is a split personality living inside my wife?","That didn’t make sense.","Aurelyx was a secondary consciousness likely due to the incident. An alternate personality that surfaced and retreated within Lyra’s body. She wasn’t a separate physical person and couldn’t operate independently to execute assassinations without Lyra’s body being present.","Unless...","Unless the switching happened frequently enough, and she was actually the main one personality.","The possibility was horrifying but entirely plausible.","\"Moreover,\" Selene continued, \"the name has circulated through the upper echelons of the Hero Association. The top brass are aware of her existence. They have a file on her, although it’s apparently mostly empty and the one they have is about her kills.\"","She paused.","\"Anyone who knows that name should probably distance themselves from anyone associated with it.\"","Dexter’s face didn’t change. But inside, his mind was racing like a horse through a desert.","The number one assassin in the city was lyra.","Aurelyx isn’t just a personality fragment. She’s a functional, operational, professional assassin who has been conducting missions from inside Lyra’s body for years. Probably since before the dungeon incident.","It wasn’t Lyra they were afraid of, it was Aurelyx.","Dexter’s eyes narrowed.","\"You said Aurelyx has never failed a mission,\" he said.","\"Yes.\"","\"Do you know anything else about her?\"","Selene shook her head.","\"Not much,\" she said. \"Nobody knows her true identity. Nobody knows her appearance. Nobody knows where she lives or who she works for.\"","\"Then how does the Hero Association know about her?\"","Selene shook her head slowly. \"They don’t know her. They only know the results.\"","\"The results?\"","\"Every target she accepts dies.\"","\"Regardless of how heavily protected the target is,\" Selene continued. \"Regardless of their cultivation level. Regardless of their security detail or their defensive formations or their relic equipment. She always finds a way.\"","She paused.","\"Always.\"","Dexter fell silent.","Aurylex was something else entirely. He thought about the shadow corruption.","The system had reported Lyra’s shadow corruption at zero percent. But Aurelyx had said she was the Shadow Queen. What if the shadow corruption hadn’t been cleansed? What if it had been absorbed? Integrated? Converted from a corrupting influence into a power source by a consciousness that knew how to wield it?","What if Aurelyx was, in her own right, an extraordinarily powerful entity who had been operating from inside Lyra’s body for years, conducting assassinations, accumulating power, and building a reputation as the most dangerous killer in the city?","All while Lyra slept.","Dexter’s gaze darkened.","Selene noticed the shift in his expression. Through her Echolocation, she could detect the subtle changes in his body.","\"Is something wrong?\" she asked.","Dexter immediately shook his head.","\"Nothing is wrong.\"","He forced a smile which made Selene blink.","She didn’t believe him but since Dexter didn’t want to talk about it, she couldn’t force him.","\"All right,\" she said. Her voice carried a trace of reluctance. \"I should take my leave.\"","She turned around and left.","Dexter watched her begin to leave as her hand found the doorframe.","\"Wait,\" Dexter said.","Selene froze at the door and her hand remained on the frame with her body half-turned toward the hallway, one foot already across the threshold.","She froze.","Then, in a voice so soft voice, she murmured.","\"We can wait until you’re in a good mood.\"","[A/N: I’ve promised a lot and I’ve utterly failed. I can’t think of a worthy explanation for you all. I’ve disappointed you and I’m ashamed of my self. I won’t promise again cause I seem to always fail at that. I really and truly apologize for that. So I will stop speaking about mass release. Won’t be surprised if y’all stopped reading the book cause of that. I truly am utterly and deeply sorry for that. Any explanation would just be an excuse. Please accept my apology. Also, this isn’t a filler you can count, just in case.]"]},{"number":220,"title":"Chapter 220 | Rely On Me!","paragraphs":["Selene froze at the door and her hand remained on the frame with her body half-turned toward the hallway, one foot already across the threshold.","She froze.","Then, in a voice so soft voice, she murmured.","\"We can wait until you’re in a good mood.\"","Sha felt that she might be a burden to Dexter and immediately wanted to leave.","This made Dexter’s chest tighten and he spoke immediately.","\"No, I’m quite alright.\"","He paused as he continued in an honest tone.","\"And even if I’m in a bad mood, I will always want to help you.\"","Selene’s body trembled slightly as though she heard singling she almost couldn’t believe.","Selene didn’t respond immediately and five seconds passed.","’ Did I say too much ?’","Just when Dexter was about to speak and assure her; Selene suddenly nodded her head.","\"Okay,\" Then she turned back into the room with her head was lowered. Her silver hair fell forward, screening her face as she walked to the bed slowly.","She reached the edge of the bed and then under dexter’s gaze, she sat down.","Then after a while, she crossed her legs beneath her, placed her hands on her knees with palms upward and then closed her eyes.","She began cultivating.","Dexter watched her settle and the tension in her posture gradually eased. He immediately exploded with his heavenly flames, letting the intense heat wash through her entire body and even the entire room.","Suddenly, ao thing sparked in Dexter’s mind and he felt bolder.","\"Come closer to the bed,\" he said. \"So your back can rest against the headboard.\"","He leisurely patted the space directly beside him.","Selene’s body froze as her white eyes opened andwidened.","She blinked rapidly, obviously startled by Dexter’swords.","Through her Echolocation, she could perceive him him and the space he was pointing to. The space that was directly next to his body.","He was asking her to sit next to him.","Selene blinked again and her ears turned pink. Dexter wasn’t asking and was telling her as though it was a casual thing she could do.","She was about to shake her head when to Dexter’s shock, she nodded her head slowly as the blush crept from her ears down her neck,","She suddenly leaned and then placed her hand on the bed as she bent down like a cute cat and then cat-crawled forward.","Seeing the arc of her back made Dexter’s heart race like a position in an engine!","That move was so damn captivating!","Selene moved across the bed on all fours, her silver hair swinging beneath her, until she reached the space beside him and then she settled.","Her back found the headboards her knees crossed beneath her as her shoulder came to rest against his.","The contact was electric.","The warmth that had been reaching her in diluted waves across the bed now flowed directly into her body through the point of contact. The heat seeped through her sleeping gown, through her skin, through the damaged meridians beneath, and into the cold that lived in her bones.","And she exhaled.","They sat together. Shoulder to shoulder. Backs against the headboard. Cultivating in silence.","The mana flowed. The Star Nodes absorbed. The cold and the heat coexisted in the small bedroom, finding equilibrium in the narrow space between two bodies that were, in their own quiet way, learning to share space.","Minutes passed.","Then Selene spoke.","\"You’re still thinking about her, aren’t you?\"","Dexter froze.","The question came from nowhere. Or rather, it came from the particular nowhere that existed between two people sitting close enough to feel each other’s heartbeats. The space where observations formed without conscious intent and words escaped without permission.","\"About who?\" Dexter asked. His voice was carefully neutral.","\"Aurelyx.\"","Dexter stared at her profile. Her silver hair. Her pale skin. Her closed eyes. The faint, barely visible smile on her lips.","\"You aren’t very good at hiding things,\" Selene said.","Dexter sighed.","\"You’re becoming quite perceptive,\" he said.","\"I’ve always been perceptive.\" Selene’s lips curved slightly. The smile was small. Quiet. The smile of someone who had just delivered a compliment to themselves and was slightly amused by it. \"After all, I can’t see. I have to rely on everything else.\"","Her head tilted toward him.","\"Your heart rate changes when you’re thinking about something that bothers you. It becomes slightly irregular. Not enough for most people to notice. But I notice.\"","She paused.","\"Your breathing changes too. It becomes more controlled. More deliberate. As though you’re trying to regulate your thoughts by regulating your lungs.\"","Another pause.","\"And your body temperature fluctuates. When you’re calm, the heat from your bloodline is steady. Even. When you’re disturbed, it pulses. Like a heartbeat within a heartbeat.\"","Dexter looked at her.","She had been studying him. Not visually. Not through observation of facial expressions or body language. Through the tools that her blindness had forced her to develop. Sound. Vibration. Temperature. The invisible, constant data stream that her Echolocation and her enhanced senses provided.","She couldn’t see his face.","But she could read him better than anyone else in the house.","Dexter’s expression softened.","\"Then rely on me,\" he said.","The words were simple. Three words. Subject, verb, object. The most basic sentence structure in the English language.","But they carried weight.","Not the weight of a promise. Not the weight of an obligation. The weight of an offering. A man opening a door and standing aside, making room for someone to enter if they chose to.","Selene’s smile disappeared.","She became completely still. Not the stillness of cultivation. The stillness of a person who had just heard something that required recalibration. Something that didn’t fit into the existing framework of her understanding and needed to be processed before she could respond.","For several seconds, neither of them spoke.","The room was quiet. The mana hummed. The Pure-Air Fragrance Artifact released its gentle, clean scent into the air. The moonlight, filtered through the window, cast pale silver patterns on the floor.","Then Selene lowered her head slightly.","\"Okay,\" she said.","Her voice was so soft that Dexter almost didn’t hear it. The word existed on the threshold of audibility, barely disturbing the air, more felt than heard.","But he heard it.","He smiled.","\"Good.\"","The room became quiet once again. The cultivation resumed. The mana flowed. The warmth spread."]},{"number":221,"title":"Chapter 221 | Where Are You Going?","paragraphs":["The two of them stayed together through the night.","Not speaking nor moving, just existing in the same space, shoulder to shoulder, warmth flowing into cold.","Dexter had stayed awake through all of it.","He had felt the weight of her head settling against him. Felt her arms, which had been resting on her knees, slowly unfold and find his waist and felt as her fingers curl into the fabric of his shirt, gripping it loosely, the way a child grips a blanket in sleep.","He didn’t move.","For the second night in a row, he sat perfectly still for hours, his body stiff and his legs numb and his mana reserves slowly depleting from the sustained output of the Abyssal Flame.","Morning came slowly and Dexter’s eyes snapped open.","The first thing he registered was weight, a warm, solid weight pressed against his chest and wrapped around his waist. He looked down.","Selene was sleeping on him.","Her head rested against his chest, just below his collarbone, her silver-white hair spilling across his shirt in a cascade of moonlight-colored silk.","Her arms were wrapped around his waist, both of them, her fingers interlaced at the small of his back and her breathing was slow.","The Eternal Winter Ice, which typically made her sleep restless and broken, had been suppressed throughout the night by the steady warmth of his Heavenly Flame, and the result was the another peaceful sleep.","A faint, barely audible sound escaped within her lips. She wasn’t snoring but it sounded like a cat’s purr.","Dexter looked down at her sleeping face and she was extremely beautiful to him. If a man was to wake up to such beauty, then they are lucky for a hundred lifetimes.","\"Cute,\" he muttered uncontrollably before he could stop himself.","So not to startle her awake, he wanted to turn off the alarm for today and also chevked the time.","4:30 AM.","He needed to start cooking.","One hundred portions of Grade One Enchanted Meal. That was the order Tessa had placed yesterday.","Which meant he needs to start cooking them soon.","Dexter began the careful, painstaking process of extracting himself from Selene’s embrace without waking her.","His withdrew his arms first and then shifted his torso. He leaned forward slowly, creating space between his chest and her head. This gave her room to settle onto the pillow rather than onto the empty space.","Suddenly, Selene’s arms tightened making Dexter freeze.","’ This girl.’","He chuckled as her face pressed even harder against his chest and a small sound of protest.","\"Mmm~\"","Dexter held still and waited for her grip to stabilize. Then patiently, he extracted his other arm and his body. A process which took 5 minutes.","Eventually, he was free as he slid off the bed.","He turned back to the bed. Selene had settled into the space he had vacated, her face now pressed into his pillow instead of his chest. Her arms, finding nothing to hold, had curled around the pillow he had used as backrest and were gripping it.","Dexter reached for the duvet at the foot of the bed, tucking the edges around her shoulders.","She looked very peaceful with a tiny smile at the corner of her lips.","Dexter watched her for a moment, then inhaled deeply to calm his rising self and he turned to leave.","Suddenly-","\"Tap...\"","A hand gripped his arm. Dexter stopped and looked back.","Selene’s hand had wrapped around his wrist.","Her eyes were half open as through barely conscious.","\"Where... are you going?\" she murmured in a sluggish and groggy voice.","Dexter looked at her and smiled as he realized she was sleep talking.","He bent down beside her and his face came close to hers. Then gently, he reached out and started to stroke her hair. Running his fingers through the cool, silky strands, pushing them back from her face, smoothing them against the pillow.","\"Sleep,\" he whispered.","Selene’s eyes, which had been half open fluttered and then she eventually slept.","Her grip on his arm loosened as her fingers relaxed and her hand slipped away, falling back onto the mattress beside her face, the fingers curling slightly inward as they released their hold.","She was asleep again.","Dexter straightened up. He watched her for one more moment. Then he turned and left the room, closing the door behind him with a soft click.","--","He walked to the kitchen and began.","The process of making one hundred portions of Grade One Enchanted Meal was, by now, a familiar routine.","He started the rice first. While the rice cooked, he prepped the vegetables.","The Arcane Nutrition Insight guided his combinations.","He cooked through the early morning hours. The kitchen filled with the familiar, comforting aromas of seasoned rice and seared chicken. The pots bubbled. The oil sizzled. The knife board rattled with the rhythmic percussion of chopping.","By 5:30 AM, the first fifty portions were done. Packed. Sealed. Stacked.","By 6:30 AM, the second fifty were finished.","Dexter placed them all in his spatial storage, organized and counted, and turned his attention to the girls’ breakfast.","This was different.","For the girls, he didn’t hold back.","He pulled out the ingredients that no amount of money could buy at a market. Diamond Rice, Transcendent-Class beast meat, Star Essence Serum, Millennium Blood Ginseng, Void Spirit Lotus, etc.","The Type-II Spirit Cooking Pot came out as the heavenly Flame ignited. His Great Grandmaster Foodsmith techniques activated fully.","[Ding! Congratulations! You have successfully created Celestial Phoenix Nectar Bowl (Grade 5)]","[Effect: Accelerates meridian repair by 40%. Stimulates nerve regeneration. Boosts mana regeneration for 8 hours. Induces deep cellular healing. Strengthens bloodline integration. Increases cultivation speed by 300% for 6 hours.]","The Transcendent-Class meat had pushed the meal two grades higher than the Celestial Dawn Nectar Bowl from two days ago. The effects were extraordinary. Targeted. Designed specifically for the girls’ conditions.","Dexter plated four bowls. The food glowed as thin wisps of steam rose in spirals that seemed to form patterns, shapes that might have been characters from a language older than civilization.","He carried the bowls to the dining table. Set them down. Then turned back toward the kitchen to wash the pots.","And saw Lyra.","She was standing at the edge of the kitchen doorway. Her dark hair was wet, freshly washed, hanging in damp strands that dripped onto the shoulders of her clean shirt. Her AI glasses sat on her nose. Her dark eyes were fixed on the food with the particular, luminous intensity that Dexter had come to recognize as her default setting.","A small line of drool hung from the corner of her mouth.","Dexter shook his head.","\"Good morning, Lyra.\"","Lyra blinked. Her eyes, which had been locked on the glowing bowls of Grade Five food, slowly moved to his face. The drool remained. She didn’t seem to be aware of it.","She had just bathed. Her hair was wet. Droplets of water clung to her jaw and ran down her neck, disappearing beneath the collar of her shirt. The scent of soap mixed with the aroma of the food, creating a combination that was simultaneously domestic and appetizing.","Dexter walked toward her. He raised his hand.","Lyra saw the hand coming. Her eyes tracked it. She could have moved, the old Lyra would have, but she didn’t.","Dexter’s hand found her head. His fingers sank into her wet hair and he rubbed gently, his palm moving across her scalp, his fingers spreading the moisture evenly through the strands."]},{"number":222,"title":"Chapter 222 | What Bad Things Did You Do To Selene","paragraphs":["Lyra’s eyes widened slightly but then it softened as she leaned into his hand, almost imperceptibly, the way a cat leans into a stroke.","Dexter smiled.","\"Hope you slept well,\" he said as he transmitted the thought telepathically and she nodded, her melodious voice sounded in his mind.","\"I slept well.\"","Dexter nodded. \"Good. Sit down, I’ll plate your food.\"","He walked to the dining table and Lyra followed, her bare feet padding softly on the floor behind him as she sat in her usual chair.","Lyra’s spoon was in her hand before the bowl even touched the table.","’Foodie.’","Dexter chuckled at the foodie and was about to begin serving his own portion when Lyra’s voice entered his mind.","\" What’s Aurelyx?\"","Dexter’s body froze. But that reaction lasted less than half a second before he blinked his eyes and spoke.","\"Where did you get that name?\"","Lyra shrugged as she picked up her spoon and aimed it at the bowl with the eager, expectant gaze.","\"When you saw me just now, you muttered the name Aurelyx in your mind.\" She said casually.","Dexter stared at her.","’I muttered it?’","The moment he had turned around and seen Lyra standing at the doorway with wet hair and drool on her chin. The thought that had crossed his mind in that instant.","Aurelyx.","He had thought the name externally on refelx. Moreover, he was a bit sleep deprived too which was why Lyra had been able to pick it up.","Dexter shrugged, keeping his expression carefully neutral.","\"It’s just a random name that popped into my head.\"","Lyra looked at his face for a moment, she was about to follow up with another question when Dexter placed the bowl of Grade 5 Celestial Phoenix Nectar Bowl directly in front of her.","The aroma hit her and the question she was about to ask was instantly forgotten.","Her eyes widened as her nostrils flared and the spoon, which had been hovering in the air, descended toward the bowl with lightning speed as she ate.","Dexter watched her take the first bite as her eyes closed and her expression shifted from eager to stunned to blissful.","He sighed in relief.","At that moment, Mira arrived.","Her Spectral Arms pushed her through the hallway and into the dining room and she parked herself at the table, her crimson eyes scanning the food as her nose inhaled deeply the scent.","\"Good morning.\"","She said unconsciously as she started eating her meal.","Dexter blinked his eyes and replied. \"Morning.\"","Mira didn’t seem to hear as she descended on the food too.","Dexter was about to start eating when he noticed something, Selene wasn’t here.","Dexter immediately stood up and left the dining room and walked to the girls’ bedroom.","Selene should have finished bathing by now. She should have emerged, found her way to the dining table, and begun eating as that was the routine.","But whe he checked the girls bedroom, it was empty.","Dexter stood in the doorway and blinked.","\"Don’t tell me she’s still in my room.\"","He walked across the hall, opened his bedroom door.","Selene was still in his bed.","She hadn’t moved and was exactly where he had left her, curled up beneath the duvet he had draped over her, her silver-white hair spread across his pillow, her arms wrapped around it too as she slept soundly.","Dexter stood in the doorway and stared.","Then he smiled softly. He could wake her but it would be useless.","He watched her for a moment, then he turned and walked back to the dining room.","---","Mira’s eyes tracked him as he returned.","Her eyes stared at the doorway, then stared at Dexter, then at the doorway again, then at Dexter.","She didn’t say anything as she continued eating for a few minutes. Suddenly she spoke.","\"What did you do to Selene?\"","The question landed on the table like a grenade as Dexter’s spoon froze halfway to his mouth.","Lyra also froze and her dark eyes, which had been exclusively focused on her bowl, widened and shifted to Dexter’s face.","The food had been so engrossing that Lyra had not noticed Selene’s absence until Mira spoke.","Dexter’s expression changed slightly but then, he dropped his spoke and then glared at Mira.","\"What do you mean by what did I do to Selene?\"","Mira’s lips curled upward into a smirk.","\"You know exactly what I mean.\"","Dexter pursed his lips.. \"You’re acting as if I’m some kind of villain.\"","\"Of course you’re not a villain,\" Mira said in a honey sweet tone. \"I’m pretty sure you want to do bad things, though.\"","Lyra’s ears turned pink and red at the same time !","Mira continued, completely unfazed by the destruction she was inflicting on Lyra’s composure.","\"Who knows what you’ve done to Selene? Maybe she’s tired from all the bad things you did to her.\"","Dexter stared at her.","\"I woke up this morning,\" Mira continued. \"and Selene was not in the bedroom. She was not in the living room and she was not in the backyard. Which means she was either in the bathroom or in your bed.\"","She paused.","\"She wasn’t in the bathroom, which means She was sleeping on your bed.\"","\"Which means you definitely did bad things to her. So what bad things did you do to Selene?\"","Dexter sat in his chair and stared at the woman in the wheelchair.","He wanted to argue but he knew it would be of no use.","So Dexter took a different approach.","He smiled and spoke.","\"Are you jealous? Do you also want me to do bad things to you?\"","Mira’s expression froze and her smirk vanished as she was stunned by dexters words.","Her neck turned red and she stuttered.","\"Pervert,\" she spat. \"I knew it. Pervert.\"","Dexter chuckled.","\"Selene wasn’t comfortable sleeping with her illness. Her Eternal Winter Ice was acting up. So she came to my room and we cultivated together. My Heavenly Flame suppressed the cold. She fell asleep. That’s all.\"","Mira glared at him. Suspiciously.","Dexter met her gaze without flinching.","Eventually, Mira sniffed and then returned to her food."]},{"number":223,"title":"Chapter 223 | The Festival","paragraphs":["The subject was closed.","Lyra exhaled slowly. The pink in her ears faded gradually, returning to a color that suggested her cardiovascular system had resumed normal operations. She picked up her spoon and dove back into her bowl with the relieved urgency of someone who had been caught in someone else’s crossfire and was grateful to still be alive.","---","They ate. The Grade Five meal was consumed in its entirety by all four of them. Mira cleaned her bowl. Lyra ate four portions. Dexter ate one. The remaining portions went into the refrigerator for later.","As the meal wound down, Dexter set his spoon down and looked at the three women.","\"The festival is tomorrow,\" he said. \"Are we all ready?\"","Mira froze.","Her spoon, which had been en route to her mouth via her Spectral Arm, stopped in the air. Her crimson eyes, which had been focused on her bowl, shifted to Dexter’s face. A brief, flickering expression crossed her features. Something that might have been hesitation. Or uncertainty. Or the particular discomfort of a woman who had agreed to something days ago and was now reconsidering.","Lyra also paused. But only for a moment. The word \"festival\" registered, and with it the memory of Dexter’s earlier description. A neighborhood gathering. A picnic. Food. People. The outside world.","She resumed eating. The festival was tomorrow. That was a problem for tomorrow-Lyra.","Dexter noticed Mira’s reaction.","He noticed the way her jaw had tightened. The way her Spectral Arm had hesitated mid-motion. The way her crimson eyes had flickered with something that looked uncomfortably like doubt.","\"We’re not in the mood to go anymore?\" Dexter asked. The question was directed at Mira specifically. His eyes were on her face, reading the micro-expressions that she was trying and failing to suppress.","Mira shrugged. The shrug was too casual. Too deliberate. The shrug of someone who was trying to appear indifferent while feeling something very different. \"Anything you want.\"","Dexter inhaled slowly through his nose. Exhaled through his mouth. Then glared at her.","\"You were the main reason we wanted to go to this festival in the first place,\" he said. \"You were the one who said you wanted to go outside. You were the one who said you wanted to see the outside world. And now you’re telling me you’re not in the mood?\"","Mira’s eyes flashed. \"I didn’t say I don’t want to go. I didn’t say anything at all.\"","Dexter glared at her. \"Your body language says otherwise. And if you don’t feel like going, that’s fine. But it’s three against one now. You don’t have a choice in the matter.\"","Mira glared back.","The two of them sat at the dining table, locked in a staring contest that carried the weight of three weeks of accumulated domestic tension, mutual stubbornness, and the particular, complicated dynamic of two people who cared about each other but would rather die than admit it directly.","Mira broke first.","Not by looking away. By shoving an enormous spoonful of rice into her mouth, causing her cheeks to bulge outward like a chipmunk hoarding for winter. She chewed. Slowly. Aggressively. While maintaining eye contact with Dexter the entire time.","The effect was simultaneously menacing and adorable.","Dexter held her gaze. He didn’t blink. He didn’t smile. He simply sat there and matched her stare with his own, the two of them locked in a battle of wills that had no stakes and no resolution and was being conducted over a table of empty bowls while one of them chewed with her mouth full and her Spectral Arms crossed behind her back in a posture of absolute defiance.","Lyra was not watching.","Lyra was eating.","Her focus was so completely, so thoroughly, so exclusively devoted to the Grade Five meal in front of her that the nuclear-level domestic dispute happening across the table was registering as background noise. She didn’t notice the staring contest. She didn’t notice the tension. She didn’t notice anything except the complex, layered flavors of Transcendent-Class beast meat and Diamond Rice dissolving on her tongue.","Dexter eventually broke the stare. Not because he lost. Because there was no winning a staring contest with a woman who was chewing angrily, and he had deliveries to make.","---","After breakfast, Dexter stood up and collected the plates.","\"I need to run and deliver the meals to the bakery,\" he said. \"I’ll be back in twenty minutes.\"","Lyra looked up from her bowl. She smiled and waved from the couch, her dark eyes warm behind her AI glasses. The telepathic connection carried her voice into his mind.","\"Bye.\"","Dexter smiled and nodded at her.","He walked to where Mira was sitting. She had been wheeled to the living room by her Spectral Arms and was now positioned by the window. Her usual spot. Her crimson eyes were closed. Her expression was neutral. Carefully, deliberately neutral.","\"I’m leaving,\" Dexter said.","He didn’t look at her. He said it to the air beside her, his voice directed at the general vicinity of her wheelchair rather than at her face. The verbal equivalent of a note left on a counter.","Mira snorted. A small, sharp, carefully modulated snort.","\"Farewell.\"","The word was clipped. Final. Delivered with the precise, measured politeness of a woman who was not going to say anything more than the absolute minimum required by basic social convention.","Dexter snorted back. A small, sharp, equally modulated snort.","He walked to the front door. Opened it. Stepped outside. Closed it behind him.","The morning air was cool. Fresh. The street was quiet. The bakery was a five-minute walk. He didn’t need the SUV. The containers were in his spatial storage. He could carry them without effort.","He walked.","The neighborhood was beginning to stir. A few early risers were out on their porches, drinking coffee, reading tablets. A jogger passed him on the sidewalk, nodding politely. Somewhere down the street, a dog barked twice and fell silent.","Dexter walked and thought.","He thought about the festival tomorrow, about taking three women to a public gathering in a neighborhood where everyone knew their faces and their stories."]},{"number":224,"title":"Chapter 224 | Bloodline Awakening...?","paragraphs":["Dexter exited the house and walked toward the bakery.","The morning was still early and the air was cool, carrying the faint scent of freshly baked bread that had been drifting from the bakery as Dexter neared there.","Just like yesterday, the place was already packed, but the moment Tessa spotted Dexter through the entrance, her eyes lit up.","She was behind the counter, wearing her white apron over her blue dress. Her curly red hair was tied back with a ribbon that was already coming loose, strands escaping in every direction. Flour dusted a but of her nose, she had probably been baking since four.","She headed toward him immediately, practically skipping the entire way. The customers in her path parted without complaint. M","\"Good morning!\" she greeted, arriving in front of him with a smile that could have powered the city’s grid. \"You’re quite early today.\"","Dexter shrugged. \"Yeah. I woke up early to prepare the orders.\"","He lifted the two bags in his hands. Each one contained fifty sealed containers of Grade One Comfort Chicken Rice.","Tessa’s eyes moved to the bags.","\"Come over here,\" she said, gesturing toward the back of the bakery, leading him through the narrow hallway behind the counter, into the small storage room where the thermal shelves waited.","Dexter followed.","Tessa pointed toward the empty section of shelf that had been cleared for his meals. \"Just put them here. I’ll sell them one by one today.\"","Dexter began stacking the one hundred containers neatly.","He stepped back.","\"If that’s all, I’ll take my leave,\" he said, turning toward the exit.","\"Wait!\"","Dexter paused and turned back. Tessa was standing in the doorway of the storage room, her hands clasped behind her back.","\"You’re coming to the festival tomorrow, right?\"","Dexter raised an eyebrow. \"I already told you I was coming, didn’t I?\"","Tessa shrugged casually.","\"You might have changed your mind. I’m just making sure you haven’t.\"","She smiled.","Dexter couldn’t help smiling back.","\"No, I haven’t changed my mind. Or do you want me to change it?\"","Tessa’s eyes widened and her head shook so rapidly that her curly hair bounced in every direction simultaneously.","\"No, no, no! Of course not!\"","Dexter chuckled.","\"All right. If there’s nothing else, I really have to get going.\"","His expression became slightly more serious.","’ Selene still hasn’t woken up.’","He wanted to be there when she did and she hadn’t eaten yet. The Grade Five meal was waiting in the refrigerator, but he wanted to feed her immediately she woke up.","He didn’t want her waking up and finding him gone. So he was in no mood to waste time.","\"If there’s nothing else, I’ll head back.\"","Tessa hesitated.","Suddenly, her hand reached out and caught his sleeve.","Dexter looked at her with a puzzled look.","\"Is something the matter?\"","Tessa wanted to speak but then she hesitated again. After a while, she eventually spoke.","\"The food you gave me...\"","Dexter stopped as he looked at her hand on his sleeve. Then at her face.","\"What about it?\"","Tessa looked at him curiously.","\"The food you gave me that time. Did it have any special effects?\"","Dexter blinked.","\"Yeah, all the meals I gave you have special effect.\"","Tessa immediately shook her head as her curly hair bounced as she spoke in a serious voice. \"Now these ones. I meant the one you gave me to eat when I came to your home through the fence.\"","’ The food I gave her.’","He rewound through his memory. The first meal he had ever given Tessa. Weeks ago. Before the bakery partnership.","It had been a small portion and was the remains of his wives bloodline meals","Those ingredients carried bloodline-awakening effects as a passive property. He hadn’t thought about it affecting Tessa.","And Tessa had eaten it.","Dexter studied her carefully.","’ Did she awaken a bloodline?’","He looked her up and down. His Arcane Nutrition Insight, which provided passive information about ingredients and their effects, didn’t extend to reading other people’s cultivation status. He couldn’t detect bloodline activation through observation alone.","But he could look for signs.","Tessa’s skin was clear. Healthy. The complexion of a 17 year old who spent her days in a bakery and her evenings in a garden. Nothing unusual there.","Her energy was the same as always.","But...","There was something in her eyes. A faint, barely perceptible brightness that hadn’t been there before.","Dexter weighed his response carefully.","\"Yeah,\" he said. \"It contained some special effects.\"","Tessa’s expression became more attentive. She leaned forward slightly. The hand on his sleeve tightened.","Dexter continued. \"There were recovery effects. A slight boost to cultivation. An improvement to one’s physique.\"","He paused.","\"It also contained an effect capable of awakening a bloodline, but the amount you ate was very small.\"","He narrowed his eyes.","\"Did something happen to you?\"","The question was direct.","Tessa stared at him suspiciously for a moment.","Then she slowly shook her head.","\"No. Nothing happened.\"","She smiled. The smile was light. Casual. Perfectly calibrated to convey that everything was fine and there was absolutely no reason for concern.","\"I just wanted to make sure.\"","Dexter continued looking at her for several seconds.","Something about her answer felt wrong.","Tessa was a lot of things. She was energetic. She was entrepreneurial. She was perceptive. She was a better businesswoman at 17 than most adults were at forty.","But she was not a good liar.","Dexter considered pressing.","But he didn’t. Because it wasn’t his business anyways.","...","On his way back from the bakery, Dexter’s phone rang.","He checked the caller ID while walking. The name on the screen made him pause mid-stride.","Rachel.","He frowned slightly and his feelings was quite complicated about picking up the call.","He eventually answered.","\"Hey, Dexter.\"","Rachel’s voice came through the speaker with the warm, polished cadence that he remembered from their first meeting at the hotel bar.","\"It’s been a while,\" she said."]},{"number":225,"title":"Chapter 225 | The Call...","paragraphs":["Dexter blinked. \"Hey, Rachel. It hasn’t been all that long, actually.\"","He could feel Rachel’s smile through the phone as she spoke.","\"Which means you haven’t been thinking about me all this time. That is really sad.\"","Dexter didn’t respond to that. He had learned, through several interactions with Rachel, that engaging with her flirtatious comments was like feeding a stray cat.","\"I’ve been really busy,\" he said instead.","Rachel went silent for a moment.","\"How are your wives doing?\" she asked sincerely. \"I hope they are doing all right and hope they are healing quite nicely.\"","\"They are doing quite fine, thank you,\" Dexter responded.","He paused and the phone was silent. Rachel was waiting.","Dexter sighed.","\"What about you? Hope you’re doing all right.\"","He could feel Rachel’s excitement through the phone.","\"Yes, I am doing quite all right. Thank you for asking.\"","Dexter shrugged, even though she couldn’t see it. \"Yeah, anytime.\"","Then Rachel spoke again.","\"We should try to get together sometime. Maybe for breakfast. Lunch. Dinner or something.\"","Dexter frowned slightly but he didn’t respond immediately.","Rachel sensed his hesitation. She immediately added, \"You know, as friends. Just to catch up with each other. Maybe take a break from other stuff.\"","The word \"friends\" was emphasized.","\"I’m always busy,\" Dexter said. \"I don’t have much time for taking breaks and stuff.\"","Rachel remained silent for a while. The silence lasted long enough for Dexter to hear the faint sound of traffic on her end. She was outsid, walking or maybe in her car.","\"It’s all right,\" she said. \"I understand. Maybe another time then.\"","Dexter didn’t speak and the conversation felt like it was winding down.","Then Rachel said, \"Oh, right, before I forget. What do you know about Harvest Homes?\"","Dexter’s eyes flashed coldly.","\"What happened?\" he asked. \"Why do you ask?\"","\"I read a report down here,\" Rachel said. \"About a sudden incident at Harvest Homes. A breakout. An altercation. And your name was also in that report. So I had to ask.\"","Dexter’s jaw tightened.","’ My name was on the report?’","\"How?\" he asked. \"Who filed it?\"","\"Hero Association internal intelligence,\" Rachel replied. \"They monitor significant incidents involving registered heroes. The Harvest Homes event flagged automatically because of the scale of the damage and the cultivation levels involved.\"","She paused.","\"Your name was redacted, though. It wasn’t quite clear. Your involvement wasn’t explicitly stated. But you were one of the people connected to the incident.\"","Dexter thought about it then shook his head.","\"It’s nothing,\" he said. \"I was just nearby Harvest Homes when that happened. Coincidence.\"","Rachel didn’t respond immediately. The silence on her end was evaluative.","\"All right,\" she said. The tone was neutral. Neither believing nor disbelieving.","Then she continued.","\"Oh, before I forget. Aurora.\"","Dexter blinked. \"What about Aurora?\"","\"I heard you met with her. At the restaurant. Yesterday.\"","\"Yeah,\" Dexter said. \"She was there. At the restaurant. When I met with the squad.\"","\"Aurora told me,\" Rachel said. \"She told me you two are quite connected. Are you?\"","Dexter frowned. \"What do you mean, connected? She approached me after the meeting. She had a proposition. That’s all.\"","Rachel’s voice carried a trace of amusement. \"A proposition? That sounds interesting. What kind of proposition?\"","\"Business,\" Dexter said flatly. \"Nothing else.\"","\"Mm-hmm,\" Rachel said. The sound was noncommittal. The verbal equivalent of a raised eyebrow.","Then he continued. \"She told me you two are quite connected. She said you know each other now. Are you best friends? Or something?\"","\"No,\" Rachel said, answering her own question before Dexter could. \"We are not family. And neither are we friends.\"","Dexter blinked. He was confused. If they weren’t family and they weren’t friends, what else could they be? Colleagues? Acquaintances? Professional contacts?","Then he could feel Rachel smirking through the phone.","\"We were involved,\" she said.","Dexter’s stride stopped.","He was standing on the sidewalk, three houses from his bungalow, his phone pressed against his ear, his brain processing two words that had just rearranged his understanding of two women he knew.","\"Involved?\" he repeated.","\"With each other,\" Rachel clarified. \"For a while. Just casually. Nothing too serious.\"","She paused.","\"She’s more busy now. And I also like someone else. So the fling had to eventually cut off.\"","Dexter was stunned.","Rachel. Who had kissed him at the hotel bar and Aurora, the S-Rank hero of this generation.","These two women had been involved with each other.","Romantically and casually too!","\"Fling?\" Dexter said. The word came out as a question, but it wasn’t really a question. It was a verbal placeholder. A sound produced by a brain that needed a few more seconds to process.","\"Yeah,\" Rachel confirmed. Her voice was relaxed as she spoke.","\"I’m not just straight, you know?,\" she said. \"I am also bi.\"","Dexter felt something spark in his mind as his body trembled slightly.","Rachel was bisexual, which meant she was attracted to both men and women.","\"Yeah, I’m also bi. That means I can be with a man or a woman. And I’m also comfortable sharing my man...\"","The sentence trailed off deliberately and Dexter’s brain completed the sentence.","His brain completed it in multiple ways. Several of which were extremely inappropriate. All of which were immediately suppressed by the disciplined, practiced, iron-fisted mental filter that he had spent twenty years developing in the Ashford estate!","But the spark remained.","The implication hung in the air between the phone and his ear. Rachel was comfortable sharing. Sharing. A word that, in the context she had established, carried a very specific, very clear, very loaded meaning.","Dexter swallowed.","\"Rachel,\" he said. His voice was controlled. Steady. The voice of a man who was absolutely not going to engage with the implication. \"Is there a specific reason you’re telling me this?\"","\"Because I wanted to be honest with you,\" Rachel said. Her tone had shifted. The teasing edge was still there, but beneath it was something more genuine. More sincere. \"I didn’t want you to find out from someone else and think I was hiding something.\"","She paused."]},{"number":226,"title":"Chapter 226 | Suspicious Individuals","paragraphs":["\"Aurora and I were involved. It’s over now. But we still talk and share information. Which is how she knew about you, and which is how I know she met with you.\"","Another pause.","\"I like you, Dexter. I’ve made that pretty clear. I’m not going to pretend I don’t. But I also respect that you have three wives and that your situation is complicated. I’m not trying to insert myself into your household.\"","Her voice softened.","\"I just want you to know that if you ever need anything, whether it’s a friend, a contact, a business partner, or... something more. I’m available. In whatever capacity you need me.\"","Dexter stood on the sidewalk. Even after what she said,he remained silent for a while and then spoke.","\"I’ll keep that in mind,\" he said.","Rachel laughed softly. \"That’s all I ask.\"","\"Okay,\" she said. \"I called mainly cause I wasworried when I saw your name along with the file on Harvest Homes. That’s why I called.\"","\"Thank you for being worried,\" Dexter said. \"I’ll talk to you later, yeah?\"","\"Okay, talk to you later.\" Rachel paused. \"And don’t forget. You promised me we’d go out sometime.\"","Dexter immediately replied. \"I didn’t promise you anything. But if I have time, I’ll let you know.\"","Rachel seemed to smile happily at that.","\"Bye, Dexter.\"","\"Bye.\"","The call ended.","Dexter pocketed his phone and resumed walking. His mind was still processing the conversation. Rachel was bisexual and had been involved with Aurora.","’She’s truly a temptress.’","He could even hear other people screaming ’pass the remote.’ In his mind.","He shook his head and continued to move. He was halfway down the block when he saw them.","Two figures walked past him, heading in opposite directions towards the bakery.","They were dressed completely in black. Black shirts. Black pants. Black boots. Black hoods pulled up over their heads, obscuring their faces.","Dexter frowned as they passed.","His Enhanced Hearing, always partially active, registered their heartbeats as they walked by and his mana affinity immediately recognized their realms.","Peak Superhuman Realm.","Both of them.","Dexter’s frown deepened. He turned his head slightly, tracking their movement as they continued past him without acknowledgment. They didn’t look at him, glance in his direction, or register his existence. They simply walked, their hoods low, their pace unhurried, their trajectory aimed precisely at the bakery ahead.","’What are two Peak Superhuman Realm cultivators doing in this neighborhood?’","This was not the mid-district. This was not the commercial center. This was the outer ring, where families lived on modest incomes and the most dangerous thing on the street was the occasional stray dog.","Peak Superhuman Realm cultivators did not wander through outer-ring neighborhoods without a reason. They were too valuable. Too well-employed. Too busy taking high-paying dungeon contracts and Association missions to waste time walking through streets where the most exciting event of the day was the bakery opening at dawn.","’But the bakery just started selling Enchanted Meals. Maybe they came to buy.’","The thought was reasonable. His meals had been selling well. The reputation was spreading. Word of mouth in a city like Stargate City traveled fast, especially when the product was genuinely effective. Peak Superhuman Realm cultivators might have heard about the Grade One meals and come to try them.","’That’s probably it. Nothing suspicious. Just customers.’","Dexter smiled at his own paranoia.","’My meals are going viral. Two Peak Superhuman Realm cultivators came to buy my food. That’s nice.’","He was about to continue home when his Enhanced Hearing caught something.","A scream.","Short. Sharp. Cut off almost as soon as it began. Not the scream of a crowd or a performance or a child playing. The scream of a single voice. Female. Young. Coming from the direction of the bakery.","Dexter’s expression changed.","His body moved before his brain finished processing. The decision to act was not conscious. It was reflexive. The particular, instant, full-body response of a man who had spent weeks fighting monsters and assassins and whose nervous system had been rewired to treat sudden sounds as immediate threats.","He flashed toward the bakery.","Not walked. Not jogged. Flashed. Using a suppressed version of Flame Burst Step that was calibrated for short-distance, civilian-adjacent movement. Fast enough to cover two blocks in seconds. Slow enough to avoid creating a sonic boom that would shatter every window on the street.","He reached the bakery in under ten seconds.","The front of the shop was still crowded. Customers milled around the display cases. The staff behind the counter were serving. Everything looked normal. Everything sounded normal. The ambient noise of a busy bakery in the middle of its morning rush.","But Tessa was not behind the counter.","Dexter’s eyes swept the room. Left. Right. Behind the pastry display. Near the ovens. In the hallway.","No Tessa.","The staff at the counter noticed him. They recognized him. He had been here twice before. They knew he was connected to the owner. They paid him no special attention as he moved through the shop with the focused, purposeful stride of a man who knew exactly where he was going.","He entered the narrow hallway. Passed the ovens. Passed the flour-dusted prep stations. Reached the storage room.","Empty.","The thermal shelves were there. His meals were there. But Tessa was not.","Dexter’s hearing expanded. He pushed the range outward, filtering through the layers of ambient sound. The hum of the refrigerators. The click of the ovens. The murmur of customers in the front. The traffic outside.","And beneath all of it, coming from further back. From behind the bakery. From the backyard.","Movement. Bodies. The sounds of physical contact. The particular, dense, heavy sounds of a fight.","Dexter didn’t hesitate.","He burst through the back door.","The backyard of the bakery was a small, enclosed space. A concrete patio. A few empty crates. A dumpster. A clothesline where aprons were hung to dry. Not large. Not designed for combat. The kind of space where a baker stepped out for fresh air between batches."]},{"number":227,"title":"Chapter 227 | Dangerous Tessa","paragraphs":["Dexter burst through the door and stopped.","The scene that greeted him was not what he expected.","Two bodies lay on the concrete.","Both of them were the figures in black. The two Peak Superhuman Realm cultivators who had walked past him on the street moments ago. They were on the ground. Motionless. One was face down. The other was on his back, eyes open, staring at the sky with the blank, unfocused gaze of a person whose consciousness had been violently and comprehensively removed.","Their hoods had fallen back, revealing two faces that Dexter didn’t recognize. Both male too and they were unconscious!","And standing over them, crouched between the two fallen bodies, one hand on the first man’s chest and the other rummaging through the second man’s pockets, was Tessa.","She was searching them calmly as her fingers moved through the man’s pockets with experience and excitement.","The back door slammed against the wall as Dexter burst through.","Tessa looked up.","Her green eyes met his.","\"Oh. Dexter. Hi.\" She blinked. \"You’re still here? I thought you’d left already.\"","Dexter stood in the doorway and his eyes moved from Tessa to the two unconscious bodies on the ground.","He walked forward slowly, clearly stunne by what he was seeing. It wasn’t a while before the question registered in his mind.","\"No,\" Dexter said. \"I was about to leave when I saw the two suspicious people coming into your bakery. I was worried.\"","He looked at the bodies again.","\"But it seems I was worried for nothing. Who are these guys?\"","Tessa shrugged. The gesture was casual. Easy. The shrug of a sixteen-year-old girl who had been asked about something she considered trivial.","\"I have no idea. They probably came to rob the store. Which is why they are here. So I had to retaliate.\"","Dexter stared at her.","Then he stared at the bodies.","Then he stared at her again.","\"Tessa. These two are Peak Superhuman Realm.\"","\"I know.\"","\"Peak Superhuman Realm cultivators don’t rob ordinary bakeries.\"","Tessa blinked. Her green eyes widened. The expression was cute. Innocent. The particular, artless innocence of a girl who had been presented with a logical objection and was choosing to address it with an answer that was technically plausible but practically absurd.","\"Maybe they really needed money desperately,\" she said. \"You know. Addicts. Addicts do stupid things just to get a fix.\"","Dexter looked at her.","He looked at the two bodies on the ground. Both were well-built. Well-fed. Well-equipped. Their clothing was high-quality. Their boots were reinforced. Neither showed signs of malnourishment, desperation, or the physical deterioration that accompanied substance addiction.","These were not addicts.","These were professionals.","And they had been taken down by a sixteen-year-old girl in an apron.","\"Tessa,\" Dexter said carefully. \"You can defeat Peak Superhuman Realm cultivators?\"","In his mind, the calculations were running.","Two Peak Superhuman Realm cultivators. If Dexter fought them simultaneously, going all out, using his bloodline, his techniques, his Type-5 weapon, he would win. But it would take time. At least a minute.","But Tessa had dealt with both of them in under thirty seconds. Less. From the time he had heard the scream to the time he had burst through the back door, approximately fifteen seconds had elapsed.","Fifteen seconds.","For a 17-year-old girl who was supposedly an ordinary baker’s daughter.","’ Who exactly is this girl?’","Tessa looked at him, her green eyes were bright. Carrying that same, enigmatic quality that he had noticed the first day they met. The quality that said ’I am more than I appear’ without actually saying it.","\"Aw, Dexter.\" She tilted her head. \"Were you really worried about me? I knew you cared about me.\"","Dexter rolled his eyes.","\"Obviously, I was trying to make sure you weren’t getting kidnapped or something. But obviously I was worried for no reason.\"","He looked at the bodies one more time. Then at Tessa. Then at the bodies.","\"Should we call the cops?\"","Tessa immediately shook her head.","\"No. Me and my dad will handle it.\"","She straightened up from her crouch. Brushed dust from her apron. Adjusted the loose ribbon in her hair. The transition from combatant to baker’s daughter was seamless. Instant. As though the fight had been a minor inconvenience, like spilling flour or dropping a tray, and had already been filed under \"handled\" in her mind.","Then she smiled at Dexter. The warm, bright, dimpled smile that he had come to associate with all things Tessa.","\"Do you want to try some of our pastries? I made a special batch this time. Maybe you can give them to your wives if you don’t want to eat them yourself.\"","Dexter stared at her.","He stared at her for a long time. Long enough that Tessa’s smile began to carry a trace of something beneath its surface. Not discomfort. Not guilt. Just the quiet awareness of being evaluated by someone who was paying very close attention.","’She took down two Peak Superhuman Realm cultivators in fifteen seconds. She’s searching their pockets instead of calling the police. She’s offering me pastries. She’s 17. Her father is a baker. Grandma Lucy can disperse Ultra-Rank auras with a tap of her finger. Her house was untouched during the monster outbreak.’","’Nothing about this neighborhood is what it seems.’","Dexter shook his head.","\"There’s no need for that. I’ll take my leave.\"","He pointed toward the street. Then sighed. The sigh was not from frustration. It was from the particular, accumulated exhaustion of a man who had been discovering secrets all week and had just found another one.","He walked toward the back gate that led to the street. His stride was measured. Unhurried. The stride of a man who was choosing to leave rather than being driven away.","Tessa’s voice followed him.","\"Bye, Dexter!\"","He raised a hand without looking back. \"Take care of yourself.\"","\"I will!\"","Her cheerful voice rang through the backyard, following him as Tessa waved enthusiastically at him.","Dexter reached the street. He paused. Turned back. Looked at the bakery. The facade was the same as always. Warm. Inviting. The smell of fresh bread drifting from the open door. Customers coming and going. The display cases full. The morning rush in full swing.","Everything looked normal.","Everything was not normal.","’Two Peak Superhuman Realm cultivators came to the bakery. They were dealt with by a sixteen-year-old girl in under fifteen seconds. She didn’t call the police. She didn’t seem scared. She didn’t seem surprised. She searched their pockets with the practiced ease of someone who had done it before.’","’And she offered me pastries afterward.’","Dexter shook his head.","He turned and walked home."]},{"number":228,"title":"Chapter 228 | Sorry, I Shouldn’t Have","paragraphs":["Dexter reached his bungalow in two minutes.","He opened the gate, walked up the path, and pushed open the front door.","\"I’m home.\"","The living room greeted him with its usual quiet and the Pure-Air Fragrance Artifact hummed softly on its shelf.","He looked to the left and saw Mira in her wheelchair by the window with her eyes closed. Cultivating. Her crimson hair caught the sunlight and burned like copper wire as her Spectral Arms were folded behind her back, motionless.","The moment he came in, one of her eyes snapped open as she stared at him but the moment she saw him looking at her, she immediately closed it and pretended she hadn’t noticed him.","Dexter laughted quietly. ’Mira...’","He looked toward the living room couch.","Lyra was cross-legged with her eyes closed. The Primordial Beast Egg rested in her lap as she cultivated.","Since she couldn’t hear and her eyes were closed, she had no way of knowing that Dexter had entered the house.","Dexter wanted to extend his thoughts but he chose not to disturb her as she looked really peaceful.","He also noticed, with a pang of guilt, that he hadn’t brought anything for her. Now that he thought about it, he would have accepted the pastries Tessa wanted to give him.","’Next time. I’ll bring pastries next time.’","He shook his head and walked toward the hallway.","The person he kinda wanted to see most at this moment was Selene.","He checked the girls’ room first. Opened the door. Looked inside but there was no one there.","Dexter was a strangely a bit relieved about this.","He closed the door and walked across the hall to his own room.","He opened the door and to bi surprise, Selene was there.","She lay in his bed exactly where he’d left her that morning, sleeping. The duvet he’d draped over her was still there, and her silver-white hair, spread across his pillow in a chaotic tangled cascade, was wrapped around the fabric like a child’s favourite toy.","\"Rustle.\"","She suddenly shifted in her sleep and pulled the duvet higher, covering her shoulders and tucked beneath her chin as she curled into it and slept much like a baby.","Dexter’s lips curled upwards.","He walked to the edge of the bed and looked down at her and she looked like a sleeping angel.","Suddenly, an instinct surged into his mind to reach out and strike her hair.","Without warning, his right arm lifted upward and his fingers spread as he was about to strike her hair!","His fingers were three inches from her head when she turned, he face rotated on the pillow and her eyes fluttered open.","Pale eyes disorientedly opened to the world as her Echolocation talent activated reflexively. A pulse went out. It bounced off the walls, the ceiling, the furniture, and the object hovering three inches from her head.","She saw the arm, Suspended in the air above her hair, in the precise, unmistakable posture of a person who had been about to stroke someone’s head and had been caught in the act.","Selene blinked.","She was still drowsy and her brain was still booting up. But the image, rendered through her Echolocation was clear enough.","She glanced at the arm then Dexter and back at the arm.","Dexter causally retracted his hand like he wasn’t doing anything wrong.","He looked down at her. His expression was neutral as he spoke.","\"You’re awake,\"","Selene blinked again. Her pale eyes, still foggy with sleep, processed the information. His voice. His presence. The arm that had been reaching for her and was now, very casually, resting at his side.","She nodded.","\"Mm-hmm.\"","Dexter smiled. The warm, gentle smile he reserved for her.","\"Good morning. You must be hungry. Should I bring your food here, or do you want to eat at the dining table?\"","Selene blinked.","\"Yeah?\" she said. The word came out as a question. Not because she was asking what he had said. Because she was asking what she wanted. The particular, uncertain \"yeah\" of a person who had just been woken from the best sleep of their life and whose brain was still negotiating the transition between dreams and decisions.","Dexter shrugged. \"I don’t mind. You can eat here if you want.\"","He gestured at the bed. At the warm, comfortable, Dexter-scented bed that she had been sleeping in. The bed that, according to the pillow she had been clutching all night, smelled like him.","Selene was about to respond. About to say something. Maybe yes. Maybe no. Maybe something in between.","Then her brows furrowed.","Her Echolocation pulsed again. Stronger this time. More focused. The pulse swept the room, bouncing off every surface, returning with a three-dimensional map of her surroundings.","The bed was not her bed. The room was not her room. The pillow was not her pillow. The walls were the wrong distance apart. The window was in the wrong position. The door was on the wrong side.","This was Dexter’s room.","The realization hit her with the force of a small, private explosion.","She scrambled out of the bed.","The motion was sudden and quick.","The duvet flew, the pillow slid, her feet hit the floor as she stood beside the bed, her white sleeping gown rumpled and her silver hair in complete disarray, her face flushed a shade of pink that spread from her cheeks to her ears to the visible skin above her collar.","\"Sorry,\" she said.","The word came out fast. Breathy. The apology of a woman who had woken up in her husband’s bed, realized where she was, and was now experiencing the particular, full-body embarrassment that came from knowing she had been sleeping there all night without permission.","\"Sorry. I should have... I didn’t mean to...\"","Dexter scratched the back of his head.","\"It’s all right,\" he said. \"I told you it’s all right. You can stay whenever and for as long as you wish.\""]},{"number":229,"title":"Chapter 229 | Reverse","paragraphs":["Selene shook her head firmly.","\"Even so, its still inappropriate for me to sleep in your bed. And not give you the chance to sleep.\"","Dexter blinked.","\"No, it’s all right,\" he said. \"I also slept.\"","Selene’s head snapped up as her pale eyes, sightless started at Dexter, stunned.","\"You slept?\"","Dexter shrugged casually.","\"Yeah. I also slept, you slept, so we slept together.\"","The words left his mouth and silence filled the entire room.","In that split second, Selene’s pale neck flushed read and she wa slightly flustered.","\"You...\" she stammered. \"We... you...\"","Dexter’s brain caught up with his mouth.","Approximately one second too late.","He chuckled and quickly clarified things.","\"I’m just joking,\" he said. \"We only cultivated together. We cultivated. You fell asleep. I put you to bed. Then I went to the kitchen to make the meals. Then I went outside to deliver them.\"","He paused. Regrouped.","\"We didn’t sleep together.\"","The clarification was explicit. Unambiguous. Delivered with the deliberate, precise enunciation of a man who was acutely aware that the wrong word or wrong inflection at this moment could result in a frost seizure in his bedroom.","Selene stared at him.","Her pale eyes, still red, still wide, still carrying the particular, stunned expression of a woman whose brain was processing information at approximately three times its normal speed, held his face for a long moment.","Then she exhaled.","\"Oh.\"","The word was soft. Relief. Clear, unmistakable relief. The exhalation of a body that had been bracing for one outcome and received another.","But Dexter, watching her through his Enhanced Hearing, detected something else in that exhale. A trace of something that wasn’t relief. Something that existed in the same frequency as relief but carried a different emotional signature.","Disappointment?","He wasn’t sure. The signal was too faint. Too brief. Too quickly buried beneath the larger, more dominant emotion of embarrassment to be reliably identified.","But it was there.","Or at least, he thought it was there.","Selene straightened her posture. She smoothed her sleeping gown with both hands. She pushed her disheveled hair back from her face. The process of reassembling her composure was visible, like watching someone build a wall brick by brick.","\"I want to go freshen up,\" she said. Her voice was controlled again. Measured. The voice of a woman who had decided that the previous thirty seconds had not happened and was now proceeding with her day as though they hadn’t.","Dexter nodded.","\"All right. I’ll have your food prepared at the dining table.\"","Selene walked out of the room.","She didn’t rush. She didn’t flee. She walked with the careful, measured grace that she always used, her bare feet finding the floor through memory and vibration. But her ears were pink. And the pink didn’t fade until she was well down the hallway.","Dexter stood alone in his bedroom. He stared at the closed door. Then at the rumpled bed. Then at the pillow that Selene had been holding.","The pillow still had the impression of her face in it.","He shook his head.","’She was disappointed. She was actually disappointed that we didn’t sleep together.’","’No. I’m reading too much into it. She was just embarrassed. The disappointment was relief that was misread by my Enhanced Hearing because I was overanalyzing micro-expressions in a woman who can’t make normal facial expressions because she’s blind and communicates through Echolocation and probably doesn’t even know what her face is doing half the time.’","’Or she was disappointed.’","’One of those two.’","He rubbed his face with both hands.","’I need to stop analyzing everything. I’m turning into a one-man surveillance system.’","He walked to the dining room.","---","He began plating the food. The Grade Five Celestial Phoenix Nectar Bowl for each of the girls. The Harmony Congee alongside it. The Star-Shaped Leaf tea in four cups.","He placed Mira’s bowl at her spot. Then Selene’s. Then Lyra’s. Then his own.","As he was setting Selene’s portion on the table, he felt something.","A gaze.","Not a sound. Not a vibration. Not a telepathic ping. A gaze. The particular, weighty, unmistakable sensation of being watched by someone who was waiting for you to notice them.","He turned around.","Lyra was sitting on the couch in the living room. Her dark eyes were open. The Primordial Beast Egg was still in her lap, but her cultivation had clearly been interrupted by the smell of food wafting from the kitchen.","She was staring at him.","Not at the food. At him. Through the living room, across the hallway, and into the dining room. Her dark eyes, behind the AI glasses, were locked onto his face with an expression that was simultaneously expectant and innocent.","The expression of a woman who wanted something to eat and was waiting for permission.","Dexter chuckled.","He projected his thoughts toward her through their telepathic connection.","\"Do you want to eat?\"","Lyra’s face immediately brightened. The transformation was instant. The serene, meditative composure of a cultivator dissolved, replaced by the eager, luminous enthusiasm of a woman who had been offered food.","She nodded. Rapidly. Her dark hair bounced. Her eyes sparkled.","\"Can I eat too?\" she asked as her telepathic voice carried the particular, hopeful quality of a child asking if it was time for dessert.","Dexter smiled. \"Of course.\"","Lyra’s face broke into a full smile, glowing like the sun itself.","She stood from the couch, egg in arm, and walked toward the dining room with excitement in her eyes.","Mira, who had been sitting in her wheelchair by the window with her eyes closed in what was supposed to be cultivation but was clearly eavesdropping!","She looked at Dexter then at Lyra but her expression was one of indifference as though she wasn’t interested in what theh were talking about.","Dexter saw her expression and he smirked.","\"You’re free not to eat with us if you don’t want to,\" he said casually but was clearly using reverse psychology on her.","Mira’s eye narrowed.","\"I wasn’t eating,\" she said."]},{"number":230,"title":"Chapter 230 | Do You Girls Want Massages?","paragraphs":["Dexter shrugged. \"So you don’t want to eat?\"","\"I didn’t say that either.\"","Dexter chuckled from the kitchen. He shook his head at the non-answer.","\"Understood,\" he said. \"I’ll set a plate down for you anyway.\"","He placed Mira’s bowl at her spot at the table. Then went to collect the tea.","By the time he returned, Mira’s food wasn’t at the dining table any longer she had taken it to the living room and was eating currently with her free arm.","Dexter said nothing.","He sat down at his own spot.","Lyra was already eating. Her spoon moved in a blur. The Grade Five meal disappeared from her bowl with speed.","Dexter blinked his eyes at the girl then at her chest and then shook his head with a small smile.","Selene emerged from the bathroom, her hair damp but her face clean. She’d swapped her sleeping gown for a simple white blouse and dark skirt, looking fresh and rested. The pink in her cheeks had faded to a natural healthy tone, slightly deeper than usual, Dexter noted.","She saw Dexter and lowered her head as she sat at the table. Found her bowl and picked up her spoon.","The three of them ate in silence and when Lyra asked for more, Dexter served her seconds without comment.","Selene ate slowly, tasting the food first and her eyes widened slightly as she spok.","\"This is different,\" she said quietly.","Dexter looked at her. \"It’s a new recipe.\"","Selene tilted her head.","\"It’s really good,\" she said. \"It feels... warm. Inside. Not temperature warm. Something else.\"","She took another spoonful.","\"I’m glad you liked it.\" he said.","Then Dexter set his spoon down as he looked at Lyra, then at Selene.","\"I want to ask you both something,\" he said.","Lyra’s spoon paused mid-air. Selene’s head tilted toward him.","\"The massage technique I use on Mira is different.\" Dexter continued. \"The 108 Body Massage Sutra. It stimulates healing at a cellular level. Increases nerve regeneration. Improves blood circulation. Accelerates the body’s natural recovery processes by alot.\"","He paused. Chose his words carefully.","\"If I apply the same technique to both of you, your healing rates would increase significantly. Selene, your frost condition might stabilize faster. The countdown to your next crisis could be extended further. Lyra, your overall recovery would accelerate.\"","He looked at them.","\"Do you want me to give you massages?\"","The question landed on the table like a stone in still water.","Lyra’s spoon clattered against the rim of her bowl.","Her dark eyes went wide. Her cheeks flushed. The pink started at her neck and climbed upward with the relentless, unstoppable progression of a woman whose circulatory system had decided to publicly broadcast her emotional state.","She was shy.","Not the mild, social shyness that characterized her usual interactions. The deep, full-body, can’t-make-eye-contact shyness of a woman who had just been asked if she wanted a man’s hands on her body.","Her mouth opened and closed but no sound escaped. This was because her vocal cords were damaged and the telepathic connection was experiencing technical difficulties. The volume of simultaneous emotional signals was overwhelming her brain’s transmission capacity.","She sat in her chair, her spoon in her hand, her face the color of a ripe tomato, and stared at her bowl as though it contained the answers to every question ever asked by humanity.","Selene was different.","Her initial reaction was similar. A faint flush appeared on her pale cheeks. Her fingers tightened slightly around her spoon. Her head, which had been tilted toward Dexter, tilted further, angling downward in the particular, self-conscious dip of a woman who was processing an unexpected proposition.","But she recovered faster.","Her Echolocation pulsed once. Twice. Mapping the room. Confirming the distance between herself and Dexter. Establishing the spatial parameters of the request.","Then she nodded.","\"If it might work,\" she said. Her voice was quiet. Careful. The voice of a woman who was weighing the practical benefits against the personal implications and arriving at a conclusion that prioritized healing over discomfort. \"Then there is no harm in trying.\"","Dexter looked at her. She was still looking at the table. Her cheeks were still pink. But her posture had settled. Her breathing was steady. She had made a decision and was committing to it.","He turned to Lyra.","Lyra was still staring at her bowl. Her face was still crimson. Her spoon was still frozen in the air. The telepathic silence continued, suggesting that her brain was still running the emotional equivalent of a system reboot.","Dexter waited.","Five seconds passed.","Ten seconds.","Lyra’s spoon descended to the bowl. She set it down. Her hands moved to her lap, where they clasped together tightly. Her dark eyes, still wide, still carrying the particular, luminous intensity of a woman whose entire nervous system was processing a significant emotional event, lifted from the bowl and found Dexter’s face.","She nodded.","One small, barely perceptible dip of her chin.","The nod was accompanied by a telepathic transmission. A single word. Fragile. Trembling. Spoken with the cautious, tentative delivery of someone who was agreeing to something they wanted but were terrified of wanting.","\"Okay.\"","Dexter smiled.","\"Good,\" he said. His voice was warm. Gentle. Carefully calibrated to convey reassurance without pressure. \"Whenever you are ready, come meet me. No rush. Anytime.\"","He paused.","\"Lyra, you don’t have to be nervous. It’s a medical procedure. I’ve been doing it on Mira for two weeks. It’s completely professional.\"","The word \"professional\" was, in retrospect, possibly not the most reassuring word he could have chosen. Because Lyra’s face immediately went from pink to a shade of red that suggested her circulatory system had abandoned all pretense of normal function.","She stood up.","The motion was abrupt. Sudden. The particular, explosive evacuation of a chair that occurred when a woman’s fight-or-flight response had been triggered and the flight option had won by default.","She grabbed the Primordial Beast Egg from beside her bowl. Clutched it against her chest. Her dark eyes met Dexter’s for one brief, mortified second.","Then she fled.","Her bare feet slapped against the hallway floor. The bedroom door opened. Closed. The faint sound of her body landing on the mattress was followed by silence.","Dexter stared at the empty chair.","He looked at Selene.","Selene was still at the table. Her pale eyes were aimed at her empty bowl. Her expression was composed. Serene. The expression of a woman who had just watched her sister-wife flee the room in embarrassment and was choosing to process the moment with dignity.","Then, very faintly, the corner of her lip twitched.","It was not a smile. It was not a smirk. It was the particular, barely perceptible micro-expression that appeared on Selene’s face when she found something amusing but was too refined to acknowledge it openly.","Dexter caught it.","He caught it because he had spent three weeks studying her face. Learning the topography of her expressions. Mapping the subtle, almost invisible movements that constituted her emotional vocabulary.","She was amused.","’She’s laughing at Lyra. Internally. Without moving a single facial muscle.’","’And probably at me too.’","Dexter shook his head.","\"I’ll be in my room when you’re ready,\" he said to Selene. \"Take your time.\"","Selene nodded slowly.","Dexter collected the dishes and carried them to the kitchen. He washed them in silence. The water ran. The soap foamed. The sponge moved in circles.","He thought about what he had just done.","He had offered to massage two women who were not Mira. The same offer that, twenty-four hours ago, had triggered a spike of jealousy so intense that the temperature in the room had visibly increased.","Mira was at the window.","She had heard.","Mira continued eating.","She said nothing but the silence was louder than any comment could have been.","Dexter dried the dishes. Placed them on the rack. Turned off the kitchen light.","He walked past Mira on his way to the hallway.","\"Ready for your massage in an hour,\" he said.","It was not a question. It was a schedule. Delivered with the calm, matter-of-fact authority of a man who was not going to ask permission because asking permission would open the door to refusal, and refusal was not on the agenda today.","Mira’s Spectral Arms folded behind her back.","Tighter than usual.","\"I didn’t say I wanted one,\" she said.","Dexter stopped walking.","He turned. Her rigid posture, folded Spectral Arms and crimson eyes fixed on the window with a determined gaze suggested she was desperately trying to focus on something other than him.","\"You didn’t say you didn’t want one either,\" he replied.","Mira’s jaw tightened.","\"I’ll be in your room in an hour,\" Dexter said. \"If you’re not there, I’ll come find you.\"","He turned and walked down the hallway.","Behind him, the temperature in the living room increased by two degrees.","Dexter smiled.","’I’m going to pay for that later.’","’But it was worth it.’"]},{"number":231,"title":"Chapter 231 | Rewards...","paragraphs":["Dexter went to his room and sat on the bed.","He had been so consumed by yesterday and also this morning’s events, that he had completely forgotten about the system reward.","\"System, open reward.\"","Golden text materialized in the air before him and Dexter’s mind went blank.","He blinked his eyes and cleaned his eyes to see if what he was seeing was true.","’What the heck? Just two rewards?’","Dexter scratched the back of his head clearly stunned and confused.","For the past several days, the system had been generous with its rewards. Each day brought a cascade of returns that had transformed him from his previous weakling status to his new found strength.","But today, the system had only given him two rewards instead of the usual ten plus.","He looked at the first reward.","’Sigh! Let’s just check why I got.’","[Reward 1: Lifespan Extension — Ten Additional Years]","Dexter stared at the notification as he pursed his lips.","Ten years was not insignificant. In the cultivation world, where breakthroughs between major realms could take decades and where the most powerful experts lived for centuries, ten years was nice but for a twenty-year-old man it wasn’t all that valuable.","Then he looked at the second.","[Reward 2: Dual Avatar Fruit]","[Grade: 8 ]","[Description: A legendary fruit born from the convergence of life energy and dimensional mana. When consumed, the fruit grants the user the ability to create a second physical body that is completely independent from the first.]’’","[Effects:]","[• The second body is a perfect physical replica of the user’s primary body]","[• The second body possesses its own independent mana reserves, cultivation base, and talent]","[• The second body can operate independently, at any distance, without affecting the primary body]","[• Damage to one body does not transfer to the other]","[• The user’s consciousness can shift between bodies at will]","[• Both bodies share the same soul, creating an unbreakable telepathic link between them]","Dexter’s hand trembled slightly. An actual grade 8 fruit? Dexter had never expected the system would give him a grade 8 fruit this early!","The Avatar Fruit could create a second body. A complete, independent, fully functional second body. With its own mana. Its own cultivation. Its own talent.","His mind went immediately to Aurelyx.","’If I give this fruit to Aurelyx, she could separate from Lyra’s body. She could have her own physical form. No more two consciousnesses fighting for control of one body.’","’Lyra would be free. Aurelyx would be free. Both of them, in their own bodies, living their own lives.’","The thought was intoxicating as this was the solution to the problem that had been consuming him since the night Aurelyx had appeared in his bedroom and kissed him and revealed herself as the Shadow Queen.","And now the solution was sitting in his hand. In the form of a fruit.","But.","Dexter’s excitement cooled.","’But I don’t know Aurelyx’s intentions.’","From what he could tell, Aurelyx was not a good person.","Giving her an independent body meant giving her freedom. Freedom to move, to act, to kill, without the limitation of having to surface from inside another person’s consciousness.","An Aurelyx with her own body was an Aurelyx unleashed.","’And I don’t know her true strength.’","This was the critical unknown. When Aurelyx was inside Lyra’s body, she was constrained by Lyra’s physical condition. Whatever power Aurelyx possessed, it was filtered through a broken vessel.","But if Aurelyx had her own body, a body created by the Avatar Fruit, a body with its own independent mana reserves and cultivation base, she would be at full power. Whatever that power was.","’The number one assassin in the city. At full power. With her own body. Answering to no one.’","’That might be worse than the current situation.’","Dexter closed his eyes.","He couldn’t give her the fruit. Not yet. Not without more information. He needed to understand Aurelyx first.","He needed to observe.","He needed to learn how the switching worked. When it happened. Why it happened. What triggered Aurelyx’s emergence and what caused her retreat.","He didn’t know any of this. And until he did, the Avatar Fruit would stay in his spatial storage.","Dexter placed the fruit in his spatial storage. The golden text faded. The system interface closed.","He sat on his bed for a moment, staring at the wall.","’I was expecting more rewards. I was hoping for a cultivation boost. Something that would push me past the Superhuman Realm and into Ultra.’","The disappointment was manageable. The system’s rewards were not predictable. They came in waves. Some days brought a flood. Others brought a trickle. The system didn’t operate on a schedule. It operated on investment. On the significance of his actions. On the depth of his care.","The past two days had been extraordinary in terms of events but perhaps less extraordinary in terms of investment. The kiss with Aurelyx had been detected by the system, but it had been attributed to Lyra.","Perhaps the past two days had been too chaotic by external events, the Harvest Homes fight, the squad meeting, Aurora’s proposition, Rachel’s call, Tessa’s secret, for the system to register the kind of deep, focused investment that triggered major rewards.","Dexter closed his eyes and began cultivating.","He cultivated for an hour. The mana flowed. His body strengthened. His mind settled. The cultivation was productive, even without a system boost. His SS-Rank mana affinity made absorption effortless. Every breath drew in energy. Every heartbeat distributed it through his system.","The alarm on his phone rang.","Dexter opened his eyes. Checked the time. One hour had passed. It was time for Mira’s massage.","He stood up. Walked to the door. Opened it. Stepped into the hallway.","Opposite his room was the girls’ bedroom. The door was closed.","He had expected it to remain closed. He had expected Mira to ignore his instruction. To stay at the window. To refuse to come. To maintain the sulk that had been her default state since the massage discussion the previous evening."]},{"number":232,"title":"Chapter 232 | I Will Seduce You In A Month","paragraphs":["Mira was stubborn, proud and also territorial. She did not respond well to being told what to do and did not appreciate having her exclusive ritual shared with other women.","Dexter had told her, one hour, my room, and had walked away without waiting for a response. As usual, Mira would never obey him.","He walked to the girls’ bedroom, opened the door and was stunned.","Mira was actually in the room!","She was in her wheelchair, parked directly beside the bed, waiting for him with her eyes closed.","Dexter blinked and then he smiled softly.","’She had actually listened to me.’","Maybe it’s because she hed heard him promised the other two girls massages but whatever the reason was, it was a good thing.","Dexter obviously wanted to tease her but paused and eventually decided not to say anything.","He walked to the wheelchair, stood behind it and placed his hands on the handles.","\"I’m going to carry you now,\" he said softly.","Mira didn’t open her eyes but she let out a ’hmph’ sound and turned her face away.","Dexter smile widened at her cute act of anger.","He lifted her from the wheelchair and carried her, then placed her on the bed.","Afterwhich, he began removing her clothing.","This morning, he had dressed her in the outfit she preferred. A white cropped top, black leather skirt and a black choker.","He removed the cropped top first and watched as the fabric slid over her head, revealing the white sports bra beneath.","Then he removed the skirt, unzipped it carefully, sliding the leather down over her hips and supple legs.","Mira lay on the bed in her sports bra and briefs. Her crimson hair on the pillow and her eyes closed.","Dexter then wore the Shockwave Glove as mana-threads tightened around his knuckles and activated it with mana.","He applied the Grade-4 Spiritual Massage Oil to his hands, set the glove to its lowest vibration setting and began.","Her Shoulders first. His oiled fingers pressed into the dense muscle where her neck met her shoulders as the shockwave Glove hummed and the Massage Sutra guided his movements through the precise, prescribed pattern.","Mira’s body was familiar to him now. Every pressure point, meridian pathway. He knew where she was tense, she was sore, the nerve damage was deepest and where the healing was furthest along.","Mira’s right arm lay on the mattress beside her body. It was no longer completely motionless. The fingers twitched occasionally.","He worked down her spine. Vertebra by vertebra.","Dexter increased the intensity slightly. The glove hummed louder as the vibration reached the deep tissue layers along her lumbar region.","\"Hm...\"","A sound escaped Mira’s lips.","Dexter paused for a bit and then continued. After a while, he spoke.","\"Mira,\"","\"What?\"","\"The marks on your back.\"","Her eyes opened.","\"What about them?\"","\"Have they changed?\"","Her expression changed slightly.","\"They’re bigger,\" she said quietly.","Dexter nodded.","The bloodline was progressing and the marks were growing.","\"How much bigger?\"","Dexter fingers measured the length. From the top of her shoulder blade to the bottom of the mark.","\"Two inches,\" he said. \"They were ten inches yesterday. They’re twelve now.\"","Two inches of growth in twenty-four hours.","At this rate, the bloodline would fully manifest within a month. Possibly less.","Mira said nothing. She simply nodded as he worked her legs, thighs, calves and feet. The muscles there were still atrophied, but the Massage Sutra was stimulating blood flow and nerve activity. With continued treatment, the legs would eventually respond.","He finished, cleaned the oil from her skin, dressed her, carried her to her wheelchair.","Mira sat in her chair. Her crimson eyes opened. She looked at nothing in particular.","\"Thank you,\" she said.","\"You’re welcome,\" Dexter replied.","He wheeled her to the living room. Positioned her by the window which is her favorite spot.","But instead of walking away, he had walked back to her and then knelt down to her level.","His dark eyes looking directly into her closed eyes.","Mira had just closed her eyes when she settled into her spot. But she felt his gaze.","She opened her eyes and saw him kneeling there, right in front of her.","She frowned.","\"What do you want this time?\"","Dexter smiled.","\"Can’t I just look at my wife?\" he said. \"Can’t I stare at my wife without wanting anything?\"","Mira sneered.","\"Pervert,\" she said. \"Liar.\"","But her face flushed slightly as she closed her eyes and ignored him. .","Pretended to concentrate. Resumed the mask of cultivation.","Thirty seconds passed.","But Dexter’s gaze was still on her.","She opened her eyes and immediately glared at him.","\"It seems you don’t have any work to do, right?\"","Dexter shrugged casually.","\"Yeah. I have nothing else to do.\"","Mira glared harder at him.","\"Are you trying to seduce me?\"","The word \"seduce\" came out dripping with mocking skepticism.","Dexter smirked.","\"You’ve been the one seducing me since the beginning.\"","Mira’s eyes widened by a fraction.","\"Is it working?\" Dexter continued.","Mira rolled her eyes eloquently.","\"Is that how you seduce?\" she said with contempt.","Dexter shrugged again.","\"Show me how to seduce a woman. Tell me how I can seduce you.\"","Mira glanced at his face then his feet and then back to his face.","\"You don’t have the talent,\"","Dexter was stunned but then he chuckled with confidence.","\"Are you trying to challenge me?\"","Mira scoffed.","\"Challenge?\" she repeated. \"Even if I give you one hundred years, there is no way you will be able to seduce a woman, not to talk of me.\"","Dexter glared at her.","\"What do you mean by that?\"","Mira sneered.","\"I meant exactly what I said and you know exactly what I mean.\"","Dexter stood up.","He pointed at her. \"You!\"","\"Okay,\" he said. \"Challenge accepted.\"","Mira was confused as she blinked her eyes.","\"What challenge?\"","Dexter smiled.","\"You just said I can’t seduce you, even if I have one hundred years. I said challenge accepted. Give me a month. I will seduce you in a month.\""]},{"number":233,"title":"Chapter 233 | Challenge Accepted","paragraphs":["\"Challenge accepted.\"","Mira frowned in confusion as she blinked and looked at him.","\"What challenge?\"","Dexter flexed the muscles in his neck and replied with a smile.","\"You just said I can’t seduce you, even if I have one hundred years. I said challenge accepted. But will do it in ten span of a month.\"","Mira laughed as thought it was the most funny thing she had ever heard.","Her smile was so dazzling that even after seeing all of Mira, he was still incredibly stunned by that astonishing smile.","Her laughter manage to subside as she spoke.","\"You seduce me in a month? Impossible.\"","Dexter who had been initially stunned came to at her words. His eyes narrowed as he glared at her.","\"Are you trying to call me ugly?\"","Mira shook her head slightly, a small smile on her face as she replied.","\"That’s not it.\"","She paused as she pondered whether she should say what was in her mind but decided to anyways.","\"At first I never truly looked at you and thought you were quite alright,\" she said. \"But now, I realize you are actually handsome. Maybe even more than you previously were.","Dexter’s eyebrows rose and he smirked as a bit of arrogance within his mind.","\"But even with that,\" Mira continued, recovering her composure and reassembling her sneer, \"there is no way you can successfully seduce me in a month.\"","She crossed her Spectral Arms. The mana limbs folded across her chest as she challenged him.","Dexter raised eyebrow dropped and his eyes narrowed.","’Shes quite confident, isn’t she?’","He glanced at her for a while, thought for a bit and then spoke.","\"Hm... to you, what counts as successful seduction?\"","He paused as a mischievous glint appeared in his eyes.","\"Kissing or sex?\"","Mira’s crimson eyes blazed and she immediately hissed at him. \"Who the hell is going to have sex with you!?\"","Dexter chuckled as he quickly held up both hands.","\"Hey, it’s an appropriate question. I’m just asking, what counts as seduction? Kissing, making out or sex?\"","Mira glared at him as her eyes literally almost burned with flames and she said through gritted teeth.","\"Kissing,\" she said.","Dexter nodded. \"Okay. So I have thirty days to kiss you. That’s the challenge.\"","Mira immediately nodded. The nod was accompanied by an arrogant smirk.","Dexter chuckled. \"Okay. What are the stakes?\"","Mira blinked and was slightly caught off guard by the challenge.","She frowned.","\"I have nothing to offer you,\" She said quietly.","Dexter looked at her then nodded his head.","\"Okay,\" he said. \"How about we double the promise you owe me?\"","Mira’s eyes widened.","\"Instead of you doing one single thing for me,\" Dexter continued, \"let’s make it two. Two favors instead of one. If I win.\"","Mira stared at him as she thought more deeply about it.","Dexter could not seduce her in thirty days. The man could barely touch her without his heart going haywire. Although he touched her regularly, she could tell he was always on the brink of breaking and also shy.","This man was not going to seduce anyone in thirty days.","\"Okay, fine,\" Mira said confidently. \"What about me? What would you give me if you fail?\"","Dexter blinked as his eyes shifted and he smirked.","\"Anything you want.\"","Mira raised an eyebrow. \"Anything?\"","\"Anything. And also, along with a surprise, I will do everything in my power to make you walk,\" he said.","The words landed in the living room like a thunderclap.","Mira eyes went wide as she stared at Dexter.","The ability to stand without help.","Dexter was offering that.","If he failed, he would dedicate everything he had to making her walk.","She stared at him. For a long, silent moment. Her crimson eyes moved across his face. Reading. Searching. Looking for the angle.","She didn’t find one.","Or was he planning to win?","She couldn’t tell.","And that, she realized with a discomfort that settled into her chest like a warm stone, was what made it dangerous.","Because if Dexter actually tried, if he actually applied himself to the challenge with the same focused, relentless, patient determination that he applied to everything else, if he brought that level of commitment to the task of seducing her...","She might lose.","Mira looked at Dexter.","Dexter looked at Mira.","The living room was quiet.","\"Deal,\" Mira said.","Dexter smiled.","The kind that started at his mouth and reached his eyes and stayed there.","\"Deal,\" he said.","He stood up. Extended his hand.","Mira looked at the hand. Then at his face. Then at the hand again.","Her right arm, the functioning one, the one that had moved for the first time three days ago, the one that had grabbed his wrist in a moment of unconscious need, reached out.","Her fingers found his.","The handshake was brief. Firm. The clasp of two people sealing an agreement that would, in thirty days, change everything between them.","Dexter’s hand was warm. Mira’s was cool.","They held for one second. Two.","Then released.","Dexter turned and walked toward the kitchen.","\"Thirty days, Mira,\" he said over his shoulder. \"Starting now.\"","Mira sat in her wheelchair. Her crimson eyes watched him go. Her right hand, the one that had just held his, rested in her lap. The fingers were still curled slightly. Holding the ghost of his grip.","She closed her eyes.","Her heart was beating faster than it should have been.","Faster than it had been in years.","’Thirty days.’","’Impossible.’","’Absolutely impossible.’","’So why is my heart doing that?’","\"BAM BAM BAM!\"","The knock was heavy.","Not the light, rhythmic tap of Tessa’s morning visits.","Bam. Bam. Bam.","Dexter blinked.","He wasn’t expecting anyone. Tessa had already come and gone this morning. Rachel had called. The bakery delivery was done. The squad meeting was yesterday. The festival was tomorrow.","There was no one on his schedule.","His Enhanced Hearing activated automatically, expanding outward through the walls and gate to scan the space beyond. He filtered the ambient noise. Traffic. Wind. The distant bark of a dog three houses down.","Then he found the heartbeats.","Not one.","Five.","All carrying the steady, controlled rhythm of people who were calm and purposeful and had arrived with intention.","Dexter frowned.","’Police? Hero Association?’","The thought sent a cold spike through his chest. Harvest Homes. The fight. The destroyed office. The four-meter transformation. The old man sent flying through a wall. The building damaged. The cameras. The witnesses.","’If they’ve traced it back to me...’","His mind spiraled."]},{"number":234,"title":"Chapter 234 | The Intruders","paragraphs":["’Run. Take the girls. Take the SUV and disappear.’","The thought was extreme but the thought was also rational and also irrational.","’Stop. Think. Face it head-on.’","Dexter took a breath and exhaled.","He looked at Mira. She was in her wheelchair by the window, eyes closed, cultivating.","\"I’m coming,\" he muttered.","He walked to the front door, opened the door and stepped onto the porch. Then walked to the gate.","He saw them.","And he stopped.","---","Five people stood outside his gate.","They wore dark tailored and expensive suit.","Four men stood side by side, two on each side. They were all tall broad-shouldered and carried themselves with the rigid practised posture of professional security personnel.","And in the center, flanked by the four suited men, stood a single figure.","An old man.","Perhaps sixty or older, his age was difficult to discern. His silver hair, neatly combed, framed his white temples. His face was lined but not wrinkled, bearing the deep permanent creases of a man who had maintained a specific expression for decades. This expression had ultimately frozen into his face by default.","He wore a dark grey suit. Slightly lighter than the others. A white handkerchief in the breast pocket. A monocle in his left eye.","Behind them, parked at the curb, was a limousine.","Dexter recognized the old man immediately.","The butler.","Not just any butler. The Ashford family butler. The man who had stood at the gate of the Ashford estate on the day Dexter was disowned and had delivered, with the flat, emotionless face the terms of his exile.","Ten thousand credits. The key to the bungalow and the deed to the house.","\"The family has nothing more to do with you.\"","Those had been his words the day Dexter’s life had ended and begun simultaneously.","And now the man was standing at his gate.","Dexter’s face hardened.","The warmth from the conversation with Mira, all of it evaporated and turned cold chilling.","He walked to the gate. Stopped behind it. Looked through the iron bars at the five suited figures.","\"What the fuck do you want?\"","The words were incredibly cold and chilling and even the surprising atmosphere seem to freeze at his cold words.","The butler, however, didn’t react.","Not a twitch. Not a blink. Not a single facial muscle moving in response to the profanity. The man’s expression remained exactly as it had been. Neutral. Composed. The professional blankness of someone who had been verbally abused by better than Dexter and had long since stopped registering it.","\"That is no way for a gentleman to speak,\" the butler said. His voice was measured. Precise. Each syllable articulated with the careful, deliberate enunciation of a man who had been trained in diction and had never relaxed his standards.","\"Good day to you, Dexter. I hope I met you in good health.\"","Dexter rolled his eyes.","\"And I hope you die in the next five minutes. What the hell do you want?\"","The butler’s expression didn’t change. The monocle caught the morning light and threw a small, sharp reflection across the gate. His gloved hands, white and pristine, remained clasped in front of his body.","He reached into his jacket.","One of the suited men on his left moved. A subtle, barely perceptible shift in posture that brought his hand closer to his jacket’s interior. A defensive reflex. The movement of a bodyguard responding to a potential threat.","The butler raised one hand. A small, calming gesture. The bodyguard relaxed.","The butler produced nothing from his own jacket. Instead, he turned slightly toward the bodyguard on his right. This man held a silver tray. Polished. Reflective. The kind of tray that was used in formal settings to present items that were too important to be handed directly and too small to be carried openly.","On the tray sat a letter.","It was white. Cream-colored, to be precise. Heavy stock. The kind of paper that was used for official correspondence between families of significance. The Ashford family seal was embossed on the front in gold wax. A phoenix, wings spread, rising from flames. The symbol of the family that had risen to the top of Stargate City through wealth, power, and the systematic exploitation of everyone beneath them.","The butler took the letter from the tray. His white-gloved fingers held it by the edges, presenting it to Dexter through the gate bars with the formal, precise gesture of a man who had been presenting documents to people for decades and could perform the action in his sleep.","Dexter stared at the letter.","Then at the butler.","Then at the letter again.","He didn’t take it.","\"What is it?\" he asked.","\"An invitation,\" the butler said.","\"From whom?\"","\"From the Ashford family.\"","Dexter’s jaw tightened. The coldness in his chest spread. Through his shoulders. Down his arms. Into his fingertips, which were currently gripping the gate bars with enough force to dent the iron.","\"I have nothing to do with the Ashford family,\" Dexter said. \"Your boss made that clear days ago doesn’t that ring any bells?\"","The butler’s expression remained unchanged.","\"Circumstances have changed,\" he said. \"The family has reconsidered certain positions. The letter contains the details of an invitation that the family believes you may find... advantageous to accept.\"","\"Advantageous,\" Dexter repeated. The word tasted like ash.","He looked at the letter. At the gold seal. At the phoenix rising from flames.","’The Ashford family is inviting me after disowning me, scamming three families into marrying their daughters to a bastard.’","’And they sent the butler. The same butler who handed me ten thousand dollars and told me I was worthless.’","’Why?’","The question was the only thing that prevented Dexter from telling the butler to leave and slamming the gate. Not curiosity nor politeness.","The Ashford family did nothing without reason. Every action, every statement, every gesture was calculated. Designed. Optimized for maximum effect with minimum cost. They were chess players. Grandmasters. And they had just moved a piece onto his board.","Refusing to look at the move would be a mistake."]},{"number":235,"title":"Chapter 235 | Fuck. Off","paragraphs":["The butler continued to hold the letter like Dexter’s opinion didn’t matter.","\"If you will accept the invitation and read it, you will know every detail regarding the event. Take it.\"","Dexter looked at the letter then he glared at the butler.","\"Like I said, I have nothing to do with the Ashford family,\" he said coldly.","\"I and the Ashford family are done. You said so yourself.\"","He held the butler’s gaze.","\"It’s useless. I have nothing else to do with the family. Now, if there is nothing more, take your leave.\"","The butler’s face changed slightly as he stared at Dexter coldly.","\"You should do well to know your place. If it wasn’t absolutely important for you to attend, do you think the family would extend an invitation to a bastard they alredy cast aside? This is your opportunity and you should be groveling on the ground for this opportunity graced to you by the Ashford family.\"","Killing intent exploded from Dexter’s gaze and the smell of blood spread through the entire neighborhood as his Asura body activated.","Dexter’s lips slowly curled upwards as he stared at the old man before him. \"Fuck, Off.\"","The butler’s blood ran cold as the killing intent spread through his entire body like ice pricking his entire body.","Before he could say anything, the gate instablt slammed shut!","\"Bang!!!\"","It closed directly in the butler’s face!","The butler stood on the other side of the gate as his heart pounded slightly with fear.","He looked at the closed gate, gritted his teeth as he halted at the gate.","Inside his compound, Dexter inhaled deeply and then breathed out as he calmed his killing intent. It eas becoming even more explosive than before.","After a while, he then walked to the house and closed the door.","When he came to the door, he saw Mira turned to look at him, then she suddenly spoke.","\"The Ashford family butler,\" With her strength, she obviously can hear from far distances.","Dexter looked at her then nodded slowly. \"Yeah.\"","Mira’s brows furrowed slightly in worry.","\"What do they want?\"","Dexter shrugged as he flexed his fingers.","\"They came to drop an invitation letter. I have no idea what it’s about, and I don’t wish to know. I have nothing to do with the Ashford family. So I really don’t care.\"","Mira blinked as she stared ad his face closely.","Then she asked something unexpected.","\"Are you okay?\"","The same three words that Selene had asked the night before, when she had sensed his killing intent. But the tone was different. Selene’s version had been cautious.","Mira’s version was something else. Without pretence or sarcasm.","Dexter was taken aback.","Dexter looked at her as saw hee gaze was soft, then he smiled.","\"Yeah,\" he said. \"I’m okay.\"","Mira stared at his face for a long, silent moment and when she found what she was looking for, She nodded.","Then she closed her eyes as mana swirled around her body as she resumed her cultivation.","Dexter watched her for a moment and something warm settled in his chest.","He then turned toward the hallway.","Had had only taken one step, when,","\"Bam. Bam. Bam!!!\"","The knock hit the gate like a hammer and was even heavier than before.","Dexter stopped. His face changed and his gaze hardened.","’If they don’t leave me alone, I will teach them a lesson.’","He stormed to the front door. Yanked it open. Walked to the gate.","He grabbed the gate handle. Pulled it open.","\"Did I not tell you to leave?\" he growled.","The words were loud. Hard. Directed outward through the opening gate with the full force of a man who had reached the limit of his tolerance and was prepared to enforce it with whatever means were necessary.","But the words died in his throat.","Because the butler was not there.","The limousine was gone. The five suited figures were gone. The silver tray, the white gloves, the monocle, the cream-colored letter with the gold phoenix seal. All gone. The street was empty of everything except the fading smell of expensive perfume and the residual impression of a vehicle that had been parked at the curb.","The butler had left.","What stood at Dexter’s gate instead was something else entirely.","Something he had forgotten about.","Something he had, if he was being honest, completely forgotten existed.","Kreg.","The name registered before the face did.","Kreg.","The thug. The gang leader. The man who had walked into his house three weeks ago with four cronies and had demanded protection money.","\"We’ll be back next month.\"","That had been the promise. Next month. The monthly protection fee. The Red Fang Crew’s business model. Pay us, or we find other ways to collect.","Dexter had forgotten.","He had been so consumed by the system, that he had completely and utterly forgotten about the street thug who had robbed him in his own living room.","Kreg stood at the gate.","He was tall. Muscular. Built like a door, which was the description Dexter had applied to him the first time they had met. His white beard was the same. His leather jacket was the same. His gold tooth caught the morning light and threw a small, sharp glint across the gate bars.","He was not alone.","Behind him, arranged in the loose, informal formation of men who followed a leader because the leader was bigger than them, stood four figures. Dexter recognized them. The same four from weeks ago. The same four who had fanned out across his living room, hands in pockets, grinning with the confidence of men who believed they owned whatever street they were standing on.","Kreg looked down at Dexter and smiled arrogantly.","\"Oh,\" Kreg said, his voice deep and rough, carrying the particular, amused cadence of a man who had just been shouted at and had found it funny. \"You actually dared to shout at me?\"","Dexter stared at him. Kreg still had the gold tooth, the leather jacket and there were four minions behind him."]},{"number":236,"title":"Chapter 236 | The Thug, Kreg!","paragraphs":["Dexter blinked.","He hadn’t expected this.","He had almost forgotten about Kreg and the money and what he had said about his wives.","But here he was, standing at the gate with his four minions behind him and with the same arrogance too!","And Dexter was surprised.","Dexter was surprised by his own reaction.","Dexter had been planning to go find Kreg eventually when he had time.","But Kreg had come to him.","’Is this what they call a blessing in disguise?’","\"Kreg,\" he said.","Kreg smiled confidently as the gold tooth glinted in his mouth.","\"Oh, now you remember me,\" Kreg said. \"Nice. I assume you haven’t forgotten about my protection fee.\"","Dexter blinked and was about to say signing when Kreg moved.","He didn’t wait for Dexter to speak as he pushed past Dexter. Kreg’s shoulder caught Dexter’s chest, shoving him sideways, intending to Knick him down but Dexter didn’t move a single inch.","Kreg was a bit stunned but he didn’t put that to his mind as he entered the compound.","His eyes moved across the property as he scanned the place.","The four lackeys followed him as they also pushed past Dexter with the same casual, dismissive physical contact.","They all swaggered into the compound like they owned it.","Dexter registered their cultivation levels as they passed.","Kreg. Eighth Stage Awakened.","The others. Seventh. Sixth. Sixth.","Dexter’s eyes narrowed slightly.","Three weeks ago, Kreg had been at Third Stage Awakened. The others at First and Second. Now they were Awakned. All of them. Advanced by multiple levels in less than a month.","That kind of advancement was not natural.That kind of jump required either an extraordinary external resource or an extraordinary external intervention.","’ Someone is boosting them.’","That was the only reason.","But Dexter didn’t say anything as he didn’t care about this.","As Kreg entered, he didn’t pause as he spoke.","\"Oh,\" Kreg said. \"I see you’ve renovated. This is nice.\"","The words were casual. Appreciative in the particular, proprietary way that a landlord appreciates improvements to a property he intends to seize. The tone of a man who looked at someone else’s work and saw his own future.","He didn’t wait for a response. He opened the front door. Stepped inside.","Dexter’s front door. Dexter’s house. Opened and entered by a man who had not been invited and had not asked.","The four lackeys followed. They entered the living room with the same swaggering, take-ownership gait that their leader had used. Looking around. Evaluating. Claiming.","Dexter stood at the gate.","He watched them go.","His face was expressionless. Completely, absolutely, perfectly blank. The mask he had spent nineteen years perfecting in the Ashford estate. The mask that revealed nothing. Not anger. Not fear. Not the particular, cold, focused calculation that was running behind his eyes like a computer processing a targeting solution.","But a smile tugged at the corner of his lips.","Not a warm smile. Not a friendly smile. The particular, barely perceptible, almost invisible upward curve of a mouth that was anticipating something.","He walked through the gate. Closed it behind him. The latch clicked.","He walked up the path. Into his house. Through the front door.","Kreg was in the living room. Standing. Looking around. His eyes moving across the space with the slow, evaluating scan of a man who was mentally cataloguing everything he could take.","Then his eyes found Mira.","She was in her wheelchair by the window. Crimson hair. Pale skin. Closed eyes. Cultivating. Her Spectral Arms were folded behind her back, motionless. She was wearing the white cropped top and black skirt that Dexter had dressed her in that morning. She looked, despite the wheelchair and the paralysis and the three years of suffering, like what she was. A noblewoman. A warrior. A woman whose beauty had not been diminished by her condition but had been refined by it, sharpened to a point that was almost painful to look at.","Kreg’s smile widened.","The widening was specific. Targeted. The particular, predatory expansion of lips over teeth that occurred when a man saw something he wanted and had no intention of asking permission.","\"Oh,\" Kreg said. His voice had dropped. Softened. The particular, intimate tone that bullies used when they were transitioning from general intimidation to specific acquisition.","The lackey who had whistled at Dexter’s wives three weeks ago, the same one, the one with the sharp eyes and the loose mouth, spoke.","\"Ooh, boss. The girls are even prettier than before.\"","He walked toward the living room. His eyes were on Mira. Then on Lyra, who was on the couch with the Primordial Beast Egg, her AI glasses on, her dark eyes open, watching the men enter with an expression that was, through the barrier of her deafness, taking longer to process than it would for someone who could hear their words.","\"Boss, the girls are even prettier than before,\" the lackey repeated. \"If we wait any longer, other gangs might beat us to the chase.\"","He whistled. The sound was sharp. Loud. The particular, aggressive, proprietary whistle of a man who was making a claim and wanted everyone in the room to know it.","He walked toward the living room. Toward Mira. Toward Lyra. His eyes moving between them with the casual, evaluating hunger of someone browsing a display case.","Dexter watched.","He stood near the front door as a small smile tugged at his face.","He had closed the front door and locked it. Be had also don’t the same for the gate too.","He snapped his fingers and above the house, in the sky that had been blue and clear and ordinary, the air rippled. As the Type-5 House Protection Talisman, buried beneath the living room rug, responded to Dexter’s command.","The formation’s primary function was defense but it had several secondary function.","One of which was a ilencing.","Every sound within the dome, every voice, every scream, every impact, every crash, every cry, was contained, sealed within the boundary of the formation and prevented from traveling beyond it.","What happened inside would not be heard outside."]},{"number":237,"title":"Chapter 237 | Kreg...","paragraphs":["A young dark-haired woman stood in front of the Hero Association building, staring up at its magnificent structure. Though it wasn’t as large as the Hero Association headquarters, it was still impressive. Heroes came and went through the gate as she watched.","\"Hey,\" the woman said. \"I assume you’re Jasmine.\"","Jasmine nodded slowly. \"And you’re...?\"","The woman smiled. The smile was warm. Genuine. The kind that arrived without calculation and stayed without effort.","\"Call me Rachel. I was assigned to show you around. Show you your office. Walk you through the branch’s operations.\"","She extended her hand.","\"Welcome .\"","Jasmine took the hand and shook her.","\"Please come with me,\" Rachel said.","Jasmine nodded. She followed Rachel through the front entrance.","---","Dexter stood with his hands behind his back, looking at the five thugs in his home. His lips curled into an evil smirk as various thoughts flashed through his head.","At that moment, Kreg and the other four lackeys were still looking around the house. One had even gone to the living room, heading directly toward Mira.","However, Kreg seemed to notice something. Although arrogant, his survival instinct was extremely sharp. He knew whom to offend and whom not to offend. That was why, despite the number of strong people in the neighborhood, nobody had taught him a lesson. He had not offended the wrong people.","But now, he suddenly felt that something was wrong. He didn’t know exactly what, but he felt it.","One of his lackeys spoke. \"Boss, what do you say? We can actually take one of the girls and sell her to one of the top three families. No matter how powerful the Vance, Frost, and Callaway families are, they can never compare to the top one, top two, or top three families. If we sell one of these premium girls to that royal blood, we’ll earn enough money to live out our lives. Enough money that our generations would inherit. We could even flee the country and enjoy the rest of our lives. What do you say, boss?\"","Kreg did not answer. His brows furrowed as the wrongness persisted. He looked around the house, then turned toward Lyra.","Lyra sat on the couch in the living room, cross-legged, eyes closed in concentration. Mira’s eyes were also closed. Kreg looked at both women. It wasn’t their beauty that attracted him now. It was the fact that he couldn’t sense their strength at all.","But the danger he felt wasn’t coming from them. It came from another source. He looked around and frowned but could not see who or what it was.","\"Boss, are you all right?\" one lackey asked.","Kreg shook his head. \"Must be my imagination.\" He waved the lackey off. \"I’m all right.\" He turned back to Dexter and smiled.","\"As you know, there was a monster outbreak a few weeks ago. If it wasn’t for us—the Red Fang gang—this entire street would have been wiped out. So our protection fee has increased by more than ten times. Previously, you gave me five thousand dollars, which was barely enough to do anything. But since you were the son of the Ashford family, we gave you face and didn’t say anything. This time, our protection fee has increased a lot. It has been months since the Ashford family even cared about you. They have never come here, which means you have been truly abandoned. Your wife has also been abandoned. Therefore, there is nobody else to protect you. Their reputation cannot protect you this time. So our fee has increased to five hundred thousand dollars. What do you say?\"","Dexter blinked. Then he smiled widening and chuckled slightly.","Kreg raised an eyebrow, surprised that Dexter dared to chuckle.","Suddenly, one of the lackeys heading toward Mira froze. His face flashed with confusion. He tried to move, but pressure held him as if ten mountains had landed on him. His body was a statue; he could not move a single muscle. His eyes widened in horror. He opened his mouth to scream, but no sound came out. He tried to explode with energy, but his energy was restricted by multiple chains. He could not move at all.","The other three lackeys noticed nothing. They were staring at Dexter along with Kreg.","At that moment, Dexter spoke. \"Oh, you’re laughing.\"","One lackey said, \"No, boss. I think he has finally gone mad, actually daring to laugh at us. Should I teach him a lesson? Let me teach him a lesson.\"","The lackey stepped forward. It was the one Dexter had kicked in the nuts the first time, and he was still angry. He was about to crack his knuckles when Kreg raised a hand. The lackey froze.","\"Wait,\" Kreg said. \"Let him speak.\"","Dexter looked at the lackey, then at Kreg. \"Five thousand dollars. Five hundred thousand dollars. From five thousand to five hundred thousand. Isn’t that a bit much? That is slightly too much.\"","Kreg shrugged. \"Of course it’s much. We, the Red Fang gang, risked our lives to repel the monsters that invaded this district. That’s why it costs. I hope you understand where we are coming from.\"","Dexter slowly nodded. \"Yeah, I understand where you’re coming from. So which one of you should I give the money to?\"","Kreg’s eyes widened slightly. He had expected Dexter to negotiate, or to say he didn’t have that kind of money. But Dexter actually agreed. His brows furrowed, but then he spoke. \"If you are trying to deceive us, I hope you know the consequences.\"","Dexter nodded. \"Of course. I would never dare deceive anybody from the Red Fang gang.\"","Kreg laughed arrogantly, and his lackeys laughed with him. Dexter brought out his phone, opened his bank app, and told Kreg to give him his bank information. Kreg did. Dexter nodded and transferred the money. He showed his phone to Kreg.","Kreg chuckled. \"Satisfied. Of course, of course. Haha. I never thought you had that kind of money at hand. Wonderful, wonderful.\"","The lackeys erupted in laughter and joy."]},{"number":238,"title":"Chapter 238 | You’re Going To Die","paragraphs":["Kreg chuckled. \"Satisfied. Of course, of course. Haha. I never thought you had that kind of money at hand. Wonderful, wonderful.\"","The lackeys erupted in laughter.","Suddenly, Kreg ’s laugh paused as he noticed something wrong. He turned to the side and realized his lackey on Mira’s side was still there. \"Victor? What are you still doing there? Victor!\"","Victor didn’t answer. \"Victor!\"","Still no answer. One of the lackeys frowned and went toward Victor. When he reached him, he froze. Victor was literally crying—crying blood. His eyes were bloodshot, his body frozen, his mouth open in a soundless scream.","The lackey was stunned. Before he could turn to say something to Kreg, his body also froze as if it were a statue.","The other two lackeys and Kreg noticed something was wrong. They turned toward Mira’s side.","Dexter cracked his neck. \"So we begin.\"","\"I have waited so long for this moment. I didn’t expect you to deliver yourself to me.\"","Kreg frowned, noticing Dexter’s voice had changed. \"What do you mean by that?\"","Dexter tilted his head slowly. \"Even if you kneel, beg, or scream, it’s useless. You wanted to cripple me, right? You humiliated me in front of my wife. Threatened my wife. And you dared to extort me twice. I just hope I get a return for the 5000 dollars I gave you.\"","Kreg frowned and his face hardened then exploded with his seventh-level awakened strength. \"What the fuck are you talking about? Do you want to die?\"","Dexter chuckled. \"Die? The one to die would be you.\"","Kreg’s voice had barely fallen when Dexter disappeared.","\"Bang!\"","A fist slammed into Kreg’s stomach. His eyes bulged as the air was violently knocked from his lungs. His entire body folded inward, doubling over around the impact, before he was sent flying across the room like a ragdoll.","\"BOOM!\"","He crashed into the wall, leaving a spiderweb of cracks behind. Dust and plaster rained down around him as his body crumpled to the floor in a broken heap.","He gasped, wheezed, tried to breathe—but his lungs refused to cooperate. The air tasted like copper and chalk. His ribs screamed with every shallow, ragged gasp.","Before Kreg could recover, Dexter was already standing in front of him.","Kreg’s pupils contracted.","\"How...?\"","He hadn’t even seen Dexter move. One moment, Dexter was across the room. The next, he was there.","Dexter grinned as he grabbed him by the hair and slammed his head into the floor.","\"BANG!\"","The impact shook the room. The floorboards cracked beneath Kreg’s skull. Blood sprayed across the wood in a dark, wet arc. The coppery scent of it filled the air, thick and cloying.","\"You’re an 7th-level awakened now,\" Dexter said calmly. \"You probably thought that made you powerful.\"","Kreg coughed, blood dripping from the corner of his mouth. His vision swam. His thoughts scattered like startled birds. He tried to speak, tried to form words, but all that came out was a wet, pathetic gurgle. The sound of a man whose body was failing him faster than his mind could track.","Dexter lifted him again by the hair, forcing Kreg to look up at him. Forcing him to meet his eyes.","\"Look at me. You really think you are strong but there’s always a mountain above a mountain...\"","\"BANG!\"","He slammed him down again. The sound was sickening. Bone meeting wood. Flesh meeting force. The particular, wet, cracking resonance of a skull being introduced to a surface that would not yield.","\"You’re nothing.\"","Kreg gritted his teeth.","\"You cripple!\"","He activated his talent as his arms covered in bone spikes as he punched hard at Dexter.","Dexter caught his fist effortlessly, mid-swing, as though he were catching a thrown ball as the spike cracked and shattered against his palm.","Dexter’s body was insane. Not to mention Awakened level 7, Superhuman level 7 could barely penetrate his skin.","Dexter held his fist and squeezing gently, letting Kreg feel the absolute futility of resistance.","Letting him feel the particular, crushing, inexorable pressure of a grip that could not be broken.","A sharp crack echoed through the room as Dexter twisted his arm.","Kreg screamed.","\"AAAGH!\"","The remaining lackeys finally understood. They had kicked a diamon stone.","\"Run!\"","One of them shouted and desperately tried to escape. He bolted toward the door, He reached the door—","Only for an invisible force to slam him backward.","BOOM!","He crashed into the floor. The impact drove the air from his lungs and left him gasping like a fish on dry land. Dexter didn’t even look at him. The formation had sealed the compound. Nobody was leaving. Not until Dexter decided they could. Not until he was finished.","\"I’ll save you for last,\" Dexter faced Kreg as he spoke. \"It’s always the sweetest.\"","He smiled as he turned away from Kreg.","He hadn’t used any pressure from his superhuman strength, yet Kreg was frozen in fear. The man who had walked into his home with confidence, with arrogance, with four men and a plan—that man was gone. What remained was a trembling shell.","Dexter licked his lips and turned toward another lackey—the man who had previously touched his wife the first time they came. The one who had put his hands on Mira’s shoulder while she sat helpless in her wheelchair. The one who had smiled while doing it.","\"Bang!\"","His chest caved in as blood spilled from his lips and he was sent flying. He hit the ground hard, rolled, and came to a stop against the base of the couch.","He tried to breathe. Blood bubbled between his lips with each shallow, labored gasp. The sound was wet and rhythmic, like a leaking valve.","Dexter slowly approached him. The man’s face turned extremely pale. The color of a corpse that hadn’t realized it was dead yet.","\"Please...\"","Dexter stopped in front of him. \"You remember me?\"","The man trembled. \"I... I was wrong.\"","Dexter crouched down. \"You were wrong?\"","[A/N: Really sorry about the confusion]"]},{"number":239,"title":"Chapter 239 | Killing The Thugs","paragraphs":["\"Please...\"","Dexter stopped in front of him. \"You remember me?\"","The man trembled. \"I... I was wrong.\"","Dexter crouched down. \"Oh... you were wrong?\"","His voice was frighteningly calm.","\"You came into my home.\"","He grabbed the man’s collar, twisting the fabric in his fist.","\"You robbed me.\"","He lifted him off the ground with one hand, holding him suspended like a puppet whose strings had been cut.","\"You threatened my wife.\"","His eyes became cold, colder than the void between stars and merciless like a demon.","\"Beat me up and you thought you could do it again?\"","The man’s entire body trembled in fear and suddenly, his grey pants turned dark as his bladder let go, soaking his pants, and dripping on the floor.","He wanted to beg, find mercy from Dexter but found nothing.","Dexter looked down at the ground as the water stained his floor.","\"Disgusting.\"","Dexter immediately threw him aside.","\"BOOM!\"","The man crashed through the coffee table, shattering it into splinters as he lay there, broken and bleeding, whimpering like a wounded animal.","Two were frozen by Mira’s pressure. Their bodies locked in place, eyes bleeding, mouths open in silent screams that would never be heard. The worst part is they were aware if everything but but utterly incapable of doing anything about it.","And only one was left.","Dexter looked at him with a dark smile as he took a step forward. Before his feet could touch the ground, he flashed and appeared before him.","\"Crack!\" \"Crack!\" \"Crack!\"","The thug’s neck rotatated twisted three times around his head as the flesh of his neck bulged and looked obscene as he stood there for three seconds.","His face was pale with fear and even as he was dying, fear and horror could be seen in his face as he fell to the ground.","He didn’t die immediately but he lost all motor fiction as he lie there.","Dexter walked over to the one with the cracked chest.","The one who had suggested selling his wives.","\"You’re the one who wanted to sell my wives aren’t you?\"","Dexter smiled as he bent down, picking up the man’s arm.","\"Crack!\"","\"Ahhh!!!\"","The man screamed in pain and agony as Dexter broke his arms inch by inch.","The screams became even more high-pitched and piercing as Dexter finished twisting the entire right arm. He turned to the left arm and did the same. Making sure every inch of the nine was broken.","The man fainted and Dexter immediately woke him up with a slap.","\"Now now, don’t sleep on me, we are now done.\"","Dexter did the same to his legs.","Breaking them inch by inch. Placing his legs on the man’s balls.","\"Pop!\" \"Pop!\"","Two popping sounds echoed through the entire place. And the man screamed even more as Dexter tortured him.","Until Mira said, \"Noisy.\"","With a whoosh, flames erupted from her arm and landed in the man as shs burnt him with her flames, which made him scream even more horrifyingly than before.","The burning was slow, too. Deliberate. It consumed his clothing first. Then his skin. Then the tissue beneath. Layer by layer.","Dexter blinked. It seemed her flames could actually affect the soul. He watched the particular, faint, barely visible distortion that appeared around the man’s body as the flame consumed him.","When he was done burning, silence descended over the room. The particular, absolute, ringing quiet that followed the removal of all sound sources. What remained on the floor was not a body but an outline.","He then went to the two beside Mira and killed them too.","They collapsed without a sound.","Kreg was barely conscious. His arrogance was completely gone. His gold tooth was missing. His confidence was gone.","\"What... are you?\"","Dexter walked toward him. \"You don’t need to know.\"","Kreg tried to crawl backward. His hands scrabbled against the floor.","Dexter grabbed him by the throat and lifted him effortlessly. Kreg’s hands clawed at Dexter’s wrist. His legs kicked uselessly. His face changed color. From red to purple. From purple to blue.","\"You should have stayed away from my family.\"","Kreg’s eyes widened. \"Wait—\"","Crack.","Dexter’s grip tightened. Kreg’s struggling stopped. His body went limp. The particular, quiet, definitive sound of a trachea being compressed past its structural limit.","Dexter released him, allowing the body to fall to the floor.","One by one, he finished off the remaining members of the Red Fang Gang. When the last of them stopped moving, Dexter stood silently in the middle of the room.","His expression was cold.","He looked around. At the bodies. At the ash outline. At the blood on the walls. At his living room—the space he had spent three weeks cleaning, repairing, painting, and protecting. At the Pure-Air Fragrance Artifact that still hummed on its shelf, doing its job regardless of what had happened in the room it was filtering.","He walked to the front door. Unlocked it. Opened it.","The morning air came in.","Dexter stood in the doorway, closed his eyes and breathed.","The five men who had entered his home were now dead. The Red Fang Crew was finished.","And Dexter Ashford was still standing.","After Dexter killed Kreg, he looked around.","Lyra was still on the chair, her eyes closed, still cultivating. It seemed she hadn’t noticed anything. Or perhaps she had noticed something and simply chosen to ignore it. Alternatively, she might have been cultivating so deeply that the violence in the living room had registered as nothing more than background noise.","Dexter watched her for a moment and the coldness in his gaze dissipated like smoke as he smiled at her.","’It’s time for clean up.’","Then he started to clean up.","He took the bodies of the remaining thugs—the ones Mira hadn’t incinerated, the ones who had died by his own hands—and stacked them in the backyard. Greg’s lifeless body went on top. Dexter carried them all as if they weighed nothing, his expression unchanged, his pace steady. The particular, casual ease of a man who had done this before and would likely do it again."]},{"number":240,"title":"Chapter 240 | Where Do You Want Me?","paragraphs":["’It’s time for clean up.’","Then he started to clean up.","He took the bodies of the remaining thugs—the ones Mira hadn’t incinerated, the ones who had died by his own hands—and stacked them in the backyard. Kreg lifeless body went on top. Dexter carried them all as if they weighed nothing.","When he reached the backyard, Selene was cultivating on the swinging chair.","She turned to face him as he walked in.","She ’saw’ the corpses Dexter was dragging raised an eyebrow but didn’t say anything.","Dexter blinked, then offered a small, apologetic nod. \"Sorry for the disturbance.\"","Selene shrugged. \"It’s all right.\"","Dexter threw the corpses onto the center of the backyard. Then, activating his Heavenly Flame, a fireball materialized in front of him and landed in the corpses.","The corpses burned.","The smell that rose was not unpleasant. It was the particular, rich, smoky aroma of roasting meat—barbecue, almost, if one didn’t think too hard about the source. That was the main reason Dexter hadn’t burned them in the living room. The smell would have lingered and seeped into the furniture.","Here, in the open air, it would disperse.","And fortunately, the air purifier Mira had burned—the Pure-Air Fragrance Artifact—had already cleansed the interior. The smell wouldn’t reach the house.","When the flames died and nothing remained but ash, Dexter turned to go back inside.","Then Selene spoke.","\"I...\"","She stopped herself.","Dexter, who was about to enter, paused. With his enhanced hearing, he had caught her speaking before she stopped herself.","He turned back toward her. \"Do you need anything?\"","Selene blinked. She remained silent for a while. The particular, internal, visibly conflicted silence of a woman who wanted to ask for something but didn’t want to impose.","Then she spoke.","\"Was it your massage technique that healed Mira’s arm?\"","Dexter blinked. Then he slowly nodded.","\"Yes. It’s a massage technique—but not just the massage technique. The healing was due to many factors. The food I provide. The tea. The medicine. The massage. All of it, working together. But yes, the massage is one of the factors.\"","Selene nodded slowly. Then she opened her mouth to say something else.","Then closed it.","Dexter watched her. He knew how shy she was. Knew that she didn’t like to ask for things. Knew the particular, self-effacing, almost apologetic quality of a woman who had spent too long in the background and had never quite learned how to ask for what she wanted.","So he spoke first.","\"If you want, I can try it on you.\"","Selene’s eyes widened slightly.","\"Right now, since I’m not doing anything at the moment. It will only take ten to twenty minutes of your time.\"","Selene blinked. Her face flushed—the particular, pale, almost translucent blush of a woman whose complexion was so fair that any color at all stood out like a stain on white silk. It made her look, for a moment, almost human.","She slowly nodded. She didn’t look at him.","\"Okay.\"","Dexter chuckled internally.","He turned and headed back into the house to prepare.","But first, Dexter needed to deal with the mess in the living room.","He started with the ashes—the particular, fine, grey-white residue of the body Mira had incinerated. The flames had burned so completely that nothing remained but a faint, almost invisible smudge on the carpet. He vacuumed it away, watching the particles disappear into the machine with the particular, clinical detachment of a man who had long since stopped being bothered by such things.","Then he addressed the wall.","The spiderweb of cracks where Kreg had slammed against it.","It took less than two minutes to clean the living room.","The wall would need to be repaired, of course. But he had materials left over from the window repair and he had purchased during the renovation. But he won’t fix it now.","Not when he had somewhere else to be.","His heartbeat had increased thinking about it but he tried to hide his excitement.","He was about to leave the living room when Mira spoke.","\"Won’t you be in trouble?\"","Dexter paused.","Mira’s voice was quiet.","\"Since they’re dead,\" she continued, \"there might be others who would look for them. It might cause trouble for you.\"","Dexter shrugged. \"It doesn’t really matter.\"","Mira blinked at him.","\"It can’t be big enough trouble,\" he said, \"that we can’t handle when the time comes.\"","She looked at him for a moment. Then she nodded. \"Okay.\"","Dexter smiled at her.","He was about to leave when he paused.","He looked down at Lyra.","She was still on the couch, cultivating.","Dexter smiled slightly.","He flipped his fingers. A pastry appeared on his left palm.He gently placed it on the couch beside Lyra.","when she woke, she would see it.","Dexter left.","---","He went to the room to prepare.","The bed was already made—the particular, clean, crisp, folded precision of sheets that had been smoothed to perfection. He placed the oils on the nightstand. The shockwave glove. The particular, soft, warm towels he had warmed in advance.","He arranged everything beside Selene bed, then waited.","Two minutes later, the door creaked.","The atmosphere in the room suddenly chilled.","Dexter raised his head.","The door creaked open, and a figure slowly entered. It was Selene. Her head was bowed. Her white hair—the particular, silver, almost luminous cascade of it—covered her entire face as she entered the room.","She moved with the particular, hesitant, almost reluctant grace of a woman who was not used to being seen. Not used to being the center of attention.","Dexter didn’t speak.","He simply waited.","Selin stepped fully into the room, and the door clicked shut behind her.","The silence stretched.","Then, slowly, she raised her head.","\"Where do you want me?\" she asked.","Her voice was quiet and shy as she spoke.","Dexter gestured to the bed. \"Lie down. Face up. I’ll start with your shoulders.\"","Selene nodded as she slowly walked up to the bed."]},{"number":241,"title":"Chapter 241 | Massaging Selene","paragraphs":["Dexter voice sounded even thicker and huskier than it should have been as he spoke.","\"Lay down.\"","Selene was dressed in a cardigan over her body and a thick skirt. As she lay down on her bed, Dexter’s heartbeat immediately increased. He closed his eyes and managed to calm himself, his face remaining expressionless as he approached her.","\"It’s a deep tissue massage,\" he explained. \"Which is why j would need to remove most of your clothing.\"","At that moment, Selene glanced at him, her pale white eyes narrowing as if she were about to attack him.","Dexter immediately raised his hands. \"Just like I said, it’s a deep tissue massage. The more clothing you wear, the less chance for the technique to work. Don’t worry. Although I’m not gay—I would never think of you girls that way.\"","Selene frowned, and Dexter felt the chill in the surrounding air increase drastically.","\"Are we that unappealing to you?\" she asked, her voice carrying a cold edge.","Dexter shook his head immediately. \"No, it is actually quite the opposite.\"","Selene blinked, looking at him.","Dexter continued. \"You girls are more appealing than anyone I have ever seen in my entire life. Apart from a single person. But I have a technique to suppress my thoughts and suppress myself. That’s why I said I would never think of you girls that way. This is purely professional.\"","He paused, letting his words settle.","\"And you want to increase the healing to your body, don’t you? To do that, I have to do this massage. If you don’t let me do that, although you will heal, the healing might be even lesser than before.\"","Selene couldn’t see, but her pale white eyes glanced at him for a few seconds. Then she slowly nodded.","\"Okay. I shall lie down on the bed.\"","Dexter smiled. \"I will start to remove your clothes.\"","Selene’s face flushed red, but she slowly nodded and muttered a tiny \"okay\" that even with Dexter’s enhanced hearing, he could barely hear.","He successfully removed her cardigan. Then he removed the shirt she was wearing underneath, leaving the bra she wore. His fingers slowly went downward as he removed her skirt.","\"I’m removing your skirt right now,\" he said.","Selene’s face flushed even redder, her entire body turning red. She didn’t say anything, but Dexter attributed it to her saying \"okay.\" So he went down and removed her skirt.","Dexter’s eyes widened as he saw her entire pale skin.","Her skin was even paler than anything he had ever seen in his entire life. He had never expected somebody’s skin to be so white. He had never seen anybody’s skin, or even thought anybody’s skin could be so white, so crispy, and so clean.","Her skin was fucking crispy, clean, white, and fresh. It was like she was a newborn baby. There was no freckle on her skin.","Mira’s skin was fresh and had a few freckles on it, giving it its beauty. Selene’s skin was different entirely, having no freckles, not a single thing, not a single blemish on it. It was fucking white like milk.","Dexter’s heartbeat increased rapidly, even when he tried to distract himself by using his cultivation, by chanting his cultivation chant. The sight of that skin made his heartbeat increase rapidly.","However, he still managed to calm himself as he spoke.","\"Turn around.\"","He spoke with a nonchalant tone, keeping his voice steady.","Selene looked at him for a while, then she turned her back on him, revealing her back.","As she turned her back on him, Dexter, who was using all his best to suppress the redness of his face because Selene was looking at him, suddenly blurted out.","The moment he blurted out, his entire face flushed red in an instant, as blood rushed through his entire face and skin. If Selene had been looking at him at this moment, she would have immediately known what he was thinking.","But she wasn’t looking. She was facing away, her silver hair cascading down her pale back, waiting.","Dexter took a deep breath, steadying himself. He reached for the oil, pouring a generous amount into his palms and warming it between his hands. The familiar scent of herbs filled the room, grounding him.","He placed his hands on her shoulders, and Selene flinched slightly at the contact. Her skin very cool to the touch, almost cold.","\"Relax,\" he said softly. \"This will feel strange at first, but it will help.\"","Dexter then began the technique, channeling his mana through his palms in slow, deliberate pulses. The shockwave glove on his hands hummed faintly, sending micro-vibrations through her muscles, breaking down tension and stimulating circulation.","Selene let out a small breath as he’d shoulders, which had been rigid, slowly began to loosen.","Dexter worked methodically, moving from her shoulders down her spine, then to her lower back. Each press, each pulse, each wave of warmth was measured and precise. He focused entirely on the technique—on the healing—pushing everything else from his mind.","Seconds passed, and then minutes passed in silence. The only sounds were the soft hum of the glove and the occasional whisper of breath.","At that moment, Dexter suddenly knew. If he didn’t do anything else to distract himself, he might actually be consumed by lust. Might actually lose control entirely.","So he suddenly spoke.","\"Selene, I want to ask you a question.\"","Selene was silent for a while before she spoke. \"Okay.\"","Dexter continued, distracting himself from the feeling. \"Is this house okay to you, or should I get a different one separate from this place?\"","Selene remained silent for a while before she spoke.","\"Although this house is quite decent and the neighborhood is quite okay, our families know exactly where we are staying. The Calloway family, the Vance family, the Frost family, and the Ashford family all know exactly where we are staying. We are put at a disadvantage toward them, and we are at their mercy staying exactly here. While I know you have the deed to the house, it doesn’t matter to any of the top three families. They can do whatever they wish in this place. So while this particular neighborhood isn’t bad, it is quite practical to immediately change location, so we won’t be at the mercy of the top three families.\"","Dexter remained silent for a while as he thought. Selene’s thought was exactly his thought. That was what he had been thinking about when he wanted to get a new house."]},{"number":242,"title":"Chapter 242 | Selene Bloodline Awakening","paragraphs":["Dexter knew he was in trouble.","If he did not distract himself immediately, he was going to lose control. The warm, glowing skin under his hands was sending signals to his brain that his meditation techniques could barely filter out. If he did not engage his mind with something complex, something analytical, he would be consumed by the heat building in his chest.","He needed a distraction.","\"Selene,\" Dexter said suddenly, his voice a bit too loud in the quiet room. \"I want to ask you a question.\"","Selene was silent for a moment. The only sound was the soft hum of the Shockwave Glove against her skin. \"Okay.\"","Dexter kept his hands moving along her shoulders, forcing his brain to focus on strategy. \"Is this house okay for you? Or do you think we should get a different one? Somewhere else?\"","Selene did not answer right away. He felt her shift slightly under his hands, her head tilting as she considered the question.","\"Although this house is decent and the neighborhood is quiet, our families know exactly where we are staying. The Calloway family, the Vance family, the Frost family, and the Ashford family. They all know our exact location. We are at a disadvantage here. We are at their mercy.\"","She paused.","\"Even though you have the deed to the house, it does not matter to the top three families. They can do whatever they wish to this place. They can send whoever they want. It is practical that we change locations immediately, so we are not at their mercy.\"","Dexter remained silent.","Her thoughts mirrored his own exactly. That was the exact reason he had gone to Harvest Homes. But then he remembered what had happened there. He had been scammed out of one million credits because the Ashford family controlled the city. They had put a word out, and the agency had robbed him.","He realized then that he could not just buy a new house under his own name. The Ashford family controlled Stargate City. If he tried to purchase property anywhere, they would know. They would interfere. The only way to get a new house was to use someone else’s name. Someone unconnected to him. But even that was a gamble.","As he thought about this, his eyes drifted down. The smooth, milky white skin of Selene’s back entered his vision. The information traveled straight to his brain, wiping out his strategic thoughts completely. His body grew hot. The heat rushed up his neck and threatened to flush his face again.","He immediately fled from that train of thought. He needed another topic. Something complex. Something that would force his brain to work overtime and ignore the beautiful woman lying half-naked on his bed.","\"Did you dream?\" Dexter asked suddenly.","Selene turned her head slightly toward him. \"Did I dream about what?\"","\"Flying,\" Dexter said. He kept his hands moving down her spine. \"Do you dream about flying? Or something else?\"","Selene was quiet. \"No, not really. Why do you ask?\"","Dexter frowned.","Mira had dreamed about flying. She dreamed about wings ripping out of her back. He had assumed that the bloodline awakening would manifest as wings for all three girls. But Selene was saying she didn’t dream about flying.","That meant two things. Either Selene’s bloodline was not manifesting yet, or the bloodline she was awakening did not involve wings. Each of them might get a different bloodline.","Dexter shook his head. \"Nothing. Don’t worry about it.\"","\"But I dreamt about something else,\" Selene said suddenly.","Dexter’s interest peaked. The strategic part of his brain engaged again, fighting back the biological distractions. \"What did you dream about?\"","\"It isn’t about flying,\" Selene said. \"It’s about control. No, not control.\" She paused, searching for the right word. \"I dreamt that I could see.\"","Dexter’s hands stopped on her lower back. The hum of the glove continued, but his hands were frozen. \"You dreamt you could see?\"","\"Yes,\" Selene said. Her voice was soft, carrying a weight of wonder and sadness. \"The dream was very vivid. I dreamt I could see almost everybody in the world. Even those hidden in different dimensions. Even those hidden across the entire earth. I felt like a god staring down at everybody.\"","Dexter stared at the back of her head. His mind was racing. Seeing everyone. Hidden dimensions. God-like perception.","\"Of course, even if the dream was realistic, I know it was just a dream,\" Selene added quietly.","Dexter did not respond.","His mind was no longer on the massage. It was no longer on her skin. It was on her face. He was looking at her face, or rather, the side of her face as she lay turned away from him. And suddenly, he noticed something he had noticed before but had dismissed.","Three distinct marks on her face.","They were very faded. So faded that he had thought it was an illusion the first time he saw them. But now, with the morning light hitting her face at the right angle, he could see them clearly.","One mark was on her forehead. Right in the center. Perfectly horizontal.","Another mark was underneath her left eye. A thin, curved line.","And the third mark was underneath her right eye. Identical to the left.","Three marks. Like closed eyes.","His brain connected the marks to her dream. Mira’s marks were on her shoulder blades. They were ten inches long and looked like scars from wings trying to rip through. They matched her dream of flying like a phoenix.","Selene’s marks were on her face. On her forehead and under her eyes. They matched her dream of seeing like a god.","The bloodline was manifesting differently for each of them.","Mira was getting wings. A Phoenix bloodline.","Selene was getting eyes. A Clairvoyance bloodline. Or something similar. A bloodline of sight.","The irony was not lost on Dexter. Selene was blind. She had been blind for three years. And the bloodline she was awakening was giving her marks around her eyes. A bloodline of vision for a woman who could not see.","Selene was becoming something else.","Something with eyes.","What was Lyra becoming?","The thought brought him back to Aurelyx. The Shadow Queen.","If Mira was getting wings, and Selene was getting eyes, what was Lyra getting? And more importantly, what was Aurelyx getting?","The Avatar Fruit sat in his spatial storage. Waiting. The potential solution to a problem that was growing more complex by the day."]},{"number":243,"title":"Chapter 243 | Selene Massage","paragraphs":["There were hundreds of thousands of known bloodlines in the world. The Bloodline Codex, maintained by the Hero Association, catalogued over three hundred thousand of them across every grade and type — and the Codex was still incomplete. Some bloodlines existed outside its pages. Some had never been recorded at all. Some were so rare, so ancient, or so powerful that no one had encountered them in living memory, and therefore no one had thought to write them down.","Without the system, identifying a bloodline from its early manifestation marks alone was impossible.","What Dexter could tell was that it was high-grade.","The higher the grade, the harder the manifestation. The longer the body took to integrate it. The more the body had to adapt before the bloodline could fully emerge.","That was why the girls hadn’t awakened yet. It seeded the bloodline into the body’s DNA, and then the body had to merge with it. Restructure itself at a cellular level to accommodate a new genetic framework.","With the system, the process would have been instantaneous. When the system had given Dexter his Flame Demon Bloodline, the integration had taken seconds.","But the girls didn’t have the system.","So the bloodline would only integrate with time.","And judging by the marks on Selene’s face and Mira’s back, that pace was accelerating.","The massage continued.","His hands moved down Selene’s spine. The Shockwave Glove hummed. The oil glistened. The 108 Body Massage Sutra guided his fingers through the precise, prescribed patterns that stimulated nerve regeneration and accelerated healing.","He noticed her skin again.","Every inch of Selene was silky and milky white and was cool to the touch. Not cold the way poor circulation is cold.","Dexter suddenly had an idea.","He activated his Heavenly Flame.","A thread — the thinnest, most precisely calibrated thread of heat his evolved bloodline could produce.","He channeled it through his hands, Into her skin.","The heat didn’t stay on the surface. He pushed it deeper. Past the skin, past the muscle, into the bone. The kind of penetrating, reach-the-source application of thermal energy that targeted the Internal Winter Ice at its root.","The effect was immediate.","Selene moaned in relief and pleasure.","That cold was being touched by heat for the first time.","And Selene’s body answered.","The sound hit Dexter like a freight train.","His hands froze and arousal spiked instantly.","Dexter took a deep breath and chanted his cultivation mantra in his head.","But wasn’t working.","His brain was willing. His body was not and his trousers immediately became tight.","Dexter’s face flushed red.","Luckily, Selene was turned away.","Face down on the bed. Back to him. Silver hair spread across the pillow. She couldn’t see him, and her Echolocation had been muted by the deep, relaxed state the massage had induced as she was drifting in the space between consciousness and sleep si She hadn’t noticed.","Dexter exhaled slowly and kept massaging.","None of it worked.","Because his hands were still on Selene’s body. And Selene’s body was still responding. And every response — every micro-movement, every shift in breathing, every subtle change in muscle tension beneath his fingers — was being processed by his Enhanced Hearing and transmitted to his brain through a channel that bypassed every meditation technique he had.","He was losing.","Dexter’s eyes drifted. Without permission. From his hands to her back — to the smooth, unbroken, impossibly white expanse stretching from her shoulders to her lower back.","Her back was beautiful.","The anatomical, structural beauty of a spine’s curve, a shoulder blade’s angle, the taper of a waist — the quiet, graceful architecture nature had designed and three years of isolation had preserved.","And then Dexter noticed something else.","Something that made the situation considerably worse.","Selene was not flat.","Far from it","Her back was wider than he’d thought. The shoulder-to-waist ratio that accommodated her chest was more substantial than her thick cardigans had suggested.","Dexter’s dragon, which had been standing at attention since the moan, reached a state of structural rigidity that was, from a purely engineering perspective, impressive.","He did not look down and kept massaging trying his best to hold himself.","Twenty minutes later","He removed the glove. Set it on the nightstand. Drew the blanket over Selene’s body, covering her from shoulders to feet.","She was asleep.","The deep tissue massage, combined with the heavenly Flame and the Grade-4 oil and the Shockwave Glove had produced a cumulative effect that overwhelmed her remaining defenses and sent her under so completely that she hadn’t even noticed when he massaged her face.","She had slept through it.","Dexter was a bit stunned, not by her sleep though.","But the depth of it surprised him. She had always been hyper-vigilant but now, she fell asleep.","And Dexter understood why.","The Internal Winter Ice didn’t just cause pain. Pain was the obvious symptom — the visible, measurable, diagnosable component. But beneath the pain was something else. Something that never showed up on examinations or scans.","Irritation.","The constant, never-ending, low-grade, impossible-to-ignore discomfort of frost energy seeping through your meridians and nerve endings and bone marrow every second of every day.","It made sleep almost impossible.","But with Dexter Flame, things changed.","As she slept, Dexter looked at her for a while, then he turned and left the room, closing the door quietly behind him.","As he stepped into the hallway, he suddenly saw Lyra.","She was eating the pastries he had given her. Her mouth was open as she fed herself, cheeks puffed out like a chipmunk storing nuts for winter. It seemed she had been about to enter the room when Dexter came out and closed the door behind him.","She stared at Dexter. Then at the door. Then back at Dexter. Her eyes blinked rapidly, processing the situation with the innocent curiosity of someone who had just witnessed something she didn’t quite understand.","Dexter immediately knew what she was thinking.","Before she could think even further, he spoke.","\"It’s not like that. I just went there to give her a massage. I just finished giving Selene a massage, and she has fallen asleep already.\"","Lyra slowly nodded her head. \"Oh,\" she said in understanding. Her mental voice was soft, accepting, but there was a hint of something else there. Curiosity, perhaps. Or maybe just the simple relief of knowing that nothing inappropriate had happened.","Then her eyes suddenly lit up.","She spoke in his mind—because she was mute, but with her talent she could speak directly into his thoughts. Her voice echoed in his head like a gentle chime.","\"Oh, what about me? Me too, me too, me too!\" she said excitedly, bouncing slightly on her heels.","Dexter smiled at her cuteness. The enthusiasm radiating from her was infectious, a bright spot in the otherwise heavy atmosphere of the house.","\"All right, when you are done eating, I will also give you your own massage.\"","Lyra’s eyes lit up. She smiled excitedly and nodded her head. In that split second, she immediately put all the remaining pastries into her mouth and finished the entire plate in a single bite.","Dexter was stunned.","Under his stunned gaze, she dusted her hands together and said, \"I’m done.\"","Dexter chuckled slightly. The sound was warm, genuine. It had been a long time since he had laughed like that. \"All right.\"","He was about to tell her to head to her room so he could massage her. But then he remembered—Selene was sleeping in their room. If he started massaging Lyra there, Selene might wake up, and they might disturb her. Selene needed her rest. The Eternal Ice was a cruel mistress, and any peaceful sleep she could get was precious.","So he told Lyra, \"Since Selene is sleeping in the room, would you come to my room and let me start the massage on you?\"","Lyra was immediately stunned. She stared at him.","The words suddenly echoed in her ear. She realized what Dexter meant. She was actually going to Dexter’s room. His private space. The room where he slept. The room that smelled like him.","Her face flushed slightly, a warm pink spreading across her pale cheeks. But she still turned and headed toward Dexter’s room.","Dexter was holding the massage oil and the necessary items he had used for Selene. Now he was going to do the same for Lyra.","Lyra headed to his room. She started to look around, her eyes taking in every detail. The simple bed. The wooden desk. The window that looked out into the backyard. The walls that were bare except for a single painting—a landscape of mountains and mist.","As she looked around, Dexter suddenly said, \"You’ve never been here, have you?\"","Lyra nodded her head. Her voice echoed in his mind. \"No. This is the first time I’m seeing your room. It is quite nice. It is quite nice and spacious.\"","Dexter blinked his eyes and spoke. \"Yeah, it is quite spacious. I would have let one of you girls come share the room with me, but it would be quite inappropriate, and I don’t think any of you would accept.\""]},{"number":244,"title":"Chapter 244 | Lyra’s Massage","paragraphs":["\"You’ve never been here, have you?\" Dexter asked.","Lyra shook her head. Her telepathic voice echoed in his mind.","\"No. This is the first time I’m seeing your room. It is quite nice. Spacious.\"","Dexter blinked. \"Yeah. It is quite spacious. I would have let one of you girls come share the room with me, but it would be inappropriate. And I don’t think any of you would accept.\"","Lyra shrugged. The gesture was casual. Easy.","\"It’s all right. The three of us are quite comfortable sleeping in one room.\"","Dexter nodded as he began preparing the bed. Spreading the blanket. Adjusting the pillow.","\"Even though I feel like you girls need your own personal rooms,\" he said.","Lyra continued looking around. Her fingers touched the edge of his nightstand. Traced the grain of the wood.","\"Yeah. We are women, so we definitely need privacy. However, since the three of us are cultivating the same technique, there is no secret between us. So there is not much need for privacy between ourselves.\"","She paused.","\"But getting a new house would be much better.\"","Dexter nodded. He agreed completely but he would have been moving if not for the incident with the Harvest Home.","The bed was ready. Pillow positioned, oil, glove, towel, all in place.","He looked at Lyra.","\"Remove your outer clothing,\" he said. \"The massage works best on bare skin.\"","Lyra was caught off haired by Dexter’s bluntness and she was immediately shy.","Dexter opened his mouth to explain about deep tissue massage and mana transfer and pressure points and the importance of direct skin contact for optimal technique performance.","L","Before the first word of the explanation left his mouth, Lyra reached for the hem of her gown and pulled it off in one swift motion and then dropped it beside the bed without ceremony, revealing a dark bra and dark panties.","Dexter’s breath caught and he was stunned.","Lyra’s chest was massive that even her bra was struggling to fully hold them.","Selene’s chest wasn’t as massive but her back compensated for it. Mira hed both front and back. While not that large, it was a handful while Lyra had a massive front!","He immediately inhaled and calmed himself.","\"Come,\" he said. His voice was steady. \"Lie down on the bed.\"","Lyra blinked at him innocently and obviously as she nodded and walked to the bed. Lay down. Face down.","On the blanket. Her dark hair spread across the pillow. Her hands rested at her sides.","Dexter looked at her.","Even face down, Lyra’s chest was visible, spreading to the sides, visible from above as a curve of flesh that extended beyond the width of her ribcage.","Dexter inhaled deeply and fit his own peace of mind, he cut off the circulation to his lower body!","He started with her legs.","He placed his oiled hands on her right foot and began.","Her feet were clean. Incredibly clean. The particular, soft, smooth, well-maintained quality of skin that had been cared for despite three years of hardship.","Then Lyra spoke.","\"Your bed smells nice and masculine.\"","The words arrived in his mind through the telepathic connection.","Dexter’s hands paused on her calf.","\"Thank you,\" he said.","Then Lyra spoke again.","\"Do you use perfume? Or is this your natural musky scent?\"","Dexter blinked.","\"No,\" he said. \"I don’t use perfume.\"","Lyra raised her head. Turned it slightly to look back at him.","\"That is really surprising,\" she said. Her telepathic voice carried genuine wonder. \"Because your bed smells really good. I can’t quite place the smell. It is very exotic. And attractive.\"","The last word landed in Dexter’s mind with the particular, weighted, loaded quality of a term that was being used in a specific, biological, pheromone-related context.","Dexter knew what she was talking about.","His bloodline.","The Ancient Flame Demon Bloodline, evolved to its Ancient Grade, had been changing his body in ways that went beyond cultivation and combat ability.","His skin produced pheromones.","The particular, concentrated, enhanced, bloodline-amplified pheromones that an Demon Bloodline generated as a passive byproduct of its evolutionary advancement.","The pheromones were designed by the bloodline’s biological framework to attract.","The effect was not something Dexter could control.","Everyone who entered his room would smell it.","The particular, exotic, musky, impossible-to-identify but impossible-to-ignore scent that was not perfume and not cologne and not any commercially produced fragrance but was instead the chemical signature of his bloodline.","To women, the effect was particularly pronounced. The pheromones were designed to be attractive to females.","Not consciously. Not in a way that could be identified or resisted through awareness. The attraction operated at the level of instinct. At the level of biology. At the level where the body responded to chemical signals before the brain could evaluate them.","Lyra was responding.","Her body, pressed against his bed, surrounded by his scent, was processing the pheromones through her olfactory system.","The chemical signals were traveling through her nasal passages to her limbic system, where they were triggering responses that she was interpreting as \"exotic\" and \"attractive\" without understanding the biological mechanism behind the interpretation.","She didn’t know it was pheromones.","She just knew his bed smelled good.","Dexter knew it was pheromones.","And he knew that the pheromones, combined with the massage, combined with the physical intimacy of the situation, combined with the fact that Lyra was already predisposed to find him attractive, were creating a particular, volatile, potentially combustible combination of biological and emotional factors that he needed to manage very carefully.","\"It’s just my natural scent,\" Dexter said. \"Nothing special.\"","Lyra turned her head back into the pillow and then pressed her nose into it and inhaled deeply.","If was as though she didn’t mind he was inhaling his scent and just did it.","\"It’s very nice,\" she murmured into the pillow. Her telepathic voice was drowsy and really relaxed. \"Very masculine and also very warm. Are you sure you aren’t using any perfume?\"","She asked suspiciously.","Dexter chuckled ass he continued his massage. \"There’s no reason I’d lie to you Lyra.\""]},{"number":245,"title":"Chapter 245 | Have You Kissed Anyone Before?","paragraphs":["So because of his demonic bloodline, it made his pheromones even more attractive to females.","That was the reason why Lyra felt like his natural smell was like perfume. Even when Dexter said it wasn’t perfume—that it was just his natural scent—he could still hear Lyra unconsciously inhaling the smell of his room. Inhaling the smell of his bed.","Dexter blinked his eyes but didn’t say anything as he continued to massage Lyra’s feet.","Her feet were particularly very clean, smooth, and nice. As he massaged her feet, then all the way to her legs, then her thighs, the vibration touched every part of her, every inch of her muscle as he used his mana to activate the healing part of the massage technique.","Suddenly, as Dexter was massaging her body, Lyra blurted out.","\"You know,\" she said in his mind, \"I’ve never felt anything like this before.\"","Dexter continued massaging all the way to Lyra’s upper thigh, reaching underneath her. He noticed that Lyra was packed—although it wasn’t as big as Selin’s back, Lyra’s back was still a handful. If you were to say something, Selin had a big front, Lyra had a big front, Selin had a big back. It was as if they were each compensating for the other. It was quite funny. And Mira was the perfect combination of the two of them, although her front and her back weren’t as big as Lyra’s front and Selin’s back. It was quite a handful also, and was above average.","Dexter continued to massage Lyra’s leg.","Then suddenly Lyra spoke. \"I am feeling something.\"","Dexter was stunned. \"What was that?\"","Lyra frowned. Lyra, who was lying there on her front, suddenly spoke to Dexter’s mind. \"I have no idea what it is, but I really like it. Continue.\"","Dexter was quite a bit stunned because he was directly massaging Lyra’s upper thigh. With the vibration of the shockwave glove, the vibration was definitely going through her pelvis area. For her to say she was feeling something—","Dexter at first thought she was feeling pain. \"Is it painful?\"","Lyra remained silent for a while before she said, \"No. No, it’s not painful. It’s actually quite the opposite.\"","Dexter was stunned.","Quite the opposite? Which meant—","He thought for a bit, then his eyes widened slightly as he knew what she was talking about.","Lyra continued, \"It is quite enjoyable. I like it. It’s quite enjoyable.\"","Dexter paused for a bit. He quickly knew what she was talking about.","Without hesitation, he went upwards. He continued massaging her pelvis area, but then he switched upwards to her upper back as he continued massaging her upper back.","If he continued to massage her pelvis, if he continued to massage her upper thighs and her pelvis area, it would count as taking advantage of her. He didn’t want to take advantage of her. If he wanted to do something with her, he would want it to be genuine. He didn’t want to take advantage of Lyra at all.","So he stopped massaging her upper thigh and went to her waist, massaging her waist.","As he did this, Lyra suddenly let out a slight groan of dissatisfaction.","Dexter shook his head at her naivety.","But he didn’t know if Lyra was truly naive or if she actually knew what he was doing. But Dexter didn’t want to get into it. He massaged her upper body. He massaged her upper back all the way to her arm.","Then he told her, \"I will turn you over now.\"","He carried her, then turned her over.","Lyra’s entire face was flushed red, and her eyes were a bit glassy as she looked at him.","Dexter was quite a bit startled as he said, \"Is anything wrong?\"","Lyra shook her head softly as she spoke into his mind. \"No, there is nothing wrong. I just really like the massage a lot.\"","Dexter smiled at her and said, \"Okay, if you like the massage a lot, then how about I give you a massage every day?\"","Lyra’s eyes lit up as she looked at him, as if he had given her the best food in the entire world. She looked at him and said, \"Really?\"","Dexter nodded his head and said, \"Yeah, really. If you don’t mind. Because you will mostly be half naked during the massage.\"","Lyra shook her head. Her face flushed even redder. But then she shook her head as she spoke in his mind. \"No, I don’t mind.\"","Then she looked up at him with curiosity and asked, \"What if I am fully naked? Would the massage be even better?\"","Dexter almost choked on his spit as he coughed. He never expected such a question from Lyra.","At that moment, Lyra suddenly smirked and said, \"I’m just joking.\"","Dexter rolled his eyes as he spoke. \"You are becoming quite naughty, aren’t you?\"","Lyra chuckled as she closed her eyes and enjoyed Dexter’s massage.","As Dexter continued massaging her, Lyra suddenly spoke. \"Have you ever kissed anyone before?\"","Dexter was stunned by the question. \"Why do you ask?\"","Lyra opened her eyes as she said, \"I’ve seen a lot of people kissing, in real life and some in Movies too and they seem to really enjoy it. I just wonder what people see in it.\"","Dexter shrugged and said, \"If two people like each other and they kiss, then they would naturally enjoy the kissing.\"","Lyra blinked her eyes, then unconsciously placed her finger on her lips as she spoke in his mind. \"Hmm. I would really like to know how it feels.\"","Dexter blinked his eyes and then he looked at Lyra. He looked at her rosy lips and then swallowed.","\"Haven’t you ever kissed anyone?\" He asked curiously.","Lyra shook her head. \"No, not really.\"","Dexter was a bit surprised as he replied. \"Nit even when you were young?\"","Lyra shook her head again. \"No, I spent all my youth cultivating. I didn’t have much time to interact with anyone.\"","Dexter blinked his eyes and then spoke. \"What about your fiancée? I heard he’s your childhood sweetheart.\""]},{"number":246,"title":"Chapter 246 | Kissing Lyra","paragraphs":["\"Like I said, I’d really like to know how kissing feels,\" Lyra said, her finger still unconsciously stroking her lips.","Dexter looked at her. At the way her pale finger traced the soft curve of her mouth. At the innocent curiosity in her eyes. He shook his head to clear his mind of the thought.","\"If you see someone you like,\" he said, \"then you can try kissing them.\"","Lyra looked at him. She stayed silent for a while, but then her voice echoed in his mind.","\"What if the person? What if I’m not sure if the person I like likes me back?\"","Dexter was stunned. He gazed into Lyra’s eyes. She was looking directly at him. She was looking directly at him as she said this with all seriousness.","At first, he thought it was Arilex talking. He thought her second personality had surfaced. But he listened to her heartbeat—and he knew it was Lyra. From the heartbeat, it was Lyra who was speaking at this moment. It was truly Lyra.","He remained stunned for a while before he replied.","\"Even if you are not sure the person might like you back, you still have to take the risk. You still have to take that risk. Because remaining silent won’t achieve much.\"","Lyra looked at Dexter for a while, then nodded her head. \"You’re right. Remaining silent won’t achieve anything. Taking the risk would be much better.\"","She blinked her eyes and looked at him.","\"But I haven’t kissed anyone before. If I kiss the person I like, but I don’t know how to kiss, and if I kiss the person I like and the person doesn’t like it—she doesn’t like the way I kiss—it might be bad.\"","Dexter blinked his eyes. He tilted his head and pondered.","\"Not really. If the person truly likes you, regardless of whether you know how to kiss or not, they would like it as long as you kiss them.\"","Lyra blinked her eyes. \"I’m not really sure about that.\"","Dexter didn’t say anything. He remained silent.","Then suddenly Lyra spoke.","\"How about you teach me?\"","Dexter’s hands, which were massaging Lyra’s body, froze. His mind went blank.","Teach her? What does she mean, teach her?","They were talking about kissing, and she was saying he should teach her how to kiss. Isn’t that basically both of them kissing?","He immediately focused. He used his enhanced hearing talent again and heard Lyra’s heartbeat. It was a bit faster this time. But it was still Lyra’s signature heartbeat—just slightly faster.","Dexter stared at Lyra for a while before he said, \"How should I teach you how to kiss?\"","Lyra smiled innocently. She looked at him innocently.","\"Dummy. Of course you have to use your lips. I know you have a lot of experience in kissing. So of course you use your lips to teach me how to kiss.\"","Dexter was flabbergasted.","He had never expected such a situation to occur right at this exact moment. He didn’t know what to do. Of course he would like to kiss Lyra. But he didn’t want it to be like he was taking advantage of her.","So he asked, \"Are you sure?\"","Lyra nodded her head. \"Yes, I’m sure. I want you to teach me how to kiss.\"","Dexter inhaled and told her, \"All right. You have to relax your body first.\"","Lyra nodded her head. \"I am quite relaxed.\"","She leaned on the bed as she relaxed quite a bit. She relaxed very well on the bed.","She relaxed as she raised her eyes toward him, waiting patiently. Dexter looked at Lyra as his heartbeat increased slightly. His heartbeat increased slightly as he looked at her.","Then slowly his face edged toward her. Slowly his face edged toward her. Just when his face was ten inches away from her face, he spoke to Lyra.","\"Do you prefer—\"","Just when he was ten inches away from her face, Lyra suddenly spoke. \"Should I close my eyes, or should I open them?\"","Dexter paused. Dexter paused as he spoke. Dexter paused, then later he spoke.","\"It depends on what you are feeling during the kiss. Your eyes may remain open, and once you are kissing, your eyes may close naturally. I’m not really sure. It depends on you. I’m not really sure, but it depends on each person’s preference.\"","Lyra blinked her eyes as she nodded her head and said, \"Okay. Okay, let’s continue.\"","She gave him a small smile.","Dexter blinked and then he inhaled deeply as he exhaled slowly. As he held his breath, he inhaled deeply and held his breath as his face inched closer toward her. He edged closer and closer toward her—five inches, four inches, three inches, two inches—and then their lips met.","Dexter felt his spine jolt slightly as his lips met hers. Lyra’s lips were incredibly soft. Really, really nice. Her lips were incredibly soft and really, really nice.","As their lips met, Dexter’s eyes were still open. Lyra’s eyes immediately closed as their lips met. Dexter checked to see if she wasn’t uncomfortable, saying that she wasn’t uncomfortable. He parted his lips and then took her lower lip into his lips, squeezing her lower lip with both of his lips as he slightly suckled on it. It was really, really soft.","By the time he caught himself, he had kissed Lyra’s lips for about a full minute. At that time, it was even Lyra’s moan. Lyra’s unconscious soft moan that jolted him up.","Dexter’s eyes widened. He didn’t even realize his eyes had been closed throughout. His eyes widened as he looked down at Lyra and immediately removed his lips as he pulled back, a bit embarrassed and he cleared his throat.","Lyra’s eyes fluttered open. Her face was flushed, her breathing slightly uneven as she unconsciously licked her lips as she looked at him with an expression he couldn’t quite read.","\"That’s...\" she started, then paused. Her voice echoed in his mind like the sound of a thousand siren. \"That’s what kissing feels like?\"","Dexter blinked his eyes and nodded. \"That’s a simple kiss.\"","Lyra touched her lips again, the same unconscious gesture from before. \"It felt... nice. Warm. I liked it.\"","Dexter smiled slightly. \"Good.\"","Lyra looked at him, then spoke again. \"Can we do it again? I want to practice more.\"","Dexter blinked. His heartbeat, which had been relatively steady, suddenly quickened.","\"Lyra...\"","She looked at him innocently. \"What? You said you would teach me. I need more practice to learn properly.\"","Dexter stared at her for a long moment. Then he sighed. ’This girl is really naughty.’","A small smile tugged at his lips as he thought.","\"All right. One more time.\"","Lyra smiled brightly. She closed her eyes and tilted her head back, waiting.","Dexter looked at her. At her closed eyes. At her parted lips. At the gentle rise and fall of her chest beneath the dark fabric of her bra.","He leaned in again.","This time, the kiss was different. Slower. More deliberate. He pressed his lips to hers and held them there, letting the warmth build between them. Lyra made a small sound—a soft, contented hum that vibrated against his mouth.","He moved his lips gently, guiding her, teaching her without words. She followed his lead, her lips soft and pliant beneath his. When he pulled back slightly, she leaned forward, chasing the contact, and he had to suppress a smile.","\"Easy,\" he whispered.","She opened her eyes, looking up at him with that same innocent curiosity. \"Did I do something wrong?\"","\"No,\" he said. \"You’re doing fine. Just... let it happen naturally.\"","She nodded and closed her eyes again.","He kissed her a third time. This time, he let his hand move to her cheek, cupping it gently. Her skin was warm beneath his palm. She leaned into his touch, a small sigh escaping her lips.","The kiss deepened. Not much—just enough to let her feel something more than simple pressure. He tilted his head slightly, changing the angle, and she followed, her lips parting just a fraction.","When he finally pulled back, they were both breathing a little harder.","Lyra’s eyes remained closed for a moment. Then they opened, and she looked at him with a soft, dazed expression.","\"That was...\" She paused, searching for words. \"That was really nice.\"","Dexter nodded. \"Good.\"","She touched her lips again. \"I think I understand now. Why people like it so much.\"","Dexter smiled slightly. \"I’m glad.\"","Lyra looked at him for a long moment. Then she spoke again, her voice quiet in his mind.","\"Thank you, Dexter. For teaching me.\"","He nodded. \"You’re welcome.\"","She settled back onto the bed, her body relaxing into the sheets. Her eyes were still on him, soft and warm.","\"Can we do this again sometime?\" she asked. \"The massage, I mean. And... maybe the kissing too?\"","Dexter blinked. His heartbeat, which had finally begun to settle, quickened again.","\"We’ll see,\" he said.","Lyra smiled happily as she replied.","\"Okay, i will hold you to that.\"","Dexter shook his head, a small chuckle escaping him. He continued the massage after that, working on her shoulders, her arms, her back. But the atmosphere in the room had shifted."]},{"number":247,"title":"Chapter 247 | Repairing The House","paragraphs":["By the time Dexter finished massaging Lyra, she had already fallen deeply asleep.","Dexter only noticed when he stopped working on her shoulders and received no response from her.","\"Lyra?\"","Nothing.","Her breathing had become slow and steady, and her face looked completely relaxed against his pillow.","Dexter stared at her for a moment.","\"She actually fell asleep...\"","A small smile appeared on his face as he picked up the towel beside the bowl of warm water. He carefully wiped away the remaining massage oil from her skin so she wouldn’t wake up feeling sticky or uncomfortable.","Once he was satisfied, he pulled the blanket over her but Dexter remained standing beside the bed.","His eyes wandered toward Lyra’s face before eventually settling on her lips. They were slightly parted, soft and pink, still faintly glistening from where she had licked them earlier.","For a brief moment, the memory of their earlier kiss returned. The warmth of her lips against his.","And along with it came the urge to kiss her again.","Dexter immediately pushed the thought aside.","Lyra was asleep.","Yes, she had given him permission earlier, but that had been different. She had been awake, curious and probably wanted to understand what kissing felt like.","That didn’t mean he could simply kiss her whenever he wanted.","Especially while she was sleeping.","That would be taking advantage of her. And despite everything, Dexter still had his principles. He had promised himself he would protect these girls, not exploit them.","Dexter shook his head.","\"Forget it.\"","He turned toward the door.","Before leaving, however, he glanced back one final time.","Then Dexter quietly closed the door behind him.","The house had become unusually peaceful.","Selene was already sleeping in the girls’ shared room, while Lyra had taken over Dexter’s bedroom. The two of them were resting.","That left only one of his three wives awake.","Mira.","Dexter headed toward the living room.","Just as he expected, Mira was there.","She sat in her wheelchair opposite the window, occupying the same position where she usually cultivated. The sun streaming through the glass cast her in its orange glow that made her hair look like it was on fire.","Her eyes were closed, her breathing calm, and there was almost no movement from her body.","For a second, Dexter wondered if she had fallen asleep while cultivating.","But the moment he stepped farther into the room, Mira’s head tilted slightly toward him.","She had sensed his presence but her eyes never opened. After acknowledging him, she simply turned her head forward again and resumed her cultivation.","Dexter didn’t disturb her.","He quietly entered the living room and sat down on the couch.","For several moments, silence filled the house.","Then Dexter’s attention shifted toward the wall.","His expression immediately changed.","Two ugly holes remained there.","They were souvenirs from his earlier confrontation with Kreg and his thugs. When Dexter had punched Kreg and one of his men, both of them had been sent smashing through the wall. He had already swept away the broken pieces and debris afterward, but cleaning the floor hadn’t exactly solved the bigger problem.","Two enormous holes were still glaring at him.","Dexter stared at them.","The longer he looked, the uglier they seemed to become.","He sighed.","\"I really did a number on this place.\"","His gaze briefly moved toward Mira.","She didn’t react.","Dexter looked back at the wall.","He couldn’t exactly leave the house like this. The girls deserved to live somewhere that didn’t remind them of violence every time they walked into the room. They had already endured enough.","Fortunately, when he had bought materials for renovating the house, he had purchased more than they eventually needed. Some of the leftover supplies were still sitting inside the storage room.","That should be enough.","Dexter stood.","Since everyone else was sleeping or cultivating, there wasn’t much else for him to do anyway.","He might as well fix the damage he had caused.","He entered the storage room and began searching through the remaining renovation materials. Boxes of drywall patches, joint compound, sandpaper, paint—everything he needed was still there, tucked away in the corner.","It didn’t take long before he found what he needed.","Dexter carried everything into the living room and placed the materials near the damaged wall.","Then he got to work.","He wasn’t a professional builder, but this wasn’t his first time doing basic repair work either. He knew enough to understand what needed to be done. He measured the holes, cut the patches to size, and fitted them into place.","Piece by piece, the holes began disappearing.","The quiet living room soon filled with the soft sounds of Dexter working. The scrape of the putty knife. The rustle of sandpaper. The occasional creak of the floorboards as he shifted his weight.","Mira remained near the window throughout the entire process.","She didn’t speak.","Dexter didn’t bother her either.","It created a strangely peaceful atmosphere. One person cultivated. The other repaired a wall he had accidentally destroyed by punching people through it. A perfectly normal night in Dexter’s increasingly abnormal life.","Time slipped past.","Roughly an hour later, Dexter finally stepped backward and examined his work.","The two holes were gone.","He wiped the sweat from his forehead with his arm before looking over the repaired sections carefully. The patches were smooth, the edges blended, and he had even managed to match the paint reasonably well.","It wasn’t perfect.","Anyone experienced in construction would probably notice the difference immediately. But considering what the wall had looked like an hour ago?","Dexter nodded with satisfaction.","\"Good enough.\"","At least nobody could walk into the house and immediately ask why there were two human-sized holes in the living-room wall.","Dexter crouched and gathered the remaining materials. After returning everything useful to the storage room, he came back with a broom and cleaned the floor. By the time he finished, the living room looked considerably better and almost normal. What was left was the wall paper.","Dexter placed both hands on his waist and inspected his work.","\"Nice.\""]},{"number":248,"title":"Chapter 248 | You’re Blushing","paragraphs":["\"You’re quite good at this.\"","Dexter paused.","He had just finished inspecting the repaired section of the wall when Mira’s voice suddenly came from behind him.","Turning around, he saw that Mira had finally opened her eyes. She had turned her wheelchair slightly and was now studying the wall he had repaired. Her gaze moved across the smooth surface and there was a faint look of admiration in her eyes.","Dexter smiled. \"Yeah. I’ve gotten a bit of practice over the years.\"","Mira looked from the wall to him.","\"Practice?\"","Dexter shrugged causally as he brushed some dust from his hands. \"I was a servant at the Ashford Estate all my life. You learn to do a little bit of everything when you’re the person everyone calls whenever something needs fixing.\"","Mira slowly nodded.","For several seconds, she said nothing as her expression became thoughtful. Her eyes narrowed slightly as she studied hum.","\"If you hadn’t mentioned it, I would’ve forgotten you were a servant with the Ashford family.\"","Dexter blinked before chuckling. \"Why do you say that?\"","\"Isn’t it obvious?\"","Mira turned her wheelchair completely toward him.","\"The raw materials you somehow get your hands on. The techniques you possess. Those ridiculously high-grade meals you cook...\"","She paused.","\"Any one of those things would make you unusual. But all of them together?\"","Her eyes narrowed slightly.","\"We have established the fact thag you’re not ordinary.\"","Dexter remained silent.","Mira continued calmly. \"And yet I’m supposed to believe that someone like you spent years living as a servant in the Ashford family despite being their firstborn?\"","She tilted her head slightly, her dark eyes never leaving his face.","\"Was being a servant only a cover?\"","For once, Dexter didn’t immediately answer.","He looked at Mira for a but then the corner of Dexter’s mouth curled upward to an imperceptible smile.","\"Does it really matter whether it was a cover or not?\"","Mira stared at him.","Then she shrugged dismissively.","\"You’re right.\"","\"It doesn’t really matter.\"","She turned slightly toward the window, gazing outside.","\"Besides, you wouldn’t tell me anyway.\"","Dexter’s smile faded a little.","He walked closer, the floorboards creaking softly beneath his feet. His presence seemed to fill the space around her, and yet he was careful not to crowd her.","\"It’s not that I don’t want to tell you.\"","Mira glanced at him.","Dexter looked toward the window as he sighed.","\"That part of my life is already the past.\"","\"I’ve spent enough time thinking about what happened before. I’m trying to focus on what comes next.\"","Mira remained silent.","Then Dexter looked directly at her. His eyes met hers with an intensity that made her pause.","\"And you three are my future.\"","Mira froze.","For several seconds, she simply stared at him.","She clearly hadn’t expected that answer.","A faint redness slowly appeared on her cheeks. It was subtle—just a hint of pink against her pale skin.","Mira immediately looked away.","\"Okay, whatever.\"","Dexter stared at her.","Then his lips slowly curved into a grin.","\"Are you blushing?\"","Mira’s head snapped toward him. Her eyes flashed with something dangerous as she glared.","\"Me?\"","Dexter’s grin widened.","\"Yes, you.\"","\"Blush?\"","Mira scoffed as though he had just accused her of committing some terrible crime. The sound was sharp, dismissive, and entirely unconvincing.","\"Nothing could ever make me blush.\"","\"Really?\"","\"Really.\"","Dexter took a step toward her.","Mira’s eyes immediately narrowed.","Dexter took another step.","She watched him suspiciously.","\"What are you trying to do?\"","Dexter stopped beside her wheelchair. He wore such an innocent expression that it immediately made Mira even more suspicious. The corners of his eyes crinkled slightly.","\"Nothing.\"","\"Dexter.\"","\"Nothing much.\"","He leaned slightly closer. His voice dropped to a murmur.","\"Just trying to seduce you.\"","Mira stared at him.","Then she sneered.","\"Seduce me?\"","A short laugh escaped her. It was sharp and full of disbelief.","\"Ha! Have you already forgotten what I told you? You won’t succeed.\"","Dexter placed one hand against his chest as though her words had wounded him. He let out a dramatic sigh.","\"Never say never.\"","\"I just did.\"","\"That doesn’t make it true.\"","\"It does when I’m the one saying it.\"","Dexter chuckled.","Mira placed her hand underneath her jaw.","There was confidence written all over her face now as she stared at him like a winner.","Dexter noticed it.","And somehow, that only made him want to tease her more.","He stepped around the wheelchair until he stood directly in front of her. Mira followed him with her eyes, refusing to be the first to look away.","\"Moreover,\" Dexter said, \"we still have a month, right?\"","The confidence on Mira’s face flickered for a second.","But Dexter caught it and his smile widened.","Mira immediately recovered.","\"So?\"","\"So...\" Dexter crouched slightly until their eyes were closer to the same level. \"That means I still have plenty of time.\"","\"To embarrass yourself?\"","\"To make you fall for me.\"","Mira almost laughed.","\"Your confidence is impressive.\"","\"Thank you.\"","\"That wasn’t a compliment.\"","\"I’ve decided to accept it as one.\"","Mira rolled her eyes.","\"You’re hopeless.\"","\"And yet you’re doing it again.\"","Her hand immediately rose toward her cheeks.","The instant she realized what she had done, Mira froze.","Dexter’s grin became unbearable. It spread across his face like sunlight, warm and infuriating.","Mira slowly lowered her hand.","\"You tricked me.\"","\"I didn’t say you were actually blushing.\"","Mira’s eyes sharpened as she gritted her teeth and glared at him.","\"Dexter!\"","He burst out laughing.","Mira’s expression darkened, but there was a giant smile.","\"You have three seconds to get away from me.\"","\"Or what?\"","\"Three.\"","Dexter straightened.","\"I’m curious now.\"","\"Two.\"","\"What’s going to happen at zero?\"","Mira’s cultivation energy suddenly stirred around her. The air grew hottter, and a faint pressure began to press against the edges of the room.","Dexter’s smile disappeared.","\"One.\"","\"Goodbye, Mira.\"","He immediately turned around.","\"Ha!\" Mira laughed victiriously.","Dexter immediately stopped in hus teacks and he slowly looked over his shoulder.","Mira had the faintest victorious smile on her face. It was small, almost imperceptible, but it was there.","That did it.","Dexter turned back toward her.","Mira’s smile vanished.","\"What?\"","\"You know,\" Dexter said, walking toward her again, \"for someone who claims she can’t be seduced, you seem awfully interested in whether I’m giving up.\"","\"I couldn’t care less.\"","\"Then why are you smiling?\"","\"I wasn’t.\"","\"You were.\"","\"You’re imagining things.\""]},{"number":249,"title":"Chapter 249 | Preparations","paragraphs":["\"Then why are you smiling?\"","\"I wasn’t.\"","\"You were.\"","\"You’re imagining things.\"","Dexter stopped beside her again. His presence was warm, familiar, and entirely too close.","For a few seconds, neither spoke. The playful atmosphere slowly settled into something quieter. Something more real.","Mira looked toward the repaired wall.","Then toward Dexter.","\"Dexter.\"","\"Hmm?\"","The teasing light in her eyes faded and her expression became more serious.","\"Do you really mean that?\"","\"Mean what?\"","\"What you said earlier.\"","Dexter knew exactly what she meant.","Still, he waited.","Mira hesitated like she didn’t want to ask but still, she continued.","\"That we’re your future.\"","The teasing disappeared from Dexter’s face.","He looked at her properly.","\"Yes.\"","Mira’s eyes narrowed as she stared deeply into his eyes and she immediately saw that he wasn’t joking and extremely serious too.","Mira’s eyes remained on him for a moment before she looked away.","\"Idiot.\"","Dexter smiled.","\"That sounded suspiciously affectionate.\"","\"It wasn’t.\"","\"Of course.\"","\"And stop smiling.\"","\"I’m not smiling.\"","\"You clearly are.\"","Dexter’s smile only widened.","Mira sighed and turned her wheelchair back toward the window.","\"You’re irritating.\"","\"And I still have a month.\"","Mira closed her eyes again.","\"You’ll need more than a month.\"","Dexter raised an eyebrow.","That wasn’t the same as saying he would never succeed.","Interesting, very interesting, Dexter decided not to point that out, Dexter turned toward the repaired wall, then looked at Mira one final time.","Later that night, he was just done washing the plates when a knock came from the front gate.","Dexter’s eyes shifted toward the sound. He didn’t immediately move. Instead, he focused his enhanced hearing, letting the sounds of the night sharpen around him. The faint rustling of leaves. Distant voices from neighboring houses. The soft hum of insects in the cool air.","And finally, the steady heartbeat of the person standing outside his gate.","Dexter recognized it immediately.","\"Tessa.\"","He got up and headed outside, his footsteps quiet against the floorboards. The house was still, everyone else asleep or cultivating. He opened the front door and walked to the gate, the night air cool against his skin.","When Dexter opened the gate, Tessa was standing there waiting for him. The moonlight caught her features, highlighting the smile that always seemed to hover at the corners of her lips.","\"There you are.\"","\"As if you haven’t been knocking for less than a minute,\" Dexter replied.","Tessa ignored that. As usual, she had come to settle the money from the meals Dexter had prepared and supplied to her father’s bakery. After accounting for her own agreed cut, she transferred Dexter’s share of the day’s earnings.","Dexter checked the transaction and nodded. Everything was correct.","Normally, they would also discuss how many meals he needed to prepare for the next day. Tonight, however, there was no need. Tomorrow was the neighborhood festival, and most businesses in the area would be closed, including Tessa’s father’s bakery.","For once, Dexter didn’t have a mountain of meals waiting to be cooked before sunrise.","\"Alright, Tessa. Goodnight.\"","He was about to close the gate when Tessa suddenly stopped him.","\"Wait.\"","Dexter raised an eyebrow. \"What?\"","\"You’re preparing for tomorrow, right?\"","Dexter gave her a strange look. \"I already told you I’m coming.\"","\"I know that.\"","\"Then what preparations are you talking about?\"","Tessa blinked. Then realization appeared on her face. \"You seriously don’t know?\"","\"Know what?\"","\"About the food.\"","\"What food?\"","Tessa stared at him for several seconds. Then she sighed, the sound heavy with exaggerated patience. \"You really don’t know.\"","Dexter folded his arms. \"That’s why I’m asking.\"","Tessa stepped a little closer. The smell of bread and sugar clung to her clothes—the familiar scent of the bakery she worked at every day. \"Everyone calls it a festival, but it’s actually more like a huge neighborhood picnic.\"","Dexter nodded slowly. \"Okay...\"","\"Families come out, people sit together, talk, eat, and enjoy themselves. Most importantly, everyone brings food.\"","\"That makes sense.\"","\"I’m not finished.\"","Dexter gestured for her to continue.","\"We exchange meals.\"","Dexter raised an eyebrow. \"Exchange?\"","\"Yeah. It’s a tradition around here. You cook something, someone else cooks something, then everyone shares. You give people some of your food and they’ll give you some of theirs.\"","Dexter finally understood. \"So basically, I need to cook enough food to share.\"","\"Exactly!\"","Tessa smiled brightly. A small dimple appeared on her cheek, softening her features. It was a smile that made her look younger, more carefree.","\"And I’ll be expecting yours tomorrow.\"","Dexter narrowed his eyes playfully. \"Now I understand why you came all the way here to explain the tradition.\"","\"What?\"","\"You just want free food.\"","Tessa placed a hand against her chest, feigning offense. \"Free food? It’s a cultural exchange.\"","Dexter almost laughed. \"Of course.\"","\"A very important cultural exchange.\"","\"Right.\"","Tessa pointed at him. \"So make sure you save some for me. I want to taste more of your cooking.\"","Dexter smiled. \"If you’re late, it won’t be my fault if everything finishes.\"","Tessa’s mouth immediately fell open. Then she pouted. \"You’re trying to bully me.\"","\"I’m warning you.\"","\"That’s bullying.\"","Dexter chuckled and waved his hand. \"Goodnight, Tessa.\"","Tessa continued pouting for another second before eventually smiling. \"Goodnight, Dexter. See you tomorrow.\"","\"See you tomorrow.\"","She waved before turning away. Dexter watched her leave, her figure growing smaller as she walked down the quiet street. Then he closed and locked the gate.","He returned inside.","The house was quiet again. Everyone had already eaten. Selene and Lyra had woken up earlier in the evening, and Lyra had returned to the girls’ room after eating. Mira had eaten as well. By now, everyone had retired for the night.","Dexter entered his bedroom and sat on the edge of his bed.","Tomorrow.","He leaned backward slightly and thought about it. Tomorrow would be the first time in quite a while that he was taking all three girls outside simply to enjoy themselves.","No fighting. No cultivation emergency. No business. No thugs smashing through walls.","At least, Dexter hoped so.","He wasn’t entirely sure whether he should be nervous about taking all three of his wives to a neighborhood festival at once. Still...","Dexter smiled.","He was looking forward to it. The girls had spent far too much time inside the house recently. A change of scenery would be good for them.","Especially Mira."]},{"number":250,"title":"Chapter 250 | Preparations II","paragraphs":["Dexter’s expression became thoughtful. He would need to wake up early and prepare enough food for the picnic. Since the tradition involved exchanging meals, making only enough for himself and the girls wouldn’t work.","Fortunately, tomorrow was also one of the rare mornings when he didn’t have to prepare food for sale. Most businesses in the neighborhood would be closed for the festival. That included Tessa’s father’s bakery.","Technically, Dexter would lose a day’s income. But considering how much work he normally did every morning, having one day where he could cook without worrying about orders wasn’t exactly terrible.","\"A day off won’t kill me.\"","He could wake up early, prepare several dishes for the picnic, and still have enough time to get ready before they left.","Dexter began mentally arranging everything he would need. Ingredients. Containers. Utensils. He would need to make enough for four people, plus extra for sharing. Maybe some pastries, since Lyra seemed to enjoy them. Something warm and hearty for Mira. And perhaps something lighter for Selene, whose body still struggled with the Eternal Ice.","Then his bedroom door suddenly opened.","A cold current swept through the room.","Dexter didn’t even need to turn around.","\"Selene.\"","She stepped inside.","Something about her was different tonight. During her previous visits, Selene had always hesitated at the doorway. Sometimes she would stand there awkwardly, almost as though she needed to convince herself to enter. Her pale eyes would flicker around the room, her posture rigid with uncertainty.","Tonight, she simply walked in.","She only stopped briefly when her eyes met Dexter’s. He smiled. That seemed to remove whatever tiny amount of uncertainty remained.","Selene walked forward and sat on the bed opposite him without waiting for an invitation. She crossed her legs, her silver hair cascading over her shoulders like moonlight made solid.","\"Hi.\"","\"Hey.\"","Selene glanced around before looking at him again. \"I hope I’m not disturbing you.\"","\"Not at all.\"","\"You’re sure?\"","\"Completely.\"","Selene nodded. \"Okay.\"","She closed her eyes. Almost immediately, she entered a cultivation state. Her breathing slowed, her body stilled, and the cold energy within her began to stir.","Dexter watched her for a moment. Then he activated his Heavenly Flame talent.","No visible flames appeared. He deliberately kept the manifestation suppressed, allowing only the intense warmth produced by the Heavenly Flame to flow through his body. Heat gradually spread across the bed, radiating outward like invisible sunlight.","Selene’s tense expression relaxed almost immediately. The cold energy inside her was extremely troublesome, but Dexter had already discovered that his Heavenly Flame could suppress it. The closer she remained to him, the more effective that suppression became.","Less than a minute later, Dexter spoke. \"Selene.\"","Her eyes opened.","\"Come sit closer.\"","Selene blinked. Dexter tapped the empty space beside him. \"You’ll feel the heat better from here.\"","Selene looked at the space. Then at Dexter. For a brief second, the old hesitation returned. But it quickly disappeared.","\"Okay.\"","She shifted across the bed and sat directly beside him, resting her back against the headboard. A slight flush appeared on her cheeks—barely visible against her pale skin, but there nonetheless.","Dexter noticed it. He also noticed something else. She wasn’t nearly as uncomfortable around him anymore. The first few times she had entered his room, every movement had been filled with hesitation. Now she had walked in herself. Sat on his bed without being invited. And when Dexter asked her to move closer, she had done so without arguing.","Progress.","Dexter smiled faintly.","Selene noticed. \"What?\"","\"Nothing.\"","She stared suspiciously at him. \"You’re smiling.\"","\"Am I not allowed?\"","Selene looked away. \"I didn’t say that.\"","Dexter chuckled softly. \"Continue cultivating.\"","Selene closed her eyes again. Dexter did the same.","The Heavenly Flame stirred inside him. Warmth radiated outward. The cold energy within Selene instinctively reacted, but whenever it threatened to surge, Dexter’s heat pressed against it, suppressing the icy outbreak before it could spread.","Selene’s breathing gradually became calmer. Dexter focused on maintaining the balance. Heat and cold. Two completely opposing forces existed only inches apart. Yet instead of clashing violently, they gradually settled into an unusual harmony.","Minutes became hours. Neither of them spoke again. Eventually, the night disappeared.","---","Dexter’s eyes opened.","For a moment, he remained completely still. His internal clock had awakened him almost exactly when he wanted. He glanced toward his phone. Five minutes before the alarm.","Dexter reached over and switched it off before it could ring.","Then he tried to sit up.","Something stopped him.","Dexter looked down.","Selene was hugging him. Sometime during their cultivation, she had apparently moved closer until she was practically wrapped around him, instinctively seeking the warmth produced by his Heavenly Flame. Her arms were draped across his chest, her face pressed against his shoulder.","Her face was peaceful. More peaceful than he had ever seen it. The permanent tension around her eyes was gone. The slight frown that usually lingered on her lips had vanished.","Dexter stared at her for several seconds. Then he smiled.","\"So much for sitting closer.\"","He carefully loosened her arms from around him. Selene shifted slightly. Dexter froze. She didn’t wake. He waited another second before slowly slipping out of her embrace and getting off the bed.","Selene instinctively moved toward the warmth he had left behind, hugging part of the blanket instead. Dexter almost laughed.","He pulled the blanket over her properly, tucking the edges around her shoulders.","Then he quietly left the bedroom.","The house was still silent. Outside, dawn was only beginning to arrive. The sky was a pale grey, the first hints of orange just beginning to creep over the horizon.","Dexter stretched his arms.","Today was the festival. And apparently, thanks to Tessa’s warning, he had quite a bit of cooking ahead of him.","Dexter entered the kitchen, rolled up his sleeves, and looked over the ingredients he had available. Flour. Rice. Vegetables. Meat. Eggs. Spices. Everything he needed was there, organized and waiting.","A smile slowly appeared on his face.","\"If everyone is exchanging food...\"","He reached for the first ingredient.","\"...I might as well make something worth exchanging.\"","And with that, Dexter began preparing the meals for the picnic."]}]);
